WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
It was November 3rd

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:06.360
, 1991 and Blake Newsom loved his job.&nbsp;
He had a passion for organization,&nbsp;

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:11.520
an undying love of American political history,&nbsp;
and was a life-long member of the Republican&nbsp;

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:16.440
party. That’s why he took great pride in his&nbsp;
position as a filing clerk at the Ronald Reagan&nbsp;

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:23.340
Presidential Library. Or at least, he did,&nbsp;
until his horrifying encounter with SCP – 1981.&nbsp;

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:29.520
The worst day of Blake’s life began like any&nbsp;
other. He was taking inventory of the archive’s&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.300
wide array of Betamax tapes, and&nbsp;
making sure they were all arranged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.760
carefully and conformed
with the filing system.&nbsp;

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:42.360
One by one, he checked footage of speeches and&nbsp;
addresses off of his list, until he came upon a&nbsp;

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:47.640
strange tape that had no business being there.&nbsp;
The tape looked to be completely normal, but it&nbsp;

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:53.160
hadn’t been recorded on the archive inventory.&nbsp;
And there was something else off about it. A&nbsp;

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:56.640
single white sticker was on the front of&nbsp;
the tape with “RONALD REGAN CUT UP WHILE&nbsp;

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:01.740
TALKING" scrawled hastily with what was&nbsp;
probably a felt-tipped marker. Blake was shocked&nbsp;

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.680
and appalled – they hadn’t even&nbsp;
spelled the President’s name correctly!&nbsp;

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:10.500
What poor Mr. Newsom didn’t know was that he&nbsp;
was about to see something so disturbing that&nbsp;

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.100
he’d look back on that misspelling like&nbsp;
it was a treasured childhood memory.&nbsp;

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.380
Standard policy for tapes like this would be to&nbsp;
review and catalogue, or even throw it out if&nbsp;

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:23.940
necessary. Typically, a lowly filing clerk&nbsp;
like Blake would need to seek approval from his&nbsp;

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:29.160
superiors, but curiosity got the better of him.&nbsp;
He commandeered one of the library’s televisions&nbsp;

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:33.960
and Betamax cassette players, and started&nbsp;
watching the footage. For the first minute or so&nbsp;

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:39.240
nothing seemed out of the ordinary, just the&nbsp;
president standing at a podium giving his iconic&nbsp;

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:44.160
“Evil Empire” speech to the National Association&nbsp;
of Evangelicals at Sheraton Twin Towers&nbsp;

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.760
Hotel, Orlando, Florida, on March 8th, 1983.&nbsp;

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:53.940
However, the second the tape hit the one minute&nbsp;
and ten seconds mark, something unnatural&nbsp;

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:59.580
began to occur. President Reagan’s speech began&nbsp;
to veer off, as the topic of conversation shifted&nbsp;

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:05.820
from the importance of family values to the&nbsp;
exquisite taste of human flesh. Blake was taken&nbsp;

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:12.360
aback. Surely, he was hearing things? But the&nbsp;
tape only got worse. President Reagan began to&nbsp;

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.420
divulge the fact that he enjoyed&nbsp;
the taste of young flesh the best,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:20.760
particularly that of infants. As
Reagan began to go into detail about how exactly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:25.200
one should best cook an infant if you want to
seal in the flavour, the crowd erupted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.020
into modest applause.
Blake started to feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:31.920
sick. He’d remembered watching this&nbsp;
speech, and President Reagan had said&nbsp;

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:37.860
nothing of the sort! Things only got weirder as&nbsp;
the President’s cheek suddenly opened up into a&nbsp;

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:43.740
long, bleeding gash, as though someone had cut&nbsp;
into his face with an invisible knife. As the&nbsp;

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:49.200
speech continued, and Reagan’s words became more&nbsp;
nonsensical and incoherent, the injuries got&nbsp;

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:54.900
worse, too. His face developed puncture wounds,&nbsp;
like he was being stabbed. Skin in some areas&nbsp;

00:02:54.900 --> 00:03:00.240
rotted and peeled off. Reagan showed no awareness&nbsp;
of the horrifying injuries that seemed to be&nbsp;

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.960
occurring spontaneously on his&nbsp;
body. This was a living nightmare!

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:10.080
The tape came to a merciful end 22 minutes in,&nbsp;
after President Reagan’s throat appeared to be&nbsp;

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:16.320
slashed open and his insane speech was reduced to&nbsp;
quiet gurgles. It fizzled out into static shortly&nbsp;

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:22.140
after, and Blake politely retired to the&nbsp;
bathroom to throw up. Was this some sick prank or&nbsp;

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:27.900
tampering or camera trickery, perhaps? He&nbsp;
didn’t know but that tape was disgusting, and&nbsp;

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:33.120
whoever was responsible had to be punished.&nbsp;
Newsom contacted the police, hoping obscenity&nbsp;

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.260
charges could be pressed against the creator&nbsp;
of the tape once they were found. The tape was&nbsp;

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:41.640
taken into evidence, and a low-level police&nbsp;
investigation into the possible culprits began.&nbsp;

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:46.680
While the police officers who viewed the tape&nbsp;
reported nightmares in the weeks following, the&nbsp;

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:51.720
creator of the tape was never found. The&nbsp;
investigation truly came to an end when a superior&nbsp;

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:57.060
closed the case and the tape disappeared from&nbsp;
the evidence locker. This, as you probably could&nbsp;

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:02.040
have guessed, was the work of a field agent&nbsp;
from The SCP Foundation. Amnestics were then&nbsp;

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:06.540
used to erase the memories of everyone unlucky&nbsp;
enough to witness the tape, including Blake&nbsp;

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:10.440
Newsom, who could finally rest&nbsp;
easy and return to his filing work.&nbsp;

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:17.460
The anomalous tape was now in responsible hands.&nbsp;
It was given the designation SCP – 1981, and&nbsp;

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:22.740
given the object class “Safe” due to its easily&nbsp;
controlled and self-contained nature. Proper&nbsp;

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:26.880
research and testing was now able to begin and&nbsp;
while nothing about the construction of the tape&nbsp;

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:32.160
suggested anything inherently anomalous, repeat&nbsp;
viewings of the video made it clear that this&nbsp;

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.460
went far beyond mere doctored&nbsp;
footage of a Presidential speech.&nbsp;

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:40.980
Every single time the tape is played, both the&nbsp;
speech made and the injuries received by President&nbsp;

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:46.860
Reagan change. The few rules the tape seems to&nbsp;
always follow are that Reagan never reacts to&nbsp;

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:50.340
the injuries he’s receiving, it&nbsp;
always has the same beginning and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:54.360
total runtime, and the speech is
always corrupted. These speeches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.540
have been described as “mostly&nbsp;
incoherent, lacking any sort of&nbsp;

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:02.340
underlying thematic structure and largely&nbsp;
being composed of nonsensical anecdotes and&nbsp;

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:07.680
parables”, so not that dissimilar from a regular&nbsp;
Reagan speech, but the topics always turn&nbsp;

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:14.280
incredibly dark and have included torture,&nbsp;
mutilation, death, cannibalism, ritual sacrifice,&nbsp;

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:18.180
genocide, and more.
The range of injuries shown on President&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:23.520
Reagan in the videos have included, but are by no
means limited to, impalement, mutilation, flaying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:28.380
and some tortures so gruesome that the details
have been redacted from official files.&nbsp;

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:33.960
On several occasions, the details of President&nbsp;
Reagan’s speech have also eerily predicted the&nbsp;

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:37.680
future. These include successfully&nbsp;
predicting the September 11th

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:42.120
attacks in 2001 and the outcome
of the 2008 Russian presidential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:45.780
election. Incidentally, this&nbsp;
isn’t even the only Reagan-related&nbsp;

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:50.580
SCP to predict the future. No,&nbsp;
there’s another entry in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:56.700
incredibly specific niche: SCP – 095, a
highly degraded copy of a comic known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.700 --> 00:06:01.680
“The Atomic Adventures of Ronnie Ray-Gun.” The
title character bears a striking resemblance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:04.680
to President Reagan, despite&nbsp;
the fact that the comic is&nbsp;

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:08.460
confirmed by Foundation tests to&nbsp;
have been written in the early 1930s.&nbsp;

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:12.240
The comic is set in the far-off&nbsp;
future world of the 1980s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:15.240
and follows a number of Ronnie’s
exploits in three stories.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:19.860
The first, titled “Ronnie vs. Space&nbsp;
Admiral Carter”, seems to perfectly

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:22.620
describe the events of the&nbsp;
1980 presidential election.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:29.280
The second, “Space Assassin!”, mirrors the
attempted assassination of President Reagan by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:34.980
John Hinckley Jr. And the third, titled “Jungle
Planet!”, retells the Iran-Contra controversies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:40.980
of 1986. These comics were produced under the
mysterious and apparently non-existent company,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:45.540
“Future Funnies.” The Foundation hopes to
track down the other comics from this company&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:52.080
whenever possible, but they’ve had no luck on
that front. For now, there’s only SCP – 1981.&nbsp;

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:55.860
During initial testing,&nbsp;
Foundation staff watched the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.860 --> 00:07:00.840
tape frequently in case this strange, corrupted
version of President Reagan had any other valuable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:05.760
predictions for the future. However, during
one of these screenings, one of the D-Class&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:09.480
observation personnel pointed and yelled at the
screen in horror.&nbsp;

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:14.700
Upon further examination of recorded footage,&nbsp;
researchers could see exactly what had concerned&nbsp;

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:19.980
the D-Class observer so much. While, in other&nbsp;
viewings of the tape, President Reagan’s press&nbsp;

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:25.800
detail had appeared totally normal, in this one&nbsp;
something was clearly amiss. Standing among the&nbsp;

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:28.500
other dull, suit-wearing&nbsp;
political aides was a tall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:34.320
figure dressed in a midnight-black cloak with a
large, conical hood obscuring his face. The figure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:40.080
didn’t appear to move in the footage – it just
stood there, menacingly. A later survey indicated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:43.920
that this figure would appear in roughly one in
seven viewings of the tape.&nbsp;

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:51.660
This cloaked figure was designated SCP – 1981 –&nbsp;
1, and he became part of the recurring imagery&nbsp;

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:57.960
in the nightmares that often followed a viewing&nbsp;
of SCP – 1981. Naturally, despite containment&nbsp;

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:02.820
and preservation attempts, the Foundation was&nbsp;
aware that just like any normal tape, natural&nbsp;

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:08.400
magnetic interference would eventually degrade&nbsp;
it beyond use. Attempts to copy the footage onto&nbsp;

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:13.560
another Betamax tape failed to reproduce the&nbsp;
anomalous effects. That’s why the Foundation has&nbsp;

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:18.480
painstakingly recorded any video and audio&nbsp;
they could via a standard commercial camcorder.&nbsp;

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:26.040
In one particularly terrifying playback, SCP –&nbsp;
1981 – 1 took the president’s place at the podium,&nbsp;

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:32.460
staring directly into the camera. The words “I&nbsp;
SEE YOU” appeared over a black screen shortly&nbsp;

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:36.900
after. Staff members were ordered never to make&nbsp;
an attempt at communicating with the figure,&nbsp;

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:42.060
and instead contact a Level 4 superior if&nbsp;
such an event occurs during a playback again.&nbsp;

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:48.300
The frightening and unfortunate effects of SCP&nbsp;
– 1981 would come to their logical conclusion&nbsp;

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:53.640
under the watchful eye of Dr. James Kyle&nbsp;
Robinson, Managing Archivist of Inert Safe-Class&nbsp;

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:59.640
Objects and Anomalous Items at Site 73. He was&nbsp;
contacted by Special Agent Arnold Rodriguez&nbsp;

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:04.620
and Special Agent Ethan Tate, members of&nbsp;
secret service with a duty of care to President&nbsp;

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:09.360
Reagan. Word had gotten to Reagan that there was&nbsp;
an anomalous artefact in the possession of the&nbsp;

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.260
Foundation that directly pertained&nbsp;
to him, and he wanted to see it.&nbsp;

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:19.620
Dr. Robinson obtained files and transcripts&nbsp;
pertaining to SCP – 1981 and handed them over to&nbsp;

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:23.820
the Agents, but refused to allow President&nbsp;
Reagan to see the tape directly without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:25.440
approval from
O5 Command.

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:31.140
But Reagan and the agents were persistent.&nbsp;
Eventually, O5 Command ordered a private&nbsp;

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:35.640
screening of the tape for President Reagan at&nbsp;
the Sanford Chemical Processing Plant – a front&nbsp;

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:41.040
business owned and operated by the Foundation&nbsp;
for Amnestic production. Dr. Robinson offered&nbsp;

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:45.660
President Reagan the use of Amnestics after&nbsp;
the session completed, but Reagan declined. The&nbsp;

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:50.580
screening took place in Conference Room B, and&nbsp;
the tape was re-played three times. It was on&nbsp;

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:53.460
the third playback that things&nbsp;
took an interesting turn.&nbsp;

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:58.260
As the mutilated Reagan on the screen began to&nbsp;
rant about drinking the blood of a child from the&nbsp;

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:02.640
skull of Vladimir Putin, Reagan began to&nbsp;
silently mouth along to the words, as though he&nbsp;

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:07.380
remembered them. He spoke about beings known&nbsp;
as “The Destroyers”, and potential apocalyptic&nbsp;

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:12.780
events to come. After the screening, Reagan&nbsp;
once again refused the offer of Amnestics, and&nbsp;

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:18.120
departed. It seemed as though all was well,&nbsp;
until a violent break-in at the Sanford Chemical&nbsp;

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:22.920
Processing Plant that left the night guard dead.&nbsp;
A large number of Amnestics had been stolen&nbsp;

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:27.000
during the break-in, and security footage&nbsp;
showed that Agents Tate and Rodriguez had been&nbsp;

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:29.820
responsible.
The two agents were tracked down and traced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:33.660
to the residence of Ronald Reagan, where the
Foundation came upon a disturbing sight:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:36.660
The agents had pillaged large&nbsp;
quantities of Class A and&nbsp;

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:42.206
B Amnestics and supplied them to President&nbsp;
Reagan, who – at some point after observing SCP –&nbsp;

00:10:42.206 --> 00:10:48.000
1981 – had been driven into a dangerous madness.&nbsp;
The two agents wanted to cure him before he&nbsp;

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:52.440
caused harm to himself or others, but their&nbsp;
bungling had come with severe consequences.&nbsp;

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:57.240
Misapplying such a high quantity of Amnestics&nbsp;
had essentially destroyed Reagan’s mind, and&nbsp;

00:10:57.240 --> 00:11:01.620
while the Foundation was able to stabilize his&nbsp;
condition, his impaired memory and cognitive&nbsp;

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:04.740
function would leave him unable&nbsp;
to care for himself independently.&nbsp;

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:10.740
In order to cover up for this grievous mistake,&nbsp;
a cover story was concocted about Reagan falling&nbsp;

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:16.260
victim to Alzheimer’s and facing severe cognitive&nbsp;
decline as a result. Both Agents Tate and&nbsp;

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:20.640
Rodriguez were fired for their actions, had&nbsp;
their memories wiped by the Foundation, and were&nbsp;

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:24.660
assigned new identities. Dr. Robinson,&nbsp;
for his part in the disaster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:28.440
had to face a Foundation Ethics
Committee Disciplinary Hearing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:32.760
While SCP – 1981 continues to&nbsp;
be classified as“Safe” due to&nbsp;

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:37.500
its unlikeliness to ever breach containment, when&nbsp;
you consider the havoc it wrought on the mind&nbsp;

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:42.840
of its singular target, “safe” is hardly the&nbsp;
word that comes to mind. It’s enough to make you&nbsp;

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:46.860
wonder what other tapes are lurking&nbsp;
out there, just waiting to be found...

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:53.400
“Every time a bell rings, an angel gets its&nbsp;
wings.” It’s an iconic line from “It’s a Wonderful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:59.520
Life” and even if you don’t believe in angels,&nbsp;
it’s a pleasant image. After all, angels are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:05.160
the embodiment of goodness and light, so an angel&nbsp;
getting its wings has to be a good thing, right?

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:10.140
Well, as anyone who’s ever eaten one&nbsp;
too many Christmas cookies can tell you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:15.420
it’s possible to have too much of a good&nbsp;
thing. Even something that sounds like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:22.020
the embodiment of all things good, in theory,&nbsp;
can become deadly when taken to the extreme.

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:27.240
That is where SCP-469, also&nbsp;
known as the Many-Winged Angel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:32.640
comes in. This angel-like creature is&nbsp;
anything but innocent and in fact it has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:38.040
been responsible for multiple deaths of SCP&nbsp;
Foundation personnel during its captivity.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:44.460
SCP-469 may be deadly, but it is also&nbsp;
undeniably beautiful in a mysterious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:48.300
ethereal way. When first seen,&nbsp;
it appears to be nothing more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:52.860
than a massive pile of pristine white&nbsp;
feathers, like something out of a pillow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.860 --> 00:12:58.140
commercial. The pile measures 24 feet in&nbsp;
diameter and weighs at least two tons.

00:12:58.140 --> 00:13:01.980
However, like many of the entities&nbsp;
contained within the walls of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:07.740
Foundation’s countless containment&nbsp;
sites, all is not as it seems with 469.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:11.760
What looks at first glance to be a&nbsp;
pile of feathers is in fact a dense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:17.280
curled mass of giant wings. The wings&nbsp;
vary in size, from the tiny wingspan of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:22.740
a sparrow to the staggering 3.6-meter&nbsp;
wingspan of the wandering albatross.

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:25.920
The one thing they have in&nbsp;
common is their plumage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:30.120
with each wing being covered with&nbsp;
the same glossy white feathers.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:36.060
The Foundation was able to perform a series of&nbsp;
X-rays on the mass of wings, revealing a skeletal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:41.400
structure beneath the feathers. Like those of&nbsp;
a bird, the wings’ bones are hollow. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:47.940
they are unnaturally soft and flexible, allowing&nbsp;
for a range of motion that no known birds possess.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:53.280
This accounts for the curvature of the wings, and&nbsp;
their ability to coil tightly into each other.

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:58.200
The X-Ray also provided the first, and&nbsp;
only recorded glimpse at the creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:02.580
hiding underneath all of the feathers. At the&nbsp;
center of the layers upon layers of wings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:07.980
is a humanoid creature, curled into a fetal&nbsp;
position. In defiance of the laws of natural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:14.220
anatomy, every single wing appears to be fused&nbsp;
to this creature’s spine. How it would be able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:19.200
to move under the weight of these wings,&nbsp;
or if it even could, is as of yet unknown.

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:24.240
The first Foundation personnel lost&nbsp;
to SCP-469 were D-class personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:29.520
D-112 and D-624, who were sent&nbsp;
in to investigate the nature of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:34.020
the creature and attempt to contact the&nbsp;
humanoid entity identified on the X-rays.

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:41.160
112 and 624 entered the room, equipped with gloves&nbsp;
and protective eye gear, as scientists watched the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:47.160
situation unfold on a monitor on a video feed. No&nbsp;
one expected much to come of the encounter, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:51.780
working hypothesis was that the layers of feathers&nbsp;
would simply be too thick to get through without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:57.840
seriously damaging the bones. It would be a&nbsp;
fairly uneventful experiment, or so they thought.

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:04.440
112 approached SCP-469 first, and attempted&nbsp;
to part a section of its feathers with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:10.020
hands as 624 stood back and observed. The&nbsp;
moment his fingertips touched the feathers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:13.740
a rustling sound filled the room.&nbsp;
The feathers began to quiver,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:17.760
shaking as if all waking up&nbsp;
at once from a deep slumber.

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:23.280
Suddenly, in the blink of an eye, the hundreds&nbsp;
and hundreds of wings unfurled and pulled 112&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:27.780
into their depths. He was swept into a&nbsp;
swirl of feathers and, within seconds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:30.480
he had disappeared from view completely.

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:35.340
Though 624 and the scientists watching on&nbsp;
their monitor could no longer see him…they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:39.540
could certainly hear him. From the moment the&nbsp;
wings pulled him into the sea of feathers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:43.800
112 had begun to scream in&nbsp;
agony. His screams persisted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:48.360
growing louder and more desperate even&nbsp;
as his voice cracked and grew weak.

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:55.560
624 stood, frozen in place with fear and shock.&nbsp;
624 was ordered to attempt to retrieve 112 from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.560 --> 00:16:02.220
the feathers, but made no move to do so. He simply&nbsp;
stared at the feathers, eyes wide, face pale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:07.620
as the pained shrieks of his colleague bounced off&nbsp;
the sterile white walls of the containment room.

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:12.540
A guard called over the intercom, threatening&nbsp;
to terminate 624 if he did not attempt to remove&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:19.080
112 from SCP-469’s grasp. This warning&nbsp;
seemed to shock 624 back into action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:24.540
and he made a run for the center feathers,&nbsp;
arms up to protect his face. Again, the sound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:31.080
of rustling as the feathers began to quake. The&nbsp;
wings unfurled once more, and 624 did not even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:36.480
have a chance to turn back before he was pulled in&nbsp;
to meet the same dismal fate as the other D Class.

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:40.140
His screams of pain joined 112’s&nbsp;
as the scientists watching over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:42.360
the monitor could do nothing to help them.

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:46.620
As the two men cried out in pain and&nbsp;
horror from within their winged prison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:51.660
something began to happen that the scientists&nbsp;
had never seen before. The feathers started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:55.740
to shake again, faster than before,&nbsp;
and at first the wings appeared to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.740 --> 00:17:00.240
be unfolding again. Upon a second look&nbsp;
though, it was clear they hadn’t moved.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:05.760
There were simply more of them now. As the men&nbsp;
continued to scream, more feathers appeared,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:10.380
the wings stretching out and elongating,&nbsp;
and new wings sprouting as if from nowhere.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:15.000
SCP-469 appeared to be feeding&nbsp;
on the sound of the screams,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:20.460
and using that energy to expand. It was only&nbsp;
after several long minutes when the screaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:25.620
finally stopped that the growth of the wings&nbsp;
did too. At this point, the wings shifted again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:32.580
expelling the bodies of 112 and 624 from within&nbsp;
its folds, dropping them limply on the ground.

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:35.760
Though their deaths were unfortunate, the loss of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:42.480
112 and 624 did reveal some new information&nbsp;
about SCP-469. First, that it could grow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:48.600
and apparently needed to feed on sounds in order&nbsp;
to do so. Second, that it was deadly to humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:55.020
and most likely to other living things as&nbsp;
well. Autopsies of 112 and 624’s corpses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.020 --> 00:18:01.260
would later reveal exactly what happened&nbsp;
to them, and how SCP-469 kills its prey.

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:05.160
Though 469’s feathers may look as&nbsp;
though they would be soft to the touch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:10.140
each feather is actually made up of sharp barbs&nbsp;
that are capable of piercing clothing and skin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:10.140 --> 00:18:15.240
These barbs release a neurotoxin into the&nbsp;
system that activates every pain receptor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:19.440
in the body of the victim. The neurotoxin&nbsp;
present in these feathers has not been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:23.700
identified anywhere else in nature, but is&nbsp;
somewhat similar in structure and function&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:29.400
to the neurotoxins excreted by the cone snail&nbsp;
and in the bite of the blue-ringed octopus.

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:35.280
In addition to the pain-inducing neurotoxin, the&nbsp;
feathers also carry several unidentified stimulant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:36.660
compounds, which seem to be intended to keep the&nbsp;
victim awake for as long as possible. Where the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:40.560
neurotoxin on its own would induce enough&nbsp;
pain for the affected party to pass out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:44.520
almost immediately, the stimulants&nbsp;
serve to keep the victim conscious.

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:50.400
SCP Foundation scientists posit that this&nbsp;
is so that 469 can get as much noise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:55.020
in this case in the form of screams,&nbsp;
out of its prey as possible and achieve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:58.920
maximum growth before the captive&nbsp;
creature dies or goes into shock.

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:04.800
Further experiments confirmed this theory,&nbsp;
and showed that SCP 469 will react similarly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:11.100
when exposed to any living creature capable of&nbsp;
making a sound and experiencing pain, not just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:17.100
humans. Nonliving matter though, including&nbsp;
dead animals, elicit no response from 469.

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:21.660
Additional experiments were then undertaken&nbsp;
that involved applying various different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:27.420
sounds in order to test their effect on&nbsp;
SCP 469’s growth. Though it feeds on any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:32.460
sounds produced in its presence, it seems&nbsp;
to respond most strongly to musical sounds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:38.040
exhibiting a particularly strong response&nbsp;
to classical music. No sound elicits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:42.600
a stronger reaction from this creature,&nbsp;
however, than the sound of ringing bells.

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:46.200
It is rumored that when a bell was&nbsp;
rung in the presence of the 469,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:50.880
the humanoid at the center of the feathers&nbsp;
is said to have moved for the first time on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:55.800
record. Apparently whatever is at the center&nbsp;
appeared to “wake up” and unfurl its wings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:55.800 --> 00:20:01.140
revealing itself. But unfortunately, all&nbsp;
security footage of this incident has been wiped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:06.180
and the data has been expunged from the record&nbsp;
leaving the creature’s true form a mystery.

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:10.680
You may be remembering that four members of&nbsp;
Foundation personnel on record were lost to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:17.280
SCP-469, and that only two have been mentioned&nbsp;
so far. The second pair of casualties resulted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:23.160
when the Foundation attempted to terminate&nbsp;
SCP 469. Believing that there was no more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:27.180
scientific benefit to keeping it alive,&nbsp;
or at least that the possible benefits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:27.180 --> 00:20:33.660
did not outweigh the risks, it was ordered that&nbsp;
SCP-469 be terminated by any means necessary.

00:20:33.660 --> 00:20:38.760
Two skilled personnel, Dr. Jones and Dr.&nbsp;
Smith, were sent into the containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:43.980
facility in hazmat gear, armed with several&nbsp;
sharp instruments. They were to attempt to use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:48.060
these to cut through the forest of feathers&nbsp;
and soft bones until they could reach the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:52.980
humanoid at the center. It was presumed that&nbsp;
once they did and the creature no longer had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:57.360
the protection of its poisonous feathers,&nbsp;
that it would be relatively easy to kill.

00:20:57.360 --> 00:21:00.180
They could not have been more wrong.

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:04.980
Dr. Jones approached the dense cover of feathers&nbsp;
with a pair of sharpened gardening shears,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:10.440
while Dr. Smith opted for a machete. At first,&nbsp;
the strategy appeared to be working. Dr. Jones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:10.440 --> 00:21:15.540
made several quick cuts, with feathers fluttering&nbsp;
to the floor and sticking to the Hazmat suit as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:21.060
Dr. Smith slashed into the feathers with his&nbsp;
machete, making similarly promising progress.

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:25.800
However, the situation quickly took a turn&nbsp;
for the worse when Dr. Jones dropped her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:30.900
shears and let out a bloodcurdling scream.&nbsp;
The feathers had taken a little longer to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:30.900 --> 00:21:35.580
through the suit to her skin, but somehow&nbsp;
they had managed to find a way just the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:40.140
same. Smith grabbed Jones and attempted to&nbsp;
make a break for it, but he was too slow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:40.140 --> 00:21:45.180
and far too close to the feathers already.&nbsp;
The wings wrapped around them and swallowed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:45.180 --> 00:21:50.400
them both up, leaving the researchers outside&nbsp;
helpless to do anything but listen to their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:55.080
screams and wait for them to go quiet.&nbsp;
After several minutes they finally did,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:55.080 --> 00:22:01.620
and the now larger SCP-469 had officially&nbsp;
claimed another two Foundation personnel.
 &nbsp;

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.260
Obviously, 469 could not be terminated using any&nbsp;
methods that would place the responsible personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:13.140
within its grasp. That was simply too risky.&nbsp;
So, the Foundation selected a team of D-class&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:18.120
personnel to attempt to burn the feathers with&nbsp;
an array of flamethrowers. Though the feathers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:18.120 --> 00:22:23.160
were vulnerable to fire and began to blacken&nbsp;
and disintegrate on contact, the sound of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:23.160 --> 00:22:30.300
flames being expelled was loud enough to feed&nbsp;
SCP 469. Its growth was so quick in response to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:30.300 --> 00:22:35.160
the noise that the fire could not keep up with the&nbsp;
amount of new feathers and wings being produced.

00:22:35.160 --> 00:22:39.840
By the time the flamethrowers ran&nbsp;
out of propellant, 469 was the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:39.840 --> 00:22:43.980
size as it had been when they started. Other&nbsp;
termination methods have been discussed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:43.980 --> 00:22:48.420
including the possibility of submerging the&nbsp;
entire creature in a highly corrosive acid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:48.420 --> 00:22:53.400
but so far this has not yet been attempted.&nbsp;
Whatever they end up trying, it is clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:53.400 --> 00:22:58.740
that nothing that produces a significant&nbsp;
amount of noise will be able to kill 469.

00:22:58.740 --> 00:23:03.780
So, where is it now? What’s become of this&nbsp;
perverse angel with the never-ending wings?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:08.400
Currently, it is kept isolated in an airtight,&nbsp;
soundproof chamber where nothing can trigger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:14.700
the growth of any more wings. So, what&nbsp;
is it? An angel? A demon? A twisted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:20.400
mutated bird of some kind? It is entirely&nbsp;
possible we will never know. But It’s a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:20.400 --> 00:23:25.320
Wonderful Life had something right, even&nbsp;
if by accident. Every time a bell rings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:30.120
something, twisted and deadly&nbsp;
though it may be, gets its wings.

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:36.300
It was July of 2004, and Bill Murray was enjoying&nbsp;
the peak of an extremely successful career.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:36.900 --> 00:23:41.580
Not only had the iconic actor starred in some of&nbsp;
the most beloved comedies of the 20th Century,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:41.580 --> 00:23:47.040
including Ghostbusters and Groundhog Day, he’d&nbsp;
voiced the main character of the recently-released&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:47.040 --> 00:23:52.980
live action Garfield movie. It’d been a financial&nbsp;
success, but it was a critical flop. Not that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:52.980 --> 00:23:59.160
this bothered Bill – he was happy with the&nbsp;
performance... and the paycheck. What he wouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:59.160 --> 00:24:06.360
be quite as happy about was the horrifying&nbsp;
encounter he was about to have with SCP – 3166.&nbsp;

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:12.480
On July 8th, Bill was enjoying a cold drink on&nbsp;
the porch of his luxurious Beverly Hills home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:12.480 --> 00:24:18.480
The sky was beginning to darken as the sun set&nbsp;
in the west. It was a blissful evening. His wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:18.480 --> 00:24:24.600
Jennifer, was inside, watching TV. Nothing seemed&nbsp;
particularly out of the ordinary…Until he noticed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:24.600 --> 00:24:29.700
a quick flash of orange in the distance. It&nbsp;
was almost too fast to register, this large,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:29.700 --> 00:24:34.140
orange shape darting past the corner of his&nbsp;
eye. For a second, he entertained the thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:34.140 --> 00:24:38.460
that it might have been an escaped tiger,&nbsp;
but it was gone too fast to really tell.&nbsp;

00:24:38.460 --> 00:24:42.600
Bill finished his drink and headed&nbsp;
inside. He’d had enough for one night.&nbsp;

00:24:42.600 --> 00:24:47.760
The next morning, he got up to read the paper, and&nbsp;
found the Garfield movie getting slaughtered by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:47.760 --> 00:24:53.160
the critics. One review stated “no one can accuse&nbsp;
Garfield: The Movie of infidelity to its source:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:53.160 --> 00:24:58.440
It faithfully conveys the banality of Jim&nbsp;
Davis's cartoon” Another called it“a film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:58.440 --> 00:25:04.260
without energy and without spirit.” He put the&nbsp;
paper down and ate his breakfast. A few blows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:04.260 --> 00:25:08.220
to the ego were worth it for the paydays&nbsp;
that came with big budget family films.&nbsp;

00:25:08.220 --> 00:25:13.800
Just then his wife came to him with a strange&nbsp;
question: Were you walking around downstairs in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:13.800 --> 00:25:19.140
the middle of the night? No, he hadn’t, he’d&nbsp;
been sleeping like a baby. Why did she ask?&nbsp;

00:25:19.140 --> 00:25:23.280
“Well…” Jennifer said. “I heard&nbsp;
some rustling downstairs last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:23.280 --> 00:25:28.200
night. It sounded like something big.”
He hadn’t heard anything though and told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:28.200 --> 00:25:33.180
her it was probably just her imagination. He put&nbsp;
it out of his mind and continued about his day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:33.180 --> 00:25:38.340
He decided he would keep his eyes peeled for that&nbsp;
orange blur again though. Bill didn’t see anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:38.340 --> 00:25:43.800
peculiar the rest of the morning and went to a&nbsp;
local café for lunch. He ordered a coffee and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:43.800 --> 00:25:48.060
a cream cheese bagel, then made a quick trip&nbsp;
to the bathroom while his food was prepared.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:48.060 --> 00:25:53.640
When Bill returned to his table though, he&nbsp;
was something strange. Instead of a bagel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:53.640 --> 00:25:59.640
there was a large helping of lasagne on the table.&nbsp;
What was going on? This café didn’t even serve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:59.640 --> 00:26:06.660
lasagne. Bill knew something was terribly wrong.
Things only got stranger when Bill came home to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:06.660 --> 00:26:11.400
find a small tuft of orange fur snagged on&nbsp;
the frame of his front door. And it wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:11.400 --> 00:26:17.760
synthetic fur like you see on plush toys or&nbsp;
stuffed animals. No, this was real animal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:17.760 --> 00:26:22.440
fur. Maybe someone was just goofing off&nbsp;
or trying to play some weird prank on him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:22.440 --> 00:26:30.960
but it didn’t feel like it. Deep down, Bill Murray&nbsp;
knew that he was in grave danger. Whoever, or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:30.960 --> 00:26:38.460
whatever, was behind this… it wanted to hurt him.
That night, his worst fears were realized. Bill’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:38.460 --> 00:26:42.300
wife had left town for the week and he was heading&nbsp;
to the kitchen in the middle of the night for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:42.300 --> 00:26:47.580
glass of water, when he saw something - A huge&nbsp;
figure moving up against the glass door leading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:47.580 --> 00:26:54.540
to his backyard. The thing was huge, nearly seven&nbsp;
feet tall, with a bloated, fur-covered, misshapen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:54.540 --> 00:27:01.740
body that was pressed up against the door. Its&nbsp;
fur was bright, garish orange – a cartoon orange.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:02.700 --> 00:27:08.700
Strangest of all though was the sound it&nbsp;
was making. It sounded like it was purring.&nbsp;

00:27:08.700 --> 00:27:13.560
Bill backed away from the door and then ran&nbsp;
back to his room to hide. The whole night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:13.560 --> 00:27:17.940
he sat cowering as he heard scratching&nbsp;
against the walls, like something was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:17.940 --> 00:27:23.760
trying to get in. He was terrified and too&nbsp;
scared to do anything, even move. Finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:23.760 --> 00:27:29.160
as morning broke, the noises seemed to stop.&nbsp;
Bill had to do something. He couldn’t let this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:29.160 --> 00:27:34.860
nightmare go on another night. What if things got&nbsp;
worse? What if that thing managed to get inside?&nbsp;

00:27:34.860 --> 00:27:40.500
He called the local police and when they arrived,&nbsp;
he explained the incredibly strange situation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:40.500 --> 00:27:45.720
as best he could. He told them he was being&nbsp;
stalked by some kind of huge cat, or at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:45.720 --> 00:27:51.300
someone dressed like a huge cat. Also there was&nbsp;
lasagne involved. The officers interviewing him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:51.300 --> 00:27:56.460
could barely contain their laughter as he told&nbsp;
them his story. A giant orange cat? Perhaps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:56.460 --> 00:28:01.440
one of them theorized, he’d angered some kind of&nbsp;
obsessive Garfield fan through his involvement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:01.440 --> 00:28:06.240
in the vive action movie. After all, the&nbsp;
original comic had been running for years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:06.240 --> 00:28:11.700
and had been extremely popular. Who knows what&nbsp;
kind of nut jobs were obsessed with seeing only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:11.700 --> 00:28:17.700
a faithful adaptation of the source material?
As the officers departed, Bill was confident that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:17.700 --> 00:28:22.500
they weren’t taking him seriously. He couldn’t&nbsp;
rely on any of them for protection. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:22.500 --> 00:28:26.220
from a multi-decade movie career,&nbsp;
he had plenty of disposable income,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:26.220 --> 00:28:31.200
and decided to hire a private security team to&nbsp;
protect him while he looked into this mystery.&nbsp;

00:28:31.200 --> 00:28:36.480
He had two trained bodyguards positioned around&nbsp;
his home at all times for the next month. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:36.480 --> 00:28:42.480
were armed, and given the cryptic orders to fire&nbsp;
on anything orange. Meanwhile, Bill began to fall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:42.480 --> 00:28:48.180
down a Garfield rabbit hole. He felt strangely&nbsp;
compelled to research all the Garfield media he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:48.180 --> 00:28:53.580
could find, as though the answer to his terrifying&nbsp;
situation was somehow hidden between the lines.&nbsp;

00:28:53.580 --> 00:28:59.400
Bill explored the entire backlog of thousands of&nbsp;
comic strips. He read the books and interviews&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:59.400 --> 00:29:05.100
with Jim Davis. He watched the cartoons and&nbsp;
straight-to-DVD animated movies. Ironically for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:05.100 --> 00:29:10.680
a guy who’d recently portrayed the lasagne-loving&nbsp;
orange cat, Bill had never felt quite so immersed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:10.680 --> 00:29:16.380
in the character before. He found a strange&nbsp;
pathos in the routine of Garfield and his friends.&nbsp;

00:29:16.380 --> 00:29:23.040
One particular comic really piqued his interest,&nbsp;
though. Originally published in October of 1989,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:23.040 --> 00:29:28.980
the comic began with Garfield being woken up by&nbsp;
a strange chill, an almost eerie sensation. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:28.980 --> 00:29:33.480
character observed aloud that he didn’t feel like&nbsp;
he was in his own home. He explored his little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:33.480 --> 00:29:39.720
home further, trying to find his owner Jon or his&nbsp;
housemate and sometimes nemesis, Odie, but found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:39.720 --> 00:29:45.540
nothing. As Garfield remarked on feeling alone, a&nbsp;
purple speech box delivered the sinister message:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:46.620 --> 00:29:53.160
“You have no idea how alone you are,&nbsp;
Garfield.” He then finds that his home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:53.160 --> 00:29:59.100
looks like it’s been abandoned for years. The&nbsp;
“For Sale” sign outside is practically ancient.&nbsp;

00:29:59.760 --> 00:30:06.960
Garfield slowly comes to a horrifying revelation:&nbsp;
Everyone really is gone, and his adventures and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:06.960 --> 00:30:11.520
friends now exist only in his imagination.&nbsp;
He’s trapped in a prison of his own creation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:11.520 --> 00:30:17.760
trying to stave off his endless loneliness, in&nbsp;
denial about the reality of his situation. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:17.760 --> 00:30:23.460
comic ended with a quote directly from Jim Davis&nbsp;
himself, saying “An imagination is a powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:23.460 --> 00:30:29.340
tool. It can tint memories of the past, shade&nbsp;
perceptions of the present, or paint a future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:29.340 --> 00:30:36.240
so vivid that it can entice... or terrify, all&nbsp;
depending upon how we conduct ourselves today...”&nbsp;

00:30:36.240 --> 00:30:42.180
As he read those words, Bill Murray felt a chill&nbsp;
down his spine. Why had he wanted to be involved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:42.180 --> 00:30:47.160
in the Garfield movie in the first place? What&nbsp;
had he gotten himself into? Before he could slip&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:47.160 --> 00:30:54.420
any deeper into his own mind, Bill heard a faint,&nbsp;
choked scream downstairs. He felt his breath catch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:54.420 --> 00:31:00.420
in his throat. He was terrified but he needed to&nbsp;
see what was happening. He carefully and quietly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:00.420 --> 00:31:05.880
began to creep down the stairs. At the bottom, he&nbsp;
poked his head around a corner, and that’s when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:05.880 --> 00:31:11.100
he saw a member of his security detail lying dead&nbsp;
on the floor. His face was blue from asphyxiation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:11.100 --> 00:31:16.920
his mouth was stuffed with lasagne. It&nbsp;
looked like he had been force-fed to death.&nbsp;

00:31:18.000 --> 00:31:23.820
Bill wanted to scream but he couldn’t, or maybe&nbsp;
knew he shouldn’t. Just then he heard a soft,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:23.820 --> 00:31:29.880
meaty thumping noise coming from the nearby living&nbsp;
room. He didn’t know why, but he felt compelled to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:29.880 --> 00:31:36.300
approach as if by forces beyond his control. He&nbsp;
made his way to the living room, and when he got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:36.300 --> 00:31:43.320
there, he saw where the noise was coming from.
Bill’s jaw dropped in pure horror. There was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:43.320 --> 00:31:48.060
the other member of his security detail, lying&nbsp;
limp and lifeless under a giant orange figure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:48.060 --> 00:31:54.060
It was a grotesquely huge creature, wearing what&nbsp;
looked to be a kind of crude Garfield outfit made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:54.060 --> 00:32:00.960
of sewn-together cat pelts. It stank of pasta and&nbsp;
rotten meat. In its giant paw, it held a golden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:00.960 --> 00:32:06.840
trophy, which it was using to pound the security&nbsp;
guard’s head into mush while making quiet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:06.840 --> 00:32:13.500
cat-like purring noises. The creature suddenly&nbsp;
stopped and looked up, locking eyes with Bill.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:13.500 --> 00:32:19.740
The fear of death came over him. He froze,&nbsp;
as the giant, freakish Garfield stepped over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:19.740 --> 00:32:25.740
Donny’s corpse, and began to come towards him.
Bill turned and ran, but Garfield was gaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:25.740 --> 00:32:30.600
on him. Before he could make it to the front door,&nbsp;
the creature knocked him over. He was laid out on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:30.600 --> 00:32:36.000
the ground, looking up at it, as it reached into&nbsp;
its own body cavity and began to pull out handfuls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:40.920
of lasagne. He was just about to shove a wad of&nbsp;
the horrible decaying pasta into Bill’s mouth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:40.920 --> 00:32:45.540
when suddenly, a DING was heard and&nbsp;
the creature stopped. It looked up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:45.540 --> 00:32:50.460
as if sniffing the air, and then suddenly&nbsp;
turned and lumbered towards the kitchen.&nbsp;

00:32:52.020 --> 00:32:55.860
Bill watched as the Garfield monster&nbsp;
entered the kitchen where, somehow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:55.860 --> 00:33:01.380
there was a steaming hot fresh lasagne sitting&nbsp;
in the open oven. The creature had sensed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:01.380 --> 00:33:05.940
presence of external lasagne, and felt the&nbsp;
compulsion to integrate it into its body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:05.940 --> 00:33:08.880
grabbing fistfulls and shoving it into itself.&nbsp;

00:33:09.900 --> 00:33:14.220
Just then, a group of highly trained SCP&nbsp;
Foundation personnel burst into the room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:14.220 --> 00:33:19.920
and subdued the creature. It had been an ambush.&nbsp;
The Foundation had been tipped off to the presence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:19.920 --> 00:33:24.480
of the creature by monitoring the local police&nbsp;
department dispatches, and the report of a seven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:24.480 --> 00:33:30.060
foot tall comic book cat terrorizing a Hollywood&nbsp;
actor was definitely worth looking into. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:30.060 --> 00:33:37.140
monster that had almost taken Bill Murray’s life&nbsp;
was SCP – 3166, a deadly pataphysical being that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:37.140 --> 00:33:42.840
tends to manifest around people somehow involved&nbsp;
in the Garfield intellectual property. It appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:42.840 --> 00:33:47.520
whenever the public perception of Garfield falls&nbsp;
out of favor, and because Bill had starred in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:47.520 --> 00:33:54.060
critically-panned Garfield movie, he was currently&nbsp;
at the very top of SCP – 3166’s hit list.&nbsp;

00:33:54.900 --> 00:33:59.220
Thankfully, he managed to survive his&nbsp;
terrifying ordeal, and was administered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:59.220 --> 00:34:03.180
amnestics by Foundation personnel so&nbsp;
he could return to his normal life.&nbsp;

00:34:03.180 --> 00:34:08.340
This frightening and mysterious creature&nbsp;
had been around since 1989, appearing after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:08.340 --> 00:34:12.540
the publication of the haunting Garfield&nbsp;
comic that Bill had read that very night.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:13.620 --> 00:34:18.000
It appeared in the office of United Media, who&nbsp;
were the publishers of the Garfield comic strip&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:24.000
at the time, and began wreaking havoc. Since&nbsp;
then, the creature’s manifestation has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:24.000 --> 00:34:28.680
a constant threat whenever Garfield loses&nbsp;
its popularity or audience. As a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:28.680 --> 00:34:33.780
the Foundation has spent years as the funding&nbsp;
source behind all Garfield media, and even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:33.780 --> 00:34:39.240
planting hypnotic memetics into the comic strips&nbsp;
to ensure that there is always a loyal fanbase.&nbsp;

00:34:39.780 --> 00:34:46.860
The fur is indeed real, organic cat fur, albeit an&nbsp;
unnaturally orange color, and instead of organs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:46.860 --> 00:34:52.620
the creature is filled with lasagne. Worst&nbsp;
of all though, is that testing has revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:52.620 --> 00:34:57.360
that the meat in the lasagne is genetically&nbsp;
identical to the flesh of Garfield’s creator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:57.360 --> 00:35:04.440
Jim Davis. How did this thing come into existence?&nbsp;
Perhaps it was Jim’s sheer force of imagination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:04.440 --> 00:35:10.800
that dragged it into being. As he himself&nbsp;
said, “An imagination is a powerful tool.”&nbsp;

00:35:10.800 --> 00:35:15.360
All in all, it’s lucky that Bill Murray was&nbsp;
able to survive his encounter, and return to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:15.360 --> 00:35:21.060
his normal life – well, as normal as life can&nbsp;
be for Bill Murray. And if you see Bill Murray,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:21.060 --> 00:35:26.940
don’t bother asking him about SCP –&nbsp;
3166. The amnestics were quite effective,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:26.940 --> 00:35:32.220
and just as he’s fond of saying&nbsp;
himself, no one will ever believe you.

00:35:32.220 --> 00:35:37.920
In a remote part of Russia, a mysterious disease&nbsp;
outbreak was tearing through a tiny farming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:37.920 --> 00:35:44.160
village with terrifying side effects. There was&nbsp;
no cure, no clue to where it came from, and worst&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:44.160 --> 00:35:50.580
of all, the disease’s terrifying impact didn’t&nbsp;
end with death. No, it was after those carrying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:50.580 --> 00:35:56.580
the disease died, that the real horror started.
After an agonizing fever that leaves the victims&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:56.580 --> 00:36:01.620
writhing in pain, they quickly succumb to&nbsp;
the disease, only to rise from their graves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:01.620 --> 00:36:06.000
to wreak havoc on the living. The virus&nbsp;
continues to spread, until the corpses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:06.000 --> 00:36:10.980
outnumber those trying to hide from them, as&nbsp;
the world spirals into almost certain ruin.&nbsp;

00:36:10.980 --> 00:36:16.440
It sounds like the plot of a zombie movie, but for&nbsp;
the SCP Foundation this is anything but fiction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:16.440 --> 00:36:21.780
and the terror that unfolded in that little&nbsp;
Siberian town is the first recorded encounter with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:21.780 --> 00:36:30.450
SCP - 610, also known as, The Flesh That Hates.
First, livestock began to vanish from farms. Theft&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:30.450 --> 00:36:36.180
or wild animals were suspected, but no suspects&nbsp;
could be found, and no mutilated remains turned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:36.180 --> 00:36:41.340
up. The animals weren’t being stolen, and they&nbsp;
weren’t being eaten, so…what happened to them?&nbsp;

00:36:41.340 --> 00:36:45.780
With no more animals left to lose, the&nbsp;
farmers themselves then began to disappear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:45.780 --> 00:36:50.880
but the authorities refused to take the missing&nbsp;
persons cases seriously. The missing farmers’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:50.880 --> 00:36:54.960
families would contact the police, make&nbsp;
a report, and then the whole thing was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:54.960 --> 00:37:00.180
forgotten. It was written off as just another&nbsp;
unsolved disappearance, which wasn’t uncommon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:00.180 --> 00:37:05.760
in the wild and unforgiving region. Then&nbsp;
the police themselves began to disappear.&nbsp;

00:37:05.760 --> 00:37:09.960
The families of the missing farmers would&nbsp;
sometimes report strange sounds from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:09.960 --> 00:37:15.600
surrounding woods, describing moans and&nbsp;
inhuman screeches of pain. One young boy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:15.600 --> 00:37:20.520
reported seeing a cow with what he described as&nbsp;
“tentacles” lurking around the edge of the trees.&nbsp;

00:37:20.520 --> 00:37:25.440
Regional police were dispatched to the location,&nbsp;
and ordered to investigate and report back on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:25.440 --> 00:37:30.960
their findings within 24 hours. But the units&nbsp;
sent to the area didn’t report back, and were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:30.960 --> 00:37:36.360
never heard from again. Upon learning of the&nbsp;
reports, the Russian government grew increasingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:36.360 --> 00:37:41.880
concerned, fearing domestic insurgency or foreign&nbsp;
espionage of some kind could be at play. They sent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:41.880 --> 00:37:47.400
a small team of special agents to the area,&nbsp;
and, one by one, those agents disappeared,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:47.400 --> 00:37:51.360
just like the others before them.
It seemed no one who went into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:51.360 --> 00:37:57.240
village after the disappearances started ever&nbsp;
came out again. They had all simply vanished.&nbsp;

00:37:57.240 --> 00:38:01.560
Desperate for answers, the Russian government&nbsp;
contacted the only people in the world who could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:01.560 --> 00:38:06.840
help - The SCP Foundation. What the Foundation&nbsp;
found over the course of their investigation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:06.840 --> 00:38:11.700
would shock and unnerve them, going beyond&nbsp;
anything they had previously discovered.&nbsp;

00:38:11.700 --> 00:38:16.800
Before the investigation officially began, the&nbsp;
affected area was sealed off by the Russian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:16.800 --> 00:38:21.420
government. Not knowing if it would be safe to&nbsp;
send researchers into the containment perimeter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:21.420 --> 00:38:26.520
the Foundation set up a small camera mounted&nbsp;
unit, nicknamed Herbie, to capture footage of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:26.520 --> 00:38:31.500
whatever remained of the village. The images&nbsp;
captured by Herbie revealed what exactly had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:31.500 --> 00:38:37.920
become of the people in this doomed village,&nbsp;
and the true, nightmarish nature of SCP-610.&nbsp;

00:38:38.820 --> 00:38:44.220
SCP-610 is a Keter-class entity, meaning&nbsp;
it’s an anomaly that’s exceedingly difficult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:44.220 --> 00:38:49.200
to contain consistently or reliably, with&nbsp;
containment procedures often being extensive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:49.200 --> 00:38:54.480
and complex. 610 is a highly contagious skin&nbsp;
disease that initially manifests like an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:54.480 --> 00:38:59.160
ordinary allergic reaction, with symptoms&nbsp;
including increased sensitivity, itching,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:59.160 --> 00:39:03.960
and a rash. But within just three hours of&nbsp;
those initial symptoms appearing, the rash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:03.960 --> 00:39:09.660
starts to turn into masses of scar tissue on the&nbsp;
chest and arms. These masses spread over the legs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:09.660 --> 00:39:15.240
and back of the victim, and completely consume&nbsp;
them in thick, rubbery flesh within five hours.&nbsp;

00:39:15.900 --> 00:39:20.280
Once they’re covered, the victim will cease&nbsp;
all vital functions. Unfortunately for them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:20.280 --> 00:39:25.860
and doubly so for those around them, they do not&nbsp;
stay dead. About three minutes after expiring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:25.860 --> 00:39:30.420
the victim’s vitals will restart at a heightened&nbsp;
rate, and the masses of flesh encasing their body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:30.420 --> 00:39:35.760
will begin to move and multiply, mutating them&nbsp;
into a form beyond anything resembling the human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:35.760 --> 00:39:41.280
they once were. The specific type of mutation&nbsp;
varies from case to case, but has included the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:41.280 --> 00:39:47.160
head becoming massive and bulbous, the growth of&nbsp;
extra limbs, and, in especially gruesome cases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:47.160 --> 00:39:52.620
the victim’s body splitting apart to allow extra&nbsp;
tendrils of flesh to sprout from the open wound.&nbsp;

00:39:52.620 --> 00:39:58.380
Occasionally, an infected person will stop moving&nbsp;
and become rooted to the ground in a set location.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:58.380 --> 00:40:04.020
Once it is settled, their flesh will spread&nbsp;
itself across the ground, encasing all nearby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:04.020 --> 00:40:09.240
objects in flaps of scar tissue. The infected that&nbsp;
maintain their mobility are highly aggressive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:09.240 --> 00:40:13.440
even violent, and will attempt to infect&nbsp;
any living thing that comes into their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:13.440 --> 00:40:18.720
line of sight. The disease does not only infect&nbsp;
humans, and can take over any living organism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:18.720 --> 00:40:23.760
within a matter of hours. Due to the highly&nbsp;
contagious and dangerous nature of the disease,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:23.760 --> 00:40:29.700
safe observation of infected specimens and areas&nbsp;
is only possible with drones and mounted cameras.&nbsp;

00:40:29.700 --> 00:40:33.600
This brings us back to Herbie,&nbsp;
the first such mounted camera&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:33.600 --> 00:40:38.040
to record footage of the infected area.
 
Herbie was deployed into the infection site,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:38.040 --> 00:40:42.900
also known as Site A, without any damage.&nbsp;
It remained at the outside perimeter of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:42.900 --> 00:40:47.760
village for two hours, observing several infected&nbsp;
humans, and fire damage to many of the homes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:47.760 --> 00:40:53.580
before following an infected into an intact house.&nbsp;
Herbie’s camera feed captured the infected person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:53.580 --> 00:40:58.320
entering the house and sitting down at the table&nbsp;
inside. There were several other infected humans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:58.320 --> 00:41:03.660
in the house, and one unidentified infected&nbsp;
creature that remained immobile under the table.&nbsp;

00:41:03.660 --> 00:41:08.580
After viciously assaulting one of the other&nbsp;
infected humans, the infected returned to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:08.580 --> 00:41:13.740
the table and began to lay out plates on top&nbsp;
of it. Pieces of its flesh began to wriggle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:13.740 --> 00:41:19.080
and tear away from its body, before settling&nbsp;
onto each plate. Once the plates were filled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:19.080 --> 00:41:24.540
the infected sitting at the table began to grab&nbsp;
at the flesh and crush it into their mouths, in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:24.540 --> 00:41:29.400
perverse imitation of a normal mealtime gathering.
After capturing this stomach-churning display,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:29.400 --> 00:41:34.200
Herbie left the house and continued to explore&nbsp;
the village. It recorded footage of a large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:34.200 --> 00:41:38.460
stack of bodies that seemed to be made up&nbsp;
of both Russian military and civilians,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:38.460 --> 00:41:43.260
with an infected sitting on top. As Herbie&nbsp;
maneuvered toward the remains of the town hall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:43.260 --> 00:41:48.060
an infected grabbed the rover off of the ground.&nbsp;
Herbie’s camera was able to capture the face of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:48.060 --> 00:41:52.920
the infected that grabbed the rover. The face&nbsp;
was that of a young girl around ten years old,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:52.920 --> 00:41:59.400
strangely intact atop a large, distorted body.
The final moments of Herbie’s camera feed captured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:59.400 --> 00:42:03.840
the infected girl’s face bursting open,&nbsp;
revealing tendrils of flesh that pulled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:03.840 --> 00:42:10.320
Herbie into the gaping maw. Then, the feed&nbsp;
cut to black. Herbie was regarded as lost,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:10.320 --> 00:42:15.120
but the video feed briefly resumed five hours&nbsp;
later, showing the camera covered with an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:15.120 --> 00:42:21.360
unidentified slime. After this, the video feed&nbsp;
was cut for good, and Herbie abandoned in Site A.&nbsp;

00:42:21.360 --> 00:42:26.880
The Foundation has sent several manned expeditions&nbsp;
into Site A, where many expedition forces have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:26.880 --> 00:42:31.680
fallen victim to the infected. Several operatives&nbsp;
were also lost in an earthquake that revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:31.680 --> 00:42:36.000
a network of underground tunnels. A manned&nbsp;
expedition into these tunnels was attempted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:36.000 --> 00:42:39.300
and the video feed that was captured&nbsp;
by the researchers on the expedition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:39.300 --> 00:42:44.280
was deeply disturbing. There were images of&nbsp;
an abandoned church filled with infected,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:44.280 --> 00:42:50.100
and a mass of uninfected or partially infected&nbsp;
human captives. The final moments of the video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:50.100 --> 00:42:53.760
feed from this expedition captured&nbsp;
several operatives being murdered by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:53.760 --> 00:42:58.440
an infected human wielding a farming scythe,&nbsp;
indicating that the infected are capable of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:58.440 --> 00:43:04.080
using simple weaponry in addition to brute force.
The use of this weapon, paired with the presence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:04.080 --> 00:43:08.280
of captives in the underground tunnels,&nbsp;
paints a terrifying picture of the kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:08.280 --> 00:43:14.040
of organization the infected are capable of. No&nbsp;
more manned expeditions have been attempted, or,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:14.040 --> 00:43:19.800
if they have, they have been highly classified.
 
Ordinarily, once a new SCP is discovered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:19.800 --> 00:43:24.180
it is placed in containment at the Foundation,&nbsp;
with special procedures in place, so that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:24.180 --> 00:43:29.040
can be studied or even neutralized in the rare&nbsp;
occasions where it’s deemed necessary. When it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:29.040 --> 00:43:36.060
comes to SCP-610 though, containment might just be&nbsp;
impossible. It simply covers too much area, and is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:36.060 --> 00:43:41.400
too dangerous to expose to human researchers.&nbsp;
Instead, all infected areas have been isolated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:41.400 --> 00:43:45.660
with the permission of the Russian government.&nbsp;
There is an official perimeter established around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:45.660 --> 00:43:50.700
these areas, and any civilians that approach them&nbsp;
are told to leave under the pretense of ongoing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:50.700 --> 00:43:55.980
military operations. For once, a top secret&nbsp;
military project is the more innocent answer.&nbsp;

00:43:55.980 --> 00:44:00.540
Armed guards are placed at the perimeter&nbsp;
of every infected area, and any living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:00.540 --> 00:44:06.060
thing with symptoms of SCP-610 spotted near&nbsp;
the perimeter is to be immobilized, killed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:06.060 --> 00:44:11.820
and burned from as far away as possible. Any&nbsp;
living thing that comes in contact with SCP-610,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:11.820 --> 00:44:18.240
whether a soldier, a scientist, or a civilian,&nbsp;
is immediately terminated, and their remains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:18.240 --> 00:44:22.740
destroyed. If someone comes within three&nbsp;
meters of an infected organism, they will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:22.740 --> 00:44:27.360
be quarantined and remotely examined to determine&nbsp;
if they have been infected. While the spread of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:27.360 --> 00:44:32.760
SCP-610 can be airborne, it has been determined&nbsp;
to be far less contagious when spread through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:32.760 --> 00:44:38.400
air particles as opposed to physical contact.
The infection sites remain active to this day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:38.400 --> 00:44:43.200
like modern day leper colonies. Though they&nbsp;
are isolated from the general population,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:43.200 --> 00:44:49.920
and the military is doing everything in their&nbsp;
power to contain the infected, SCP-610 is still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:49.920 --> 00:44:55.380
very much alive. It is rare for an entity to&nbsp;
exist that the Foundation cannot truly contain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:55.380 --> 00:45:02.100
but can only try to guard against, and that makes&nbsp;
this infection all the more terrifying. Who knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:02.100 --> 00:45:08.460
how much it has mutated over the years, growing,&nbsp;
spreading, hungry for new hosts? There is still so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:08.460 --> 00:45:13.020
much that the Foundation does not know about&nbsp;
the Flesh That Hates, such as how it works,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:13.020 --> 00:45:17.820
what it can do, or even where it came from,&nbsp;
since the origin of the first infection&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:17.820 --> 00:45:23.700
is still, at this point, entirely unknown.
It has shown itself to be capable of learning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:23.700 --> 00:45:28.800
planning, and protecting itself, so who is to say&nbsp;
that it couldn’t figure out a way to escape from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:28.800 --> 00:45:34.800
its isolated area? It is so highly contagious,&nbsp;
and spreads so quickly, that just one tiny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:34.800 --> 00:45:41.520
infected rabbit, and one inattentive soldier,&nbsp;
could be enough for SCP-610 to reach the general&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:41.520 --> 00:45:48.180
population. If it did, its violent, destructive&nbsp;
nature and hatred for all life would mean that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:48.180 --> 00:45:55.560
everything, not just the people but animals,&nbsp;
plants, and the world itself, could be at risk.&nbsp;

00:45:55.560 --> 00:46:01.020
And no one is ready for this kind of infection. A&nbsp;
disease that turns the human body against itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:01.020 --> 00:46:07.320
turns our skin into a weapon and a tomb,&nbsp;
stripping away identity, humanity, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:07.320 --> 00:46:13.200
everything that isn’t made of that same hateful&nbsp;
flesh. So, let’s hope that the perimeter holds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:13.200 --> 00:46:19.200
and, the next time you feel a little itchy,&nbsp;
try not to think about what might happen next.

00:46:38.340 --> 00:47:08.520
ou might be able to avert this horrible fate, if&nbsp;
only you knew what exactly you were dealing with:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:08.520 --> 00:47:16.440
SCP – 4666, also known as The Yule Man. A&nbsp;
Keter-Class Christmas monster so violent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:16.440 --> 00:47:22.380
sadistic, and terrifying, he makes Krampus&nbsp;
look like jolly Saint Nick. And this year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:22.380 --> 00:47:27.720
just like every other, he’s planning&nbsp;
on being very, very naughty.&nbsp;

00:47:27.720 --> 00:47:34.200
The SCP Foundation began cataloguing the Yule&nbsp;
Man in 1974 after a string of violent and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:34.200 --> 00:47:39.660
eerily similar home invasions during the holiday&nbsp;
season, but they have reason to believe that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:39.660 --> 00:47:46.500
entity has been around for a whole lot longer.&nbsp;
Over 2000 years in fact. Stories that describe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:46.500 --> 00:47:52.320
what look to be Yule Man massacres date as far&nbsp;
back as the First Century BC in Scandinavia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:52.320 --> 00:47:57.360
and there have been reports of similar clusters&nbsp;
of events happening around the same time every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:57.360 --> 00:48:02.880
year since. This monster is prolific, and&nbsp;
may have one of the highest body counts of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:02.880 --> 00:48:08.640
any creature under observation by the Foundation.
The Yule Man’s trail of destruction became clearer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:08.640 --> 00:48:13.980
in the eighteenth century, as accounts of the&nbsp;
carnage it leaves became more detailed. Later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:13.980 --> 00:48:19.500
still, authorities even managed to find physical&nbsp;
evidence like the Yule Man’s fingerprints – which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:19.500 --> 00:48:24.540
are similar to human fingerprints, but display&nbsp;
a distinct double-whorl pattern not seen in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:24.540 --> 00:48:29.580
human fingerprints. Much about the anomalous&nbsp;
nature of the Yule Man is still unknown though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:29.580 --> 00:48:34.320
and the Foundation has yet to discover an&nbsp;
effective way to contain it. Their only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:34.320 --> 00:48:40.140
hope is intercepting it before it can get its&nbsp;
long, gnarled fingers on its intended prey.&nbsp;

00:48:40.140 --> 00:48:45.900
Maybe you’re feeling worried, or that you’re being&nbsp;
watched. You have a good reason to be afraid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:45.900 --> 00:48:51.600
because during his yearly active period – the&nbsp;
twelve days between December 21st and January&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:51.600 --> 00:48:57.720
2nd – he’s always searching for prey. Nowhere is&nbsp;
safe, because while it was initially believed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:57.720 --> 00:49:03.300
he only appeared to those who lived north of 40&nbsp;
degrees latitude, it’s now believed that much like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:03.300 --> 00:49:09.000
Santa Claus, the Yule Man operates worldwide.&nbsp;
Anyone could be in his sights right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:09.000 --> 00:49:14.520
blissfully unaware of the nightmare coming&nbsp;
down the tracks towards them. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:14.520 --> 00:49:19.860
the SCP Foundation, through analysis of these&nbsp;
attacks which are known as Weissnacht Events,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:19.860 --> 00:49:24.720
they’ve been able to find certain patterns.
But first, what does the creature known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:24.720 --> 00:49:31.440
The Yule Man even look like? Much like SCP –&nbsp;
096, the Yule Man is a long and lanky humanoid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:31.440 --> 00:49:36.720
standing about two meters tall, who resembles&nbsp;
an emaciated human of European descent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:36.720 --> 00:49:42.180
and never wears any clothes or other coverings&nbsp;
despite the frigid temperatures he operates in.&nbsp;

00:49:42.180 --> 00:49:47.040
You might be sad if you’re spending Christmas&nbsp;
alone, but it at least guarantees you safety&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:47.040 --> 00:49:51.360
from the Yule Man, as he only appears at&nbsp;
the homes of families with a child under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:51.360 --> 00:49:56.400
the age of eight present. He also seems&nbsp;
to favor isolated and rural locations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:56.400 --> 00:50:01.620
and Weissnacht Events only occur when there’s a&nbsp;
healthy covering of snow on the ground during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:01.620 --> 00:50:07.860
event – hence the name which means “White Night”&nbsp;
in English. It’s also vital that you recognize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:07.860 --> 00:50:13.620
the three distinct stages of a Weissnacht Event,&nbsp;
too, or you won’t be seeing much of the New Year.&nbsp;

00:50:13.620 --> 00:50:18.360
The first stage occurs during the space of&nbsp;
a week. Children in the home might start to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:18.360 --> 00:50:23.100
seem worried or afraid. They might tell you that&nbsp;
they see something strange in the distance. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:23.100 --> 00:50:28.080
figure of a man they don’t recognize, standing&nbsp;
just far enough away that you can’t fully make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:28.080 --> 00:50:32.520
him out, except that he’s really tall. Of&nbsp;
course, you probably won’t see anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:32.520 --> 00:50:37.500
and your instinct will be to tell them there’s&nbsp;
nothing to be afraid of. Even when they tell you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:37.500 --> 00:50:43.200
through tears, that there’s a man pressing his&nbsp;
face up against their bedroom window at night.&nbsp;

00:50:43.200 --> 00:50:47.880
But they are right to be afraid, and you&nbsp;
should be, too. Already at this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:47.880 --> 00:50:52.920
your only hope is to try and spread the word as&nbsp;
soon as possible: Report the incident to the local&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:52.920 --> 00:50:58.980
police, write about it on Facebook, tweet about&nbsp;
it. Whatever it takes. The SCP Foundation has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:58.980 --> 00:51:03.480
operatives trawling the internet and monitoring&nbsp;
police reports constantly during this period,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:03.480 --> 00:51:09.600
especially for reports of mysterious men in the&nbsp;
snow watching homes from a distance. Getting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:09.600 --> 00:51:13.920
Foundation’s attention is your best hope&nbsp;
of stopping this thing. And if you don’t?&nbsp;

00:51:13.920 --> 00:51:19.500
Next comes stage two, taking place between&nbsp;
nights eight and eleven of the active period.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:19.500 --> 00:51:25.380
No longer will the Yule Man just be lurking on&nbsp;
the periphery. Now he’s getting closer. You’ll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:25.380 --> 00:51:30.960
start to hear strange noises in your attic or on&nbsp;
the roof, noises that sound almost like footsteps.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:30.960 --> 00:51:37.980
That’s crazy, you think, it’s probably just an&nbsp;
animal. But then, the smell starts. An awful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:37.980 --> 00:51:44.460
rotten stench that fills the house, but no matter&nbsp;
how hard you look, you can’t find the source.&nbsp;

00:51:44.460 --> 00:51:48.720
Finally, on the last night of December, you&nbsp;
tell yourself that you’ll take this matter to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:48.720 --> 00:51:54.720
the police. But of course, it’s already too&nbsp;
late. The Yule Man is here for the twelfth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:54.720 --> 00:52:01.020
night. The Weissnacht is finally upon you.
At this point, one of two scenarios will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:01.020 --> 00:52:05.220
happen. In the first, you and your entire&nbsp;
family will be tortured and murdered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:05.220 --> 00:52:11.340
except the youngest child, who the Yule Man&nbsp;
will kidnap. The SCP Foundation keeps files&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:11.340 --> 00:52:16.800
on a number of notable instances of this kind of&nbsp;
Weissnacht, and the details are truly gruesome.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:16.800 --> 00:52:22.260
Reports of incidents have involved crucifixion,&nbsp;
the removal of tongues, burning, dismemberment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:22.260 --> 00:52:28.080
post mortem bitemarks, and decapitation.
In all instances though, the entire family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:28.080 --> 00:52:34.200
was killed except the youngest child, who simply&nbsp;
disappeared. The Yule Man is a merciless and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:34.200 --> 00:52:39.120
sadistic beast. You’re now probably wondering: If&nbsp;
that’s the first of two Weissnacht possibilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:39.120 --> 00:52:44.700
what’s the second? In the second, if you’re&nbsp;
tremendously lucky, you and your family will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:44.700 --> 00:52:51.060
survive – but that doesn’t mean you won’t face a&nbsp;
grisly experience. In this scenario, which occurs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:51.060 --> 00:52:55.320
during about fifteen percent of Weissnacht Events,&nbsp;
you’ll hear footsteps throughout the night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:55.320 --> 00:53:01.200
but thankfully, you wake up alive. And when&nbsp;
you do so, there are gifts waiting for you.&nbsp;

00:53:01.200 --> 00:53:08.520
The problem is, all these gifts are made out of&nbsp;
human body parts. For example, in 1976 in Canada,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:08.520 --> 00:53:14.160
one family received the gift of a ball made&nbsp;
from a severed human head wrapped in skin. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:14.160 --> 00:53:20.700
Kazakhstan in 1903, a family received a flute&nbsp;
made from a hollowed out human femur. And in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:20.700 --> 00:53:27.420
Netherlands in 2003, a family received a wooden&nbsp;
hairbrush, covered in human teeth ranging from 400&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:27.420 --> 00:53:36.360
years old to a mere few days. These gruesome gifts&nbsp;
are referred to as SCP – 4666 – A, and it was one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:36.360 --> 00:53:41.820
of these gifts that gave us the best insight yet&nbsp;
available into the true nature of the Yule Man.&nbsp;

00:53:41.820 --> 00:53:46.620
Several gifts were dropped off at a family's&nbsp;
residence in Hoonah, Alaska, in 2018,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:46.620 --> 00:53:56.940
but most notable among them was the horrific&nbsp;
SCP-4666-A-0960 – a life-sized doll made from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:56.940 --> 00:54:04.200
a human body, with its eyes removed and mouth sewn&nbsp;
shut. Worst of all though, was that the girl was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:04.200 --> 00:54:09.480
still alive. The family who received this twisted&nbsp;
gift was given amnestics by the Foundation, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:09.480 --> 00:54:14.460
the living doll was taken for medical treatment.&nbsp;
Before succumbing to her extensive injuries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:14.460 --> 00:54:19.500
the girl was able to deliver some insights&nbsp;
into what exactly happened to the children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:19.500 --> 00:54:24.420
who were abducted during Weissnacht Events.
The children taken by the Yule Man are forced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:24.420 --> 00:54:29.700
into a large sack that seems much bigger on the&nbsp;
inside than it appears as he makes his rounds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:29.700 --> 00:54:35.400
travelling from house to house, murdering&nbsp;
and kidnapping. His victims are taken to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:35.400 --> 00:54:41.160
kind of underground grotto and workshop filled&nbsp;
with bones, like a twisted Santa’s workshop,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:41.160 --> 00:54:46.500
where they’re forced to make toys out of the&nbsp;
bodies of their fellow victims. During this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:46.500 --> 00:54:52.740
the Yule Man will continue to torture and torment&nbsp;
his victims. He’ll even take some of them away to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:52.740 --> 00:54:57.540
cook and eat whenever he feels like it.
When asked how she was turned into this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:57.540 --> 00:55:02.760
human doll, the girl told Foundation personnel&nbsp;
that her fellow victims were forced to turn her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:02.760 --> 00:55:08.340
into this by the Yule Man when she became&nbsp;
too weak to continue making toys herself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:08.340 --> 00:55:14.340
Her chilling last words were, “When you&nbsp;
can’t make the toys, you become the toys.”&nbsp;

00:55:15.000 --> 00:55:20.460
So if strange things happen to you and your&nbsp;
family between the 21st of December and the 1st&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:20.460 --> 00:55:27.180
of January, don’t ignore it. After all, you never&nbsp;
know who’s watching. But if it is the Yule Man’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:27.180 --> 00:55:33.840
grinning face pressed up against your window,&nbsp;
it may already be too late. Happy Holidays…

00:55:33.840 --> 00:55:39.720
There is a dangerous creature that could be&nbsp;
anywhere in the world, hiding in plain sight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:39.720 --> 00:55:44.880
casually walking through crowded streets&nbsp;
filled with people. A monster that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:44.880 --> 00:55:50.880
nearly impossible to see, blending into its&nbsp;
surroundings almost perfectly. Not invisible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:50.880 --> 00:55:58.560
but unnoticeable, almost completely undetectable.
But then, you spot a familiar outfit in a crowd.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:58.560 --> 00:56:06.000
You now know where the creature is. But it goes&nbsp;
both ways, since the moment you find it, it knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:06.000 --> 00:56:11.400
where you are. There is now not a single place on&nbsp;
the Earth that you could hide where it wouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:11.400 --> 00:56:18.480
find you. And it won’t ever stop looking. To the&nbsp;
staff at the Foundation this creature is known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:18.480 --> 00:56:26.520
SCP-4885. But you and I know him by a different&nbsp;
name. You may have seen his face hundreds of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:26.520 --> 00:56:34.080
times, or stared for hours at a page trying&nbsp;
to catch a glimpse of him. To us, he’s Waldo.&nbsp;

00:56:34.080 --> 00:56:39.780
While this might feel like a very long-winded&nbsp;
and silly joke, maybe even a prank that has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:39.780 --> 00:56:45.540
been inserted into the SCP archives, it&nbsp;
is anything but. If you grew up any time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:45.540 --> 00:56:50.880
after the elate 1980s, then you will likely&nbsp;
be familiar with the Where’s Waldo? books,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:50.880 --> 00:56:56.400
but for the uninitiated, these are a series&nbsp;
of puzzle books created by illustrator Martin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:56:56.400 --> 00:57:02.220
Handford. Each book in the Where’s Waldo? line&nbsp;
contains multiple double-page spreads of colorful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:02.220 --> 00:57:08.520
crowded scenes. The goal is for readers to&nbsp;
spot the ever-elusive titular character, Waldo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:08.520 --> 00:57:14.940
who is hidden among the mass of other characters.
Waldo himself is easily recognized, thanks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:14.940 --> 00:57:20.400
a design that has become truly iconic over the&nbsp;
years. He is always depicted as wearing a red and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:20.400 --> 00:57:26.940
while striped shirt, with a bobble hat in matching&nbsp;
colors. Waldo also sports jeans, circular rimmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:26.940 --> 00:57:32.640
glasses, and sometimes a wooden walking stick.
So, with that important context out of the way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:32.640 --> 00:57:39.840
up front, what exactly is SCP-4885? Is it the&nbsp;
character from these children’s books somehow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:39.840 --> 00:57:44.820
brought to life? Has the character of Waldo&nbsp;
always been a malicious, malevolent entity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:44.820 --> 00:57:52.860
too powerful to be contained within his own books?&nbsp;
Well, not exactly. SCP-4885 only seems to resemble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:52.860 --> 00:57:58.260
the famous children’s book character. Whether or&nbsp;
not he is a living manifestation of Waldo in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:58.260 --> 00:58:05.820
real world is both unclear and up for debate.
Examining its outward appearance, SCP-4885 does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:05.820 --> 00:58:10.380
share the humanoid shape and looks to be&nbsp;
wearing the same recognizable clothing of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:10.380 --> 00:58:16.140
Waldo. There are, however, two notable bodily&nbsp;
dissimilarities between the Waldo on the page,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:16.140 --> 00:58:23.280
and the physical form of SCP-4885. For one, this&nbsp;
Waldo appears to be much paler to the one found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:23.280 --> 00:58:28.620
in the book series. More noticeably however, is&nbsp;
the fact that, despite wearing the same circular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:28.620 --> 00:58:37.740
glasses, SCP-4885 seems to have no eyes.
Should a person learn of SCP-4885’s current&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:37.740 --> 00:58:43.920
location, Waldo will simultaneously gain an&nbsp;
awareness of this person. Learning instantly of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:43.920 --> 00:58:50.880
their victim’s location, SCP-4885 will traverse&nbsp;
any space necessary, tracking their target down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:50.880 --> 00:58:55.980
to anywhere they might be in the world. The&nbsp;
creature has displayed a number of space altering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:55.980 --> 00:59:02.640
abilities, including teleportation. SCP-4885&nbsp;
can also alter the state of his own matter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:02.640 --> 00:59:10.140
allowing Waldo to phase through solid surfaces.&nbsp;
No obstacle can stop his advance: not walls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:10.140 --> 00:59:18.120
not buildings, not even his victim’s own body.
When SCP-4885 finally reaches the person who has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:18.120 --> 00:59:24.000
learned of his location, Waldo will then proceed&nbsp;
to murder them in an exceptionally excruciating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:24.000 --> 00:59:30.240
manner. Using his matter changing abilities, he&nbsp;
will teleport or phase himself inside his victim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:30.780 --> 00:59:36.420
pulling himself through their body and destroying&nbsp;
their internal organs. After causing catastrophic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:36.420 --> 00:59:42.840
bodily damage, SCP-4885 will then wrench&nbsp;
their victim’s jaw open, unhinging it with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:42.840 --> 00:59:48.900
enough force to climb his way out of their mouth,&nbsp;
leaving them dead, their body completely mangled.&nbsp;

00:59:48.900 --> 00:59:54.480
However, this isn’t even the final stage of&nbsp;
Waldo’s attack. There is a strange by-product&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:54.480 --> 01:00:01.380
left after a fatal encounter with SCP-4885, a&nbsp;
yellow liquid that is produced as Waldo exits&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:01.380 --> 01:00:06.240
his victim’s body. When this substance comes&nbsp;
into contact with the deceased person’s skin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:06.240 --> 01:00:12.120
it triggers a bizarre change. The liquid will&nbsp;
cause their bodies to change after death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:12.120 --> 01:00:17.880
their skin becoming covered in symbols.&nbsp;
On closer inspection is becomes clear that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:17.880 --> 01:00:24.360
these symbols are illustrations, exactly like&nbsp;
the ones found in the pages of Where’s Waldo?&nbsp;

01:00:24.360 --> 01:00:31.620
These corpses, referred to by the Foundation&nbsp;
as instances of SCP-4855-1, will then start&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:31.620 --> 01:00:38.100
to act in a similar manner to SCP-4885, and&nbsp;
anyone who sees one or learns of its location&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:38.100 --> 01:00:43.620
will cause Waldo to come looking for them.
The Where’s Waldo? scenes left on a deceased&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:43.620 --> 01:00:48.900
victim’s skin cannot be washed off or otherwise&nbsp;
removed and the only way to undo an instance&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:48.900 --> 01:00:56.640
of SCP-4885-1 is to skin an infected body after&nbsp;
death. However, this creates a whole new problem.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:56.640 --> 01:01:02.640
If someone was to attempt this, in doing so they&nbsp;
would know the location of one of Waldo’s victims.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:02.640 --> 01:01:07.620
This knowledge would mean that whomever was trying&nbsp;
to skin one of these bodies would themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:07.620 --> 01:01:15.600
become Waldo’s next target and would likely end&nbsp;
up just another instance of SCP-4885-1. In other&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:15.600 --> 01:01:21.660
words, it would be an exercise in futility.
Naturally, the nature of his abilities and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:21.660 --> 01:01:27.660
attack patterns makes it difficult for the&nbsp;
SCP Foundation to contain Waldo. SCP-4885&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:27.660 --> 01:01:32.580
cannot be harmed through the use of firearms,&nbsp;
or other common, conventional weapons at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:32.580 --> 01:01:37.800
Foundation’s disposal. You might be forgiven for&nbsp;
thinking that making a handful of people aware&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:37.800 --> 01:01:43.620
of where to find Waldo at the same time would&nbsp;
be a viable solution. After all, he cannot be&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:43.620 --> 01:01:49.380
in multiple places at once, so perhaps he’d be&nbsp;
unable to kill these individuals simultaneously.&nbsp;

01:01:49.380 --> 01:01:55.320
However, SCP-4885 has shown to be able&nbsp;
to cope with this approach, dispatching&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:55.320 --> 01:02:01.440
his victims one at a time, transforming each&nbsp;
in turn into Where’s Waldo? printed corpses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:01.440 --> 01:02:07.740
before continuing to the next would-be victim.
If the victim is nearby, Waldo will force&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:07.740 --> 01:02:12.720
himself into their mouth, passing through&nbsp;
their body and destroying bones, organs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:12.720 --> 01:02:18.120
and even the spinal column. When his victim&nbsp;
is further away, Waldo will phase through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:18.120 --> 01:02:23.220
nearest wall and attack them, teleporting into&nbsp;
his target and then climbing out of their mouth.

01:02:23.220 --> 01:02:29.340
Waldo’s location, or that of his victims’ bodies,&nbsp;
are considered ‘infohazards’. Simply being aware&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:29.340 --> 01:02:35.940
of this information will cause SCP-4885 to&nbsp;
activate. As a result of this, the staff at&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:35.940 --> 01:02:43.440
the SCP Foundation are not even sure that Waldo is&nbsp;
actually contained at all. In theory, SCP-4885 is&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:43.440 --> 01:02:48.180
being held at an undisclosed Foundation site&nbsp;
within a non-designated containment chamber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:48.180 --> 01:02:54.420
since even a number on the door would tip off&nbsp;
what’s inside, triggering Waldo’s abilities. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:54.420 --> 01:02:59.880
here’s the clincher; because nobody can know for&nbsp;
sure where Waldo is without him coming for them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:59.880 --> 01:03:05.520
nobody at the Foundation actually knows&nbsp;
where he’s being contained, if he’s even&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:05.520 --> 01:03:10.260
contained at all! It is worth noting&nbsp;
that, if someone receives a vague,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:10.260 --> 01:03:15.420
non-specific description of Waldo’s whereabouts,&nbsp;
then he will make no attempt to seek them out.

01:03:15.420 --> 01:03:21.900
If he is contained, and if he was to ever breach&nbsp;
containment, then the SCP Foundation has an entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:21.900 --> 01:03:27.900
set of procedures in place to ensure that no one&nbsp;
ever finds Waldo. First, 36 containment chambers&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:27.900 --> 01:03:33.360
identical to the one SCP-4885 is supposedly&nbsp;
held in are connected to a self-driving&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:33.360 --> 01:03:38.280
vehicle. An expendable D-Class personnel member&nbsp;
is placed into the vehicle and a random number&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:38.280 --> 01:03:44.220
generator will select a number from one to 36.
The self-driving vehicle will then arrive at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:44.220 --> 01:03:49.740
containment chamber chosen at random, and the&nbsp;
D-Class placed inside. Within each chamber are&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:49.740 --> 01:03:54.720
digital monitors, and once the D-Class is inside&nbsp;
a chamber, all of these monitors will display&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:54.720 --> 01:04:02.460
the current location of SCP-4885. The Foundation&nbsp;
has a GPS tracking device implanted within Waldo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:02.460 --> 01:04:06.660
but this information is normally kept&nbsp;
secret to avoid any containment breaches.&nbsp;

01:04:06.660 --> 01:04:13.020
The D-Class essentially acts as bait for Waldo,&nbsp;
forcibly given the knowledge of his location so&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:13.020 --> 01:04:19.140
that SCP-4885 will consider them a target.&nbsp;
As part of the next phase of containment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:19.140 --> 01:04:24.360
Foundation staff will wait, giving Waldo enough&nbsp;
time to arrive in the containment chamber and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:24.360 --> 01:04:29.940
dispatch the D-Class within. After this, all&nbsp;
of the 36 containment chambers are transported&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:29.940 --> 01:04:37.260
to random Foundation sites in disguised trucks,&nbsp;
so that no one is sure where SCP-4885 ends up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:37.260 --> 01:04:44.100
Every time SCP-4885 breaches containment,&nbsp;
the entire procedure has to be repeated.&nbsp;

01:04:44.100 --> 01:04:50.700
The Foundation first encountered SCP-4885 a&nbsp;
number of years ago, inside a small wooden house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:50.700 --> 01:04:56.220
the exact location of which has since been&nbsp;
expunged from all the SCP Foundation’s records.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:56.220 --> 01:05:00.540
While on an assignment to secure an entirely&nbsp;
different anomaly, the Foundation’s Mobile&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:00.540 --> 01:05:06.660
Task Force Chi-19, also code named ‘Unrelenting&nbsp;
Punishment’, were the first to discover Waldo.&nbsp;

01:05:06.660 --> 01:05:10.800
The three person unit consisted of&nbsp;
Foundation operatives named Amelia Merrick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:10.800 --> 01:05:15.840
James Klein and Kurt Stoll. The trio cautiously&nbsp;
entered the wooden house where they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:15.840 --> 01:05:21.180
meant to investigate reports of an anomalous,&nbsp;
inanimate object: a pair of black spectacles.&nbsp;

01:05:21.180 --> 01:05:26.520
According to initial intelligence gathered by&nbsp;
the SCP Foundation, these glasses were capable&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:26.520 --> 01:05:32.040
of killing anyone that tried to wear them, leaving&nbsp;
their body covered in pictures like those found in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:32.040 --> 01:05:36.780
a children’s book. Sounds familiar, doesn’t&nbsp;
it? It is unknown if these black spectacles&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:36.780 --> 01:05:42.720
are the same eyewear worn by SCP-4885, but&nbsp;
it doesn’t seem like too far of a leap to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:42.720 --> 01:05:48.180
assume that this may well have been the case.
Searching the ground floor, the team found no&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:48.180 --> 01:05:53.400
sign of the object had been sent to recover. As&nbsp;
Amelia, Kurt, and James made their way upstairs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:53.400 --> 01:05:59.820
something began making scraping sounds beneath&nbsp;
them, but none of them noticed. In an abandoned&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:59.820 --> 01:06:05.160
bedroom on the upstairs floor of the house, Kurt&nbsp;
spotted a drawing on the wall, which looked to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:05.160 --> 01:06:10.260
have been made using crayons. He took a photo&nbsp;
of the illustration, and this image is still&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:10.260 --> 01:06:16.440
kept in the Foundation’s database. It appears&nbsp;
to be a child’s drawing, depicting SCP-4885,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:16.440 --> 01:06:23.100
wearing his signature striped shirt and hat,&nbsp;
with empty, vacant eyes. Next to it was scrawled&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:23.100 --> 01:06:29.580
one simple phrase: “Waldo found mommy.”
Continuing their way through the house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:29.580 --> 01:06:34.260
the team located the glasses they were&nbsp;
looking for in an upstairs bathroom. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:34.260 --> 01:06:39.360
as James bagged up the spectacles, ready for&nbsp;
transport back to the Foundation, Kurt spotted&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:39.360 --> 01:06:44.640
another inscription on a nearby wall, one that the&nbsp;
team were certain hadn’t been there when they had&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:44.640 --> 01:06:49.800
arrived. James stepped in to translate it using&nbsp;
a Foundation standard issue translation device.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:49.800 --> 01:06:55.740
The phrase on the wall read “The basement. The&nbsp;
corpses from a child’s book are in the basement.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:55.740 --> 01:07:01.500
He is there too. Fr-.” And we’re sure that you&nbsp;
can already guess what happened after that.&nbsp;

01:07:01.500 --> 01:07:06.480
Immediately after reading these words, James&nbsp;
began to groan and clutched at his stomach,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:06.480 --> 01:07:12.060
showing signs of extreme pain. Before Amelia&nbsp;
or Kurt had any chance to figure out what was&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:12.060 --> 01:07:17.280
happening to their squadmate, fingers began&nbsp;
protruding from James’ mouth. They gripped&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:17.280 --> 01:07:22.080
his jaw and pulled it apart with enough force&nbsp;
to send his jawbone flying across the room.&nbsp;

01:07:22.080 --> 01:07:29.100
SCP-4885 climbed its way out of James’ body,&nbsp;
and Amelia and Kurt both opened fire on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:29.100 --> 01:07:34.680
creature. Waldo did not react, seemingly&nbsp;
unphased by the gunfire and sustaining no&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:34.680 --> 01:07:40.800
damage as he approached Amelia, who would be his&nbsp;
next victim. Showing his fingers into her throat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:40.800 --> 01:07:47.100
Waldo wrenched apart Amelia’s jaw, breaking it&nbsp;
before he clawed his way into her mouth. As he&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:47.100 --> 01:07:53.700
watched in horror, Kurt made a panicked call for&nbsp;
help to the Foundation, but it was too late. Waldo&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:53.700 --> 01:08:00.540
had already dispatched both James and Amelia, and&nbsp;
now Kurt was about to pay the same terrible price.&nbsp;

01:08:00.540 --> 01:08:04.620
Ever since this incident, the&nbsp;
Foundation believes that they have&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:04.620 --> 01:08:11.040
SCP-4885 contained. When his file was created,&nbsp;
their researchers created an automated algorithm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:11.040 --> 01:08:16.620
designed to wipe away any mention of&nbsp;
SCP-4885’s current location or the house&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:16.620 --> 01:08:22.980
he was discovered in from Foundation records.
With SCP-4885 now assumed to be contained,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:22.980 --> 01:08:28.500
that only leaves one question, the same&nbsp;
burning inquiry that’s been plaguing&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:28.500 --> 01:08:36.600
man for decades… Where’s Waldo? In this&nbsp;
case, maybe it’s safer if you don't know.

01:08:36.600 --> 01:08:41.760
You’re a pizza delivery person for a company&nbsp;
we’re not at liberty to name. It may seem&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:41.760 --> 01:08:46.020
like a thankless job, but you’re part of&nbsp;
the thin crust between satisfaction and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:46.020 --> 01:08:50.400
starvation for people who really don’t feel&nbsp;
like cooking or going out tonight. You’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:50.400 --> 01:08:54.960
a tried and true pizza veteran. You’ve&nbsp;
seen a lot on the job - from people who&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:54.960 --> 01:08:59.520
tried to rob you on their own doorsteps, to&nbsp;
one guy who tried to tip you with a clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:59.520 --> 01:09:05.580
fake Rolex - but you haven’t seen anything like&nbsp;
the insanity you’re about to encounter tonight.

01:09:05.580 --> 01:09:12.360
That’s because you’re about to get sick. Really,&nbsp;
really sick. And we know there’s probably a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:12.360 --> 01:09:20.280
diseases you’d rather not catch, but trust&nbsp;
us, no disease bites quite like SCP-3760.

01:09:20.280 --> 01:09:25.380
But back to you. You’re parked on the saddle&nbsp;
of your prized bicycle, pedaling for your life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:25.380 --> 01:09:30.060
the biggest order you’ve ever delivered&nbsp;
strapped to the cargo rack behind you - eight&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:30.060 --> 01:09:34.860
large meat-feast pizzas. You figure you’re&nbsp;
heading towards the most hopping, or at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:34.860 --> 01:09:39.600
the hungriest party in the city, and despite&nbsp;
the frustration of needing to ferry this hot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:39.600 --> 01:09:44.640
cheesy nightmare to its destination, parties&nbsp;
have historically been pretty good tippers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:44.640 --> 01:09:49.740
Little do you know, your prized customer is&nbsp;
about to give you much more than just a tip.

01:09:49.740 --> 01:09:54.540
You pull up outside their ground level apartment&nbsp;
and park your bike. There’s no music coming from&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:54.540 --> 01:09:59.640
the apartment you’re heading to. Strange. You&nbsp;
pick up your precious cargo and trudge towards&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:59.640 --> 01:10:05.220
the door, barely managing to ring the bell with&nbsp;
your spare pinky. The door swings open instantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:05.220 --> 01:10:10.440
as though the occupant was just standing&nbsp;
behind it the whole time, waiting for you.

01:10:10.440 --> 01:10:14.460
When the door opens, you’re not sure&nbsp;
what to make of what you see inside.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:14.460 --> 01:10:19.560
There isn’t a party. There doesn’t even&nbsp;
seem to be a group. Just one person,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:19.560 --> 01:10:26.100
standing there and staring at you, and&nbsp;
something about this person is just...wrong.

01:10:26.100 --> 01:10:32.760
His skin seems to be an oddly unnatural color.&nbsp;
It has a slightly gray hue, like it’s rotting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:32.760 --> 01:10:37.260
and you see that the stranger’s shirt&nbsp;
is torn in several places. You’re trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:37.260 --> 01:10:40.800
your best to remain professional and not&nbsp;
stare, but you can’t help but notice that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:40.800 --> 01:10:45.060
whatever is under these tears doesn’t&nbsp;
look like skin. It’s almost like there&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:45.060 --> 01:10:52.080
are holes all over his body underneath the&nbsp;
shirt - big, gaping holes. And are those…

01:10:52.080 --> 01:10:56.340
You’re cut off when he takes the pile of&nbsp;
pizzas from you, and shoves what was once&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:56.340 --> 01:11:00.600
a handful of dollars into your palm.&nbsp;
They seem torn up, and worst of all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:00.600 --> 01:11:05.940
wet. You look past your strange customer, and&nbsp;
see that his apartment looks just as shoddy as&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:05.940 --> 01:11:11.640
he does. There’s stuffing torn from the couch.&nbsp;
Huge tears in the curtains. What you could swear&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:11.640 --> 01:11:16.920
are scratch or bite marks on some of the wooden&nbsp;
furniture. This man clearly needed his pizza.

01:11:16.920 --> 01:11:23.100
As you begin to step away, happy to just be rid&nbsp;
of this freaky situation, you do something that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:23.100 --> 01:11:28.920
you’ll live to regret. Just for a moment, you&nbsp;
lock eyes with the customer. There’s something&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:28.920 --> 01:11:34.860
about them that makes you feel sick. They’re wet&nbsp;
and black - more like a doll’s eyes than anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:34.860 --> 01:11:40.800
that should belong to a human. Just that one&nbsp;
instant of contact is enough to chill your bones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:40.800 --> 01:11:47.160
and according to some theories around SCP-3760,&nbsp;
it may have been the moment of your infection.

01:11:47.160 --> 01:11:51.000
As the stranger closes the door&nbsp;
in your face, presumably to eat&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:51.000 --> 01:11:55.920
his obscene number of pizzas, you stumble&nbsp;
back to your bicycle, letting your torn up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:55.920 --> 01:12:00.780
gooey tip blow away in the wind. Getting&nbsp;
out of this place is rewarding enough. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:00.780 --> 01:12:05.940
you can’t chase the thoughts of the stranger&nbsp;
out of your mind. Was he sick? Was he even&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:05.940 --> 01:12:10.620
human? These are the thoughts swimming through&nbsp;
your head as you cycle back to the restaurant.

01:12:10.620 --> 01:12:16.320
You’re so preoccupied, you don’t even notice the&nbsp;
truck speeding towards you. You get sideswiped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:16.320 --> 01:12:21.000
destroying your bike and throwing you through the&nbsp;
air. You can feel the snap of your arm breaking as&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:21.000 --> 01:12:26.760
you land. It’s a horrible feeling to go along&nbsp;
with the horrible noise. And as you fade from&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:26.760 --> 01:12:31.680
consciousness, the last thought in your mind&nbsp;
is the black, soulless eyes of the customer.

01:12:31.680 --> 01:12:36.360
When you wake up, you find that you’re in&nbsp;
a hospital bed with your arm in a cast. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:36.360 --> 01:12:41.280
doctors tell you that you’re phenomenally lucky&nbsp;
to be alive given the severity of the crash. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:41.280 --> 01:12:46.020
doctor says that you’re dealing with a compound&nbsp;
fracture in your right arm, as well as some nasty&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:46.020 --> 01:12:51.360
cuts that required stitches, but otherwise&nbsp;
you’re fine. The hospital insists that you&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:51.360 --> 01:12:57.600
at least stay the night though, and you oblige,&nbsp;
but that night you find it’s difficult to sleep.

01:12:57.600 --> 01:13:02.400
Partly because of the pain, but mostly&nbsp;
because of an extremely strange sound&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:02.400 --> 01:13:06.720
coming from inside the cast around&nbsp;
your arm. It’s a scraping noise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:06.720 --> 01:13:11.700
like something sharp scratching at the&nbsp;
interior. You figure it must just be some&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:11.700 --> 01:13:16.260
strange side effect of the pain meds - you’re&nbsp;
not going to let worry eat you up inside.

01:13:16.260 --> 01:13:20.040
Something else will be doing that soon enough.

01:13:20.040 --> 01:13:24.060
You’re discharged from the hospital the&nbsp;
next day and told that you should be fine&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:24.060 --> 01:13:28.860
in a couple months, as though that’s some&nbsp;
kind of consolation. You try to carry on&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:28.860 --> 01:13:32.460
with your daily life, as much as you&nbsp;
can with one arm out of commission,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:32.460 --> 01:13:37.560
but that awful crunching noise from inside&nbsp;
your cast persists. You even start to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:37.560 --> 01:13:44.460
become paranoid that some sort of insect is&nbsp;
trapped inside, or worse, a swarm of insects.

01:13:44.460 --> 01:13:49.560
But you aren’t left with that uncertainty for&nbsp;
long. By the next morning, your cast has fallen&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:49.560 --> 01:13:55.680
off. Well, not “fallen”, per se. A more accurate&nbsp;
description would be that it was chewed off from&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:55.680 --> 01:14:01.320
the inside. And not by something trapped in&nbsp;
there with your arm, but by your arm itself.

01:14:01.320 --> 01:14:04.500
When you finally see it, it doesn’t&nbsp;
even look like an arm anymore:&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:04.500 --> 01:14:09.660
The flesh has turned gray. That same&nbsp;
sickly gray of the customer’s skin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:09.660 --> 01:14:14.580
the night of your accident. But worse still:&nbsp;
From the top of the hand down to the base&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:14.580 --> 01:14:20.280
of the forearm, your entire arm is split&nbsp;
open into a fang-lined, chattering mouth.

01:14:20.280 --> 01:14:24.720
When you’ve gotten over the initial horror of&nbsp;
seeing the mutations that have taken hold of your&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:24.720 --> 01:14:29.640
arm, you notice something about the teeth in the&nbsp;
second mouth: They’re nothing like human teeth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:29.640 --> 01:14:35.700
they’re vicious, jagged triangles, each&nbsp;
one like a dagger. These are unmistakably&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:35.700 --> 01:14:41.040
shark’s teeth. You give yourself the luxury of&nbsp;
having a good scream - After all, what else are&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:41.040 --> 01:14:45.900
you supposed to do after you find your arm has&nbsp;
turned into some kind of fleshy shark mutant.

01:14:45.900 --> 01:14:50.820
You notice that you can hardly even feel the&nbsp;
snapping of its jaws, like it isn’t even really&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:50.820 --> 01:14:55.620
a part of you. And as much as you try to tense&nbsp;
and release what used to be the tendons in your&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:55.620 --> 01:15:03.120
forearm, there is no change. For all intents and&nbsp;
purposes, that limb is no longer yours, it just&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:03.120 --> 01:15:09.840
happens to be attached to you. Not only that, but&nbsp;
it’s always very, very hungry, as quickly became&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:09.840 --> 01:15:15.240
evident from the fact it made such short work of&nbsp;
the cast that’d been containing it not long ago.

01:15:15.240 --> 01:15:20.760
You can see that the graying flesh is beginning&nbsp;
to spread from your forearm to your bicep. It’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:20.760 --> 01:15:25.260
almost like, little by little, your&nbsp;
tissue is being switched. Somehow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:25.260 --> 01:15:30.000
you’re innately aware that if you don’t&nbsp;
feed your arm, it’ll get even worse.

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:34.680
Suddenly, everything about the strange customer&nbsp;
from the night of the accident makes sense:&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:34.680 --> 01:15:40.140
He had whatever you have now, only worse.&nbsp;
He was just hoping that the pizzas would&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:40.140 --> 01:15:44.820
keep the beast at bay, and you very much hope&nbsp;
the contents of your fridge will do the same.

01:15:44.820 --> 01:15:49.800
Wasting no time, you grab some processed&nbsp;
ham and raw chicken - you’re not an idiot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:49.800 --> 01:15:54.000
you know that if this thing is anything like&nbsp;
a real shark, it’s only going to be interested&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:54.000 --> 01:15:59.040
in meat. But when you shove the processed meat&nbsp;
into the nibbling maw in your forearm, you notice&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:59.040 --> 01:16:04.920
that it seems to spit the food out. Something&nbsp;
tells you that your offering was too… dead.

01:16:04.920 --> 01:16:10.800
Now, you’re really afraid. Will this thing want&nbsp;
live prey? Will that be the only way to stop it&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:10.800 --> 01:16:16.440
from taking the rest of your arm, or even more?&nbsp;
The thought terrifies you. It’s like being Venom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:16.440 --> 01:16:21.840
except you don’t even get a new alien friend or&nbsp;
any cool superpowers for your trouble. But you’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:21.840 --> 01:16:26.580
smart; you’re resourceful. You don’t intend to let&nbsp;
this thing take over your life without a fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:26.580 --> 01:16:31.320
and you’ve always believed what GI Joe&nbsp;
taught you: Knowing is half the battle.

01:16:31.320 --> 01:16:35.640
Sadly, doing an internet search for “My&nbsp;
injury is somehow mutating into a shark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:35.640 --> 01:16:39.720
how do I stop this” didn’t do much good.&nbsp;
And you don't want to go to a doctor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:39.720 --> 01:16:44.100
because part of you expects to be immediately&nbsp;
shipped off to the nearest circus or military&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:44.100 --> 01:16:49.080
research lab. Instead, you throw on a thick&nbsp;
leather jacket that you hope your new shark-arm&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:49.080 --> 01:16:54.480
will take a while to eat through, and head to&nbsp;
the library of the nearest medical college. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:54.480 --> 01:16:59.400
anywhere has sources on the most obscure of&nbsp;
medical problems, this would be the place.

01:16:59.400 --> 01:17:05.160
And after hours of searching through index&nbsp;
cards, you find it - what seems to be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:05.160 --> 01:17:10.500
one and only source on this ludicrous topic in&nbsp;
the thousands and thousands of books: A series&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:10.500 --> 01:17:15.900
of journal entries made by Dr. Keith Woodward,&nbsp;
Ship's Medical Officer aboard the USS Kirby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:15.900 --> 01:17:22.200
circa 1922. Even the library’s indexing system&nbsp;
prefaces the source with a disclaimer that it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:22.200 --> 01:17:29.820
likely 25% quackery and 75% ocean madness, but&nbsp;
that doesn’t deter you. Any port in a storm.

01:17:29.820 --> 01:17:35.820
Dr. Woodward told the horrifying tale of the USS&nbsp;
Kirby’s collapse due to a sudden and unexplainable&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:35.820 --> 01:17:40.500
contagion. It began with the infection of&nbsp;
a sailor on the ship named Willis Riggs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:40.500 --> 01:17:46.080
who’d fallen overboard and had his foot partially&nbsp;
eaten by a shark. Much like your arm, the man’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:46.080 --> 01:17:51.300
foot slowly became the ravenous, all-devouring&nbsp;
mouth of a shark itself. Little by little,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:51.300 --> 01:17:55.920
it spread to other crew members through&nbsp;
unknown means. Any injuries sustained by&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:55.920 --> 01:18:00.840
the crew didn’t heal like normal, but instead&nbsp;
became this vicious, living shark tissue.

01:18:00.840 --> 01:18:06.420
Soon, these ever-hungry new mouths led them&nbsp;
to eat each other, and then themselves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:06.420 --> 01:18:11.220
from inside out. Even after the humans they&nbsp;
once were could be considered long dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:11.220 --> 01:18:17.580
those hungry jaws kept snapping. There&nbsp;
was no cure. There was no solution.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:17.580 --> 01:18:22.200
Everyone on the boat was recorded&nbsp;
as having mysteriously died at sea.

01:18:22.200 --> 01:18:25.860
That is the curse of SCP-3760.

01:18:26.520 --> 01:18:31.380
As if on cue, you look down to see that the&nbsp;
shark mouth in your arm has chewed through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:31.380 --> 01:18:36.540
leather of your sleeve like it’s nothing.&nbsp;
It’s hungry, and nothing will satiate it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:36.540 --> 01:18:41.220
But perhaps some sacrifices need to be made&nbsp;
if you want to stop it from getting worse…

01:18:41.220 --> 01:18:45.720
Just as the thought crosses your mind, a&nbsp;
needle full of sedative is injected into&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:45.720 --> 01:18:50.400
your neck. Everything goes dark very quickly,&nbsp;
and when you wake up, you’re in a clean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:50.400 --> 01:18:55.620
clinical white room. You’re now officially&nbsp;
under containment by the SCP Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:55.620 --> 01:19:00.480
not that you’ll know that any time soon.&nbsp;
This may seem like the cavalry has arrived,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:00.480 --> 01:19:04.800
but sadly for your sake, they&nbsp;
have no interest in curing you.

01:19:04.800 --> 01:19:11.100
They’re just eager to gather more data on&nbsp;
how your condition progresses. SCP-3760&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:11.100 --> 01:19:15.600
exists as a latent infection in well&nbsp;
over half of humanity, but its horrific,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:15.600 --> 01:19:22.740
mutating effects are activated in only a relative&nbsp;
few. There have only been 2,785 recorded cases of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:22.740 --> 01:19:31.200
SCP-3760 activity observed between 1958 and 2016.&nbsp;
This is thanks to the Foundation’s secret weapon&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:31.200 --> 01:19:37.800
against the shark mutation menace - Subliminal&nbsp;
Memetic Agent Kappa/Omicron - or "SMA-K/O" - a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:37.800 --> 01:19:43.080
widely distributed memetic agent that suppresses&nbsp;
the symptoms of infection in most people. Not&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:43.080 --> 01:19:47.940
that this will provide much comfort to you,&nbsp;
as you join the almost 3,000 others who have&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:47.940 --> 01:19:54.000
been infected and you are doomed to slowly turn&nbsp;
into an abomination in your containment chamber.

01:19:54.000 --> 01:19:59.700
If it’s any consolation, you may not see the truly&nbsp;
advanced stages of the disease. The most common&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:59.700 --> 01:20:05.160
cause of death among the afflicted is being eaten&nbsp;
by their own ravenous shark mouths long before it&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:05.160 --> 01:20:10.260
changes your entire body. Actually, come to think&nbsp;
of it, that’s not much of a consolation at all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:10.260 --> 01:20:15.540
But hey, when it comes to anomalous mutations,&nbsp;
we’re sad to report that there’s rarely a happy&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:15.540 --> 01:20:21.960
ending in store for those afflicted, and&nbsp;
SCP-3760 is no exception to the rule.

01:20:21.960 --> 01:20:27.480
Why do so many of the indigenous cultures of&nbsp;
the colder regions of North America seem to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:27.480 --> 01:20:32.700
share the same legend? A legend that tells&nbsp;
of a monster that lurks in the forests,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:32.700 --> 01:20:39.060
bringing cold and death to any that meet&nbsp;
it. This creature is an omen of famine, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:39.060 --> 01:20:45.060
territorial beast that preys on human beings. Some&nbsp;
cultures describe it as an unholy abomination,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:45.060 --> 01:20:51.120
a spirit of winter and a warning against the&nbsp;
dangers of selfishness, one that is created&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:51.120 --> 01:20:57.780
whenever a person resorts to cannibalism in order&nbsp;
to survive. It will gladly devour any man, woman&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:57.780 --> 01:21:04.320
or child that wanders into its territory, holding&nbsp;
a horrifying and insatiable hunger for human&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:04.320 --> 01:21:11.640
flesh. So how did so many cultures end up with&nbsp;
the same story? Could it be because… it’s real?&nbsp;

01:21:11.640 --> 01:21:17.400
Depictions of the beast vary, but it is most&nbsp;
commonly recognized by its tall, skeletal form,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:17.400 --> 01:21:23.160
like a body exhumed from the grave, even&nbsp;
carrying the stench of death and decay with&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:23.160 --> 01:21:29.340
it. Anyone who encounters one risks being eaten&nbsp;
or transformed into a creature just like. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:29.340 --> 01:21:35.520
monster’s name means an ‘evil spirit that devours&nbsp;
mankind’ though to even say the name is taboo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:35.520 --> 01:21:40.800
as it’s believed to give power to the beast.&nbsp;
Of course, these are all just legends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:40.800 --> 01:21:45.660
right? Stories to warn against the dangers of&nbsp;
greed and selfishness, but otherwise nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:45.660 --> 01:21:50.760
to fear. There’s no proof that such a beast&nbsp;
could actually be roaming the frozen wastes?&nbsp;

01:21:50.760 --> 01:21:54.840
Many at the SCP Foundation&nbsp;
felt the same way, until they&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:54.840 --> 01:22:00.780
heard about SCP-323, the Wendigo’s Skull.
Kept under lock and key by the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:00.780 --> 01:22:06.600
with around the clock surveillance, SCP-323&nbsp;
is an anomalous object with ties to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:06.600 --> 01:22:13.920
various Wendigo legends. As the object’s moniker&nbsp;
suggests, SCP-323 is a skull; not a human skull,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:13.920 --> 01:22:19.560
mind you, it more closely resembles a cervid&nbsp;
skull. Cervids are a family of mammals that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:19.560 --> 01:22:24.660
include most varieties of deer, elk, and&nbsp;
other similar animals, and this particular&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:24.660 --> 01:22:31.080
cervid skull sports a tall pair of antlers.
SCP-323 is definitely not a fresh skull either.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:31.080 --> 01:22:36.900
It shows signs of weathering and a few scars&nbsp;
across the surface, looking as if the bone has&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:36.900 --> 01:22:42.600
been bleached and eroded through exposure to the&nbsp;
elements. The skull is also missing its lower jaw,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:42.600 --> 01:22:48.240
and has a sizable hole on the rear underside&nbsp;
that may have been carved using stone tools.&nbsp;

01:22:48.240 --> 01:22:54.840
SCP-323 is kept restrained inside an armored&nbsp;
container within a concrete containment cell, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:54.840 --> 01:22:59.640
personnel are only ever allowed near it to check&nbsp;
the restraints for signs of damage. Additionally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:22:59.640 --> 01:23:05.640
any Foundation staff that enter SCP-323’s cell&nbsp;
must be accompanied by an armed security officer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:05.640 --> 01:23:11.040
and in the event of a containment breach the&nbsp;
entire site is to be evacuated. Seems like a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:11.040 --> 01:23:16.500
lot of precautions and safety measures for an old&nbsp;
piece of bone. Surely a harmless deer skull could&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:16.500 --> 01:23:19.500
never be that dangerous, right?
Wrong.&nbsp;

01:23:19.500 --> 01:23:24.600
You might be forgiven for thinking that a&nbsp;
skull can’t possibly cause harm. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:24.600 --> 01:23:32.280
SCP-323 is just a skull, then whatever animal it&nbsp;
belonged to is dead. But this skull is far more&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:32.280 --> 01:23:38.160
than it appears to be. Through extensive testing,&nbsp;
the SCP Foundation’s researchers have learned that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:38.160 --> 01:23:47.460
the skull… isn’t dead. No, this skull is awake and&nbsp;
aware. It can see, hear and has a sense of touch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:47.460 --> 01:23:54.060
and it can and will react to various stimuli.
However, this does not necessarily mean that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:54.060 --> 01:23:59.520
SCP-323 is alive or even sentient, but&nbsp;
it definitely appears to have some level&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:23:59.520 --> 01:24:05.040
of sapience. It will target certain members of&nbsp;
personnel that get too close and has attempted&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:05.040 --> 01:24:09.720
multiple times to breach containment. It&nbsp;
also reacts violently to anyone speaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:09.720 --> 01:24:16.800
English or French near it, the only two&nbsp;
languages prohibited inside SCP-323’s cell.&nbsp;

01:24:16.800 --> 01:24:23.700
So, while the skull is not technically alive, it&nbsp;
is definitely aware. Still, why the need for so&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:23.700 --> 01:24:29.340
many protocols to keep it contained? It’s not&nbsp;
as if a skull can just walk off on its own. Of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:29.340 --> 01:24:36.780
course not, but SCP-323 can move, at least to a&nbsp;
certain degree. Often in a reactionary manner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:36.780 --> 01:24:43.680
SCP-323 will vibrate or move on its own. For&nbsp;
example, turning to watch as personnel enter its&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:43.680 --> 01:24:49.440
containment cell. In most cases, these movements&nbsp;
are tiny and insignificant. But other times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:49.440 --> 01:24:55.200
the skull lunges, launching itself at Foundation&nbsp;
personnel as it desperately tries to get free.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:24:55.200 --> 01:25:01.620
Now you know why it’s kept restrained.
So, we have an antlered cervid skull that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:01.620 --> 01:25:06.420
can move and has a low level of awareness, on&nbsp;
their own these would be more than enough to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:06.420 --> 01:25:11.700
warrant the Foundation’s interest, but the&nbsp;
anomalous properties of SCP-323 don’t stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:11.700 --> 01:25:17.700
there. The skull has an inherent ability to&nbsp;
influence the minds of those around it. Anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:17.700 --> 01:25:23.580
spending an hour within a fifteen-meter radius&nbsp;
of SCP-323 is likely to experience the effects&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:23.580 --> 01:25:29.640
of this influential power. This will often result&nbsp;
in them exhibiting uncharacteristic behaviors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:29.640 --> 01:25:35.640
thoughts, and urges, including cannibalistic&nbsp;
tendencies and outbursts of random violence.&nbsp;

01:25:35.640 --> 01:25:41.760
Almost three quarters of people that suffer the&nbsp;
influence of SCP-323 will feel an overwhelming&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:41.760 --> 01:25:47.220
compulsion to take the Wendigo’s Skull and fit&nbsp;
their heads into the chiseled hole on its rear&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:47.220 --> 01:25:52.680
underside. If someone attempting this finds that&nbsp;
their head is too big to fit inside the hollow&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:52.680 --> 01:25:57.300
skull, there have been cases of individuals&nbsp;
trying to bludgeon their heads on any hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:25:57.300 --> 01:26:02.700
surface they can find nearby in an attempt to&nbsp;
get their head down to a more manageable size.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:02.700 --> 01:26:08.700
This will continue until one of three outcomes&nbsp;
occurs: one, the person manages to fit their&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:08.700 --> 01:26:13.740
head into the skull. Two, they cause themselves&nbsp;
so much cranial damage that they are rendered&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:13.740 --> 01:26:19.260
unconscious. Or three, they end up killing&nbsp;
themselves through repeated violent head trauma.&nbsp;

01:26:19.260 --> 01:26:26.220
Of course, if a person actually manages to&nbsp;
fit their head inside SCP-323, then that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:26.220 --> 01:26:32.040
a different story entirely. In these instances,&nbsp;
the individual becomes classified as an instance&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:32.040 --> 01:26:39.360
of SCP-323-1. Within ten minutes of wearing the&nbsp;
skull, this person will suffer dramatic changes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:39.360 --> 01:26:44.700
their body. Any and all body fat will be rapidly&nbsp;
shed as their hair also begins to fall out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:44.700 --> 01:26:50.460
leaving them looking starved and almost skeletal&nbsp;
in appearance. Their distal phalanges - those&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:50.460 --> 01:26:55.560
are the bones at the tip of the fingers - will&nbsp;
elongate and rupture the skin as they become bony,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:55.560 --> 01:27:00.720
claw-like appendages. The subject will also&nbsp;
find that their teeth have grown abnormally&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:00.720 --> 01:27:06.000
long and sharp, while their limbs will blacken&nbsp;
as if they were suffering frostbite symptoms.&nbsp;

01:27:06.000 --> 01:27:12.900
Along with their external transformations,&nbsp;
SCP-323-1 will also get increased strength&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:12.900 --> 01:27:16.560
and a heightened resistance to pain.&nbsp;
They aren’t invulnerable though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:16.560 --> 01:27:22.500
and can still sustain damage and injuries.
SCP-323-1 will also have a dramatic change&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:22.500 --> 01:27:28.680
happen to their metabolism, which will occur a&nbsp;
few minutes into the physical transformation. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:28.680 --> 01:27:34.440
subject will now need an almost constant intake&nbsp;
of calories, which if they don’t receive, will&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:34.440 --> 01:27:40.440
cause them to starve almost instantly. With the&nbsp;
transformation process complete, the new instance&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:40.440 --> 01:27:49.260
of SCP-323-1 has finally become the Wendigo.&nbsp;
A terrifying monster with one goal - to feed.&nbsp;

01:27:49.260 --> 01:27:55.800
The SCP-323-1 instance will seek out any human&nbsp;
beings it can find so that it can feed upon their&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:27:55.800 --> 01:28:00.540
flesh. Those who have witnessed the 323-1&nbsp;
instance in the midst of a feeding frenzy&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:00.540 --> 01:28:05.700
have described the way it violently slaughtered&nbsp;
any person it could find, leaving only a mess&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:05.700 --> 01:28:11.400
of blood as it devoured them, their screams&nbsp;
mixed in with the sounds of bones crunching.&nbsp;

01:28:11.400 --> 01:28:16.860
In the times that the creature cannot find a human&nbsp;
to nourish its monstrous appetite, it will try to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:16.860 --> 01:28:23.040
keep itself alive anyway it can. Sometimes it will&nbsp;
slow down its movement to try and conserve energy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:23.040 --> 01:28:28.200
other times it will ration whatever food&nbsp;
is available to it, saving some of its last&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:28.200 --> 01:28:35.220
meal for a leftover snack. And on occasion, the&nbsp;
monster will engage in autocannibalism, a form of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:35.220 --> 01:28:41.280
cannibalism that involves eating parts of itself.
Humans certainly seem to be its preferred food&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:41.280 --> 01:28:45.120
source though. Even when other sources&nbsp;
of meat would be easier to acquire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:28:45.120 --> 01:28:53.040
SCP-323-1 will zero in on human beings and do&nbsp;
anything it can to make a person its next meal.&nbsp;

01:28:53.040 --> 01:29:00.240
When chasing down its prey, human or otherwise,&nbsp;
SCP-323-1 has been observed uttering phrases&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:00.240 --> 01:29:05.400
either spoken in the primary language of whoever&nbsp;
was transformed by the skull, or in the Severn&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:05.400 --> 01:29:11.700
Ojibwe, Potawatomi, and Cree languages. These are&nbsp;
all native languages of the numerous indigenous&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:11.700 --> 01:29:17.340
cultures that shared legends of the Wendigo.
Where do the phrases come from, though? Are&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:17.340 --> 01:29:22.140
they another side effect of SCP-323’s&nbsp;
influence, or do they originate from&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:22.140 --> 01:29:27.480
the skull itself? The Foundation’s researchers&nbsp;
are still trying to figure that out, and at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:27.480 --> 01:29:33.960
moment have no clues as to where they come from.
In one containment breach in 2006, during which&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:33.960 --> 01:29:39.900
an instance of SCP-323-1 was able to kill and&nbsp;
devour twelve members of Foundation personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:39.900 --> 01:29:49.860
on site surveillance recorded audio of the&nbsp;
creature speaking. “Hungry… so hungry” it rasped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:29:49.860 --> 01:30:02.880
while dragging a body behind it. “I… must eat. So&nbsp;
very hungry. Always… always hungry.” After this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:02.880 --> 01:30:08.520
the sound of a wet cracking noise was recorded,&nbsp;
possibly one of the victim’s bones being broken&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:08.520 --> 01:30:17.520
by SCP-323-1 so it could get to the marrow inside.
The 323-1 instance does at times seem to try and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:17.520 --> 01:30:22.080
resist the influence of the wendigo skull.&nbsp;
Additional recordings captured the creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:22.080 --> 01:30:32.340
saying “Must… not eat. I have to eat. So&nbsp;
hungry. So… lonely,” the creature then said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:32.340 --> 01:30:34.808
followed by noises of it eating the body. “Alone.&nbsp;
Hungry. Should… eat. Must. Must… eat them all. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:34.808 --> 01:30:56.940
must eat… to know… warmth. So cold! Must eat!”
It seems that even the wendigo has its own&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:30:56.940 --> 01:31:01.500
internal struggles, perhaps showing that&nbsp;
there is still something left of the human&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:01.500 --> 01:31:07.140
who put on the skull, and that deep down they are&nbsp;
fighting against their cannibalistic impulses.&nbsp;

01:31:07.140 --> 01:31:14.400
But where exactly did the Foundation find SCP-323?&nbsp;
And is it really the skull of an actual Wendigo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:14.400 --> 01:31:21.660
the famous creature from North American legend?
In 1997, the SCP Foundation sent a detachment&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:21.660 --> 01:31:26.820
to Bittern Lake in Saskatchewan, Canada. There&nbsp;
had been reports of a local community murdering&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:26.820 --> 01:31:32.340
individuals and leaving their bodies in the forest&nbsp;
to appease a dangerous creature residing nearby.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:32.340 --> 01:31:40.200
This creature, as it was later discovered, was&nbsp;
an instance of SCP-323-1. Someone had found the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:40.200 --> 01:31:45.600
skull and succumbed to its influence, placing&nbsp;
it on their head, and turning into a monster.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:45.600 --> 01:31:51.300
Ever since, the locals had been killing people&nbsp;
and offering up their dead bodies as sustenance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:31:51.300 --> 01:31:57.600
fearful of what would happen if they didn’t after&nbsp;
being brought up with legends of the Wendigo.&nbsp;

01:31:57.600 --> 01:32:02.820
SCP Foundation agents were able to capture the&nbsp;
beast, however it died of starvation while being&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:02.820 --> 01:32:07.140
transported back to containment. They also&nbsp;
covered up the recent deaths in the area&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:07.140 --> 01:32:12.120
by giving the local residents amnestics, and&nbsp;
creating a cover story about an unidentified&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:12.120 --> 01:32:17.940
serial killer. Prior to this, James Namagoose,&nbsp;
a local man who was involved in the murders was&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:17.940 --> 01:32:23.160
brought in for questioning. He remained oddly calm&nbsp;
when interviewed, but admitted he had helped move&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:23.160 --> 01:32:29.880
the bodies that were being offered up as food&nbsp;
for SCP-323-1, or as he called it, the Wendigo.&nbsp;

01:32:29.880 --> 01:32:35.400
According to James, a local story among the Cree&nbsp;
people told of men who had once tried to control&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:35.400 --> 01:32:40.980
a Wendigo, and perhaps even tame it through&nbsp;
offerings of food. Whether or not James and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:40.980 --> 01:32:46.500
his fellow locals had the same intention, their&nbsp;
primary concern was keeping themselves safe. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:46.500 --> 01:32:51.240
described first encountering the creature: “A&nbsp;
warped man walked out of the woods, killed our&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:51.240 --> 01:32:56.340
friends right in front of us. Sometimes it would&nbsp;
stare more than it would make to kill, try to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:32:56.340 --> 01:33:01.440
talk to you. It whispered at me, ‘pe misto’,&nbsp;
‘come and eat’. It made me cold in my bones.”&nbsp;

01:33:01.440 --> 01:33:06.120
As the interview continued, James claimed&nbsp;
he had felt like he understood this ‘warped&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:06.120 --> 01:33:09.600
man’. He described feeling like the&nbsp;
Wendigo was encouraging him to kill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:09.600 --> 01:33:14.940
that the creature would help him pass when&nbsp;
his own time came. James told the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:14.940 --> 01:33:19.560
doctor questioning him that he had heard the&nbsp;
creature in his mind, and had felt it watching&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:19.560 --> 01:33:24.480
him almost constantly. Mr Namagoose stated that&nbsp;
he’d hoped, in killing people as offerings to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:24.480 --> 01:33:30.420
the Wendigo, that his own family would be spared.
Like the other locals, James Namagoose was given&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:30.420 --> 01:33:35.640
amnestics to forget all about the creature and the&nbsp;
murders he’d played a part in committing. So far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:35.640 --> 01:33:40.440
none of the Foundation’s staff have experienced&nbsp;
any similar behavioral effects to those James&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:40.440 --> 01:33:47.520
described. Those who work closely with SCP-323&nbsp;
or have witnessed an instance of SCP-323-1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:47.520 --> 01:33:53.220
have felt the creature communicating with&nbsp;
them, or urging them to kill on its behalf.&nbsp;

01:33:53.220 --> 01:33:59.340
Ultimately, who’s to say if SCP-323 is the&nbsp;
skull of a Wendigo like those from the legends?&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:33:59.340 --> 01:34:04.440
It certainly seems like it is, but with no&nbsp;
way to tell exactly how old the skull is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:04.440 --> 01:34:09.660
perhaps it’s actually the reverse and it was&nbsp;
the Wendigo legend that spawned from instances&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:09.660 --> 01:34:15.900
of SCP-323-1 that were first encountered by&nbsp;
indigenous North American cultures hundreds of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:15.900 --> 01:34:23.280
years ago. One thing is for certain, if you ever&nbsp;
come across a skull with tall antlers, you should&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:23.280 --> 01:34:29.100
try to resist putting it on. Otherwise, you might&nbsp;
not be feeling like yourself for much longer.

01:34:29.100 --> 01:34:35.100
It was the summer of 2012 in Damascus, and for&nbsp;
the people of Syria, it certainly seemed like&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:35.100 --> 01:34:39.840
all the predictions about “The End of the&nbsp;
World” were coming true. The Syrian civil&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:39.840 --> 01:34:44.760
war was raging between multiple rebel&nbsp;
groups and the dictator Bashar Al-Assad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:44.760 --> 01:34:50.220
whose government was shelling its own people,&nbsp;
as well as using chemical weapons and brutal&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:50.220 --> 01:34:56.040
campaigns of violence across the country in hopes&nbsp;
of quelling the rebellion. Little did they know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:34:56.040 --> 01:35:01.680
amidst all this pain and bloodshed,&nbsp;
something even more dangerous was brewing.

01:35:01.680 --> 01:35:07.500
An anomalous phenomenon in the sunny plains&nbsp;
North of Damascus that may pose a threat to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:07.500 --> 01:35:16.680
all of humanity someday. A threat known to the&nbsp;
SCP Foundation as SCP-3989… The Bone Orchard.

01:35:16.680 --> 01:35:23.160
This temporal and spatial anomaly was discovered&nbsp;
a few years earlier in 2009, before the Syrian&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:23.160 --> 01:35:28.680
civil war even officially began. It’s strange&nbsp;
for a highly dangerous Keter Class anomaly&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:28.680 --> 01:35:34.500
to be discovered under such seemingly mundane&nbsp;
circumstances. The SCP Foundation first became&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:34.500 --> 01:35:40.560
aware of SCP-3989 after a small olive orchard&nbsp;
owner sold a strangely high amount of olives&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:40.560 --> 01:35:46.320
that shouldn’t have been possible when compared to&nbsp;
his reported number of Olea europaea olive trees.

01:35:46.320 --> 01:35:50.280
Field Agents were dispatched to question&nbsp;
the owner about his sudden success,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:50.280 --> 01:35:54.840
but he was resistant to questioning.&nbsp;
The Agents began a covert surveillance&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:54.840 --> 01:35:59.400
operation to figure what was actually going&nbsp;
on here, at which point they discovered a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:35:59.400 --> 01:36:04.380
considerable spatial anomaly. The Olive&nbsp;
Orchard was far bigger on the inside.

01:36:04.380 --> 01:36:09.420
The property was seized by the Foundation for&nbsp;
containment. The owner had no real knowledge&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:09.420 --> 01:36:14.100
of the spatial anomaly, it’s likely he just&nbsp;
decided not to look a gift horse in the mouth&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:14.100 --> 01:36:18.720
while making money hand over fist from the&nbsp;
extra olives he sold. The owner was given&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:18.720 --> 01:36:23.820
amnestics and a new life, as the Foundation&nbsp;
began to study this anomaly which was now&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:23.820 --> 01:36:30.780
labeled SCP-3989. To this day, no researcher&nbsp;
has been able to figure out the origin of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:30.780 --> 01:36:36.900
3989’s anomalous qualities. It was first given a&nbsp;
Euclid-class designation, and cordoned off from&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:36.900 --> 01:36:42.240
the public with a simple chain link fence while&nbsp;
Foundation investigations were underway on inside.

01:36:42.240 --> 01:36:47.760
On a map, the plot of land the olive farm&nbsp;
should only occupy about five square acres,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:47.760 --> 01:36:53.820
but this plot contains an unseen portal to a&nbsp;
pocket dimension within its 12 meter active zone&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:53.820 --> 01:36:59.280
which doesn’t follow the same spatial laws&nbsp;
that our reality does. This sub-dimension,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:36:59.280 --> 01:37:06.840
known as SCP-3989-A, is a hotbed of fascinating&nbsp;
anomalous activity. Upon the discovery of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:06.840 --> 01:37:11.820
hot zone, the Foundation established the&nbsp;
nearby Area 126 as a research center and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:11.820 --> 01:37:18.660
a makeshift containment facility for any&nbsp;
anomalous entities captured from SCP-3989-A.

01:37:18.660 --> 01:37:22.200
It seemed like the Foundation really&nbsp;
had a handle on this situation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:22.200 --> 01:37:26.220
but they were blissfully unaware&nbsp;
of the true horrors lurking within&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:26.220 --> 01:37:33.420
SCP-3989-A. But they’d soon find out…&nbsp;
in the most horrifying way possible.

01:37:33.420 --> 01:37:38.940
Dr. Farik Ghazalie was assigned to head the&nbsp;
research into the anomalous zone within 3989,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:38.940 --> 01:37:44.220
and naturally, he began organizing fact-finding&nbsp;
expeditions into the heart of the affected area.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:44.220 --> 01:37:49.140
The first guinea pig to head into the hot zone&nbsp;
was former Foundation Agent Josiah Harrick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:37:49.140 --> 01:37:56.220
who’d been demoted to the lowly D-Class position&nbsp;
of D-126-15 due to failures on a previous mission.

01:37:56.220 --> 01:38:00.240
With a remote link to Dr. Ghazalie,&nbsp;
Harrick was forced to venture into&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:00.240 --> 01:38:04.980
the active anomalous zone to collect footage&nbsp;
and samples of the flora and fauna within.

01:38:04.980 --> 01:38:10.200
The first thing Harrick noticed on his expedition&nbsp;
was the strange quality of the olive trees within&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:10.200 --> 01:38:16.260
the active zone. The bark was a stark white, and&nbsp;
the leaves a bloody red. Up close, Harrick could&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:16.260 --> 01:38:20.760
see that the trunks and branches of the trees&nbsp;
had undergone a process known as ossification,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:20.760 --> 01:38:26.400
where the material slowly becomes bone or&nbsp;
bone-like tissue. Hence the anomaly’s creepy name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:26.400 --> 01:38:31.920
The Bone Orchard. These ossified&nbsp;
trees became known as SCP-3989-1.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:31.920 --> 01:38:37.260
Harrick also made another discovery, all&nbsp;
over the trees and ground were worm-like&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:37.260 --> 01:38:43.920
creatures that looked like long maggots&nbsp;
that the Foundation dubbed SCP-3989-1A.

01:38:43.920 --> 01:38:48.600
Agent Harrick then noticed that something was&nbsp;
off about the leaves of the ossified trees.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:48.600 --> 01:38:53.040
They were beating. He looked closer&nbsp;
and they appeared to be heart tissue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:53.040 --> 01:38:57.840
filled with pumping veins. Dr. Ghazalie&nbsp;
ordered Harrick to take a branch for testing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:38:57.840 --> 01:39:01.860
and when he did, the tree began&nbsp;
to bleed. When he looked down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:01.860 --> 01:39:06.180
he saw that the worm-like creatures that&nbsp;
covered the ground were now crawling up&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:06.180 --> 01:39:11.880
his legs. Ignoring orders from Dr. Ghazalie,&nbsp;
Harrick fled from the active zone in terror.

01:39:11.880 --> 01:39:16.500
As he left, Dr. Ghazalie caught something&nbsp;
in the corner of Harrick’s body-cam footage:&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:16.500 --> 01:39:20.700
A long, white hind-limb,&nbsp;
disappearing behind a tree.

01:39:20.700 --> 01:39:25.860
Back in our normal dimension, tests on the&nbsp;
samples Harrick collected yielded more upsetting&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:25.860 --> 01:39:31.980
discoveries. Genetically, the trees were identical&nbsp;
to humans. The trunks were human bone, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:31.980 --> 01:39:36.900
leaves really were made of human heart tissue.&nbsp;
Fascinated and just a little bit horrified,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:36.900 --> 01:39:44.400
Dr. Ghazalie authorized further expeditions into&nbsp;
3989-A. This time though, Agent Harrick would&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:44.400 --> 01:39:49.860
be accompanied by another D-Class, and both would&nbsp;
be armed with handguns and protective body armor.

01:39:49.860 --> 01:39:55.320
As it would turn out, this expedition would&nbsp;
be even more horrifying than the first.

01:39:55.320 --> 01:39:59.700
As the two D-Classes explored the&nbsp;
active zone to collect further samples,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:39:59.700 --> 01:40:04.800
they found that the worms were responsible for&nbsp;
the ossification of the otherwise non-anomalous&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:04.800 --> 01:40:09.960
olive trees. They consumed the wood, little&nbsp;
by little, and deposited human bone matter&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:09.960 --> 01:40:14.460
in return. Harrick and his companion also&nbsp;
noticed that these trees were beginning to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:14.460 --> 01:40:18.540
bear fruit. Dr. Ghazalie ordered Harrick&nbsp;
to collect some of this fruit for testing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:18.540 --> 01:40:22.980
but when they attempted to remove&nbsp;
the fruit it burst, releasing more&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:22.980 --> 01:40:28.860
worm-creatures. It seemed that the converted&nbsp;
trees acted as incubators for their egg sacs.

01:40:28.860 --> 01:40:33.360
Before the duo could return with the samples&nbsp;
they were able to take, the creature that’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:33.360 --> 01:40:38.580
been spotted on Harrick’s body cam during the&nbsp;
first mission finally appeared. It was huge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:38.580 --> 01:40:45.840
with long, white limbs, and no facial features&nbsp;
except for a huge mouth. It grabbed Harrick’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:45.840 --> 01:40:51.240
companion and literally ate the top half of his&nbsp;
body in a single bite, before dropping his legs&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:51.240 --> 01:40:57.000
to the ground. This horrifying beast, and the&nbsp;
many others like it, would later be designated&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:40:57.000 --> 01:41:04.020
as SCP-3989-2A. Harrick pulled out his side&nbsp;
arm and shot the creature several times. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:04.020 --> 01:41:09.600
creature ignored the bullets though and charged&nbsp;
Harrick. The feed from his bodycam cut soon after.

01:41:09.600 --> 01:41:13.980
Both men were declared killed in action,&nbsp;
and in recognition of his sacrifice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:13.980 --> 01:41:20.040
Josiah Harrick was posthumously reinstated to his&nbsp;
old position in the Foundation. Job well done,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:20.040 --> 01:41:24.240
Agent. Dr. Ghazalie, meanwhile,&nbsp;
prepared for the next mission.

01:41:24.240 --> 01:41:29.460
This time, knowing of the clear dangers present&nbsp;
within The Bone Orchard, Dr. Ghazalie recruited&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:29.460 --> 01:41:36.720
the help of MTF Zeta-9, aka The Mole Rats. Three&nbsp;
members, referred to as Charlie Team, were sent&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:36.720 --> 01:41:41.940
into the anomalous zone, once again remotely&nbsp;
directed by Dr. Ghazalie. They were equipped with&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:41.940 --> 01:41:48.120
experimental ultrasound technology so that they&nbsp;
could scan the fruit of the trees within 3989-A&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:48.120 --> 01:41:55.560
without breaking any and incurring the wrath of&nbsp;
3989-2A, which seemed to act as sentries for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:41:55.560 --> 01:42:00.720
trees. Early on in their journey, they found the&nbsp;
body of Agent Harrick crucified against one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:00.720 --> 01:42:06.180
ossified trees, his skin covered in mysterious&nbsp;
symbols that were likely of a Sarkic origin.

01:42:06.180 --> 01:42:10.800
While we don’t have time to fully explore&nbsp;
Sarkicism, that will require a video explanation&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:10.800 --> 01:42:15.060
all of its own, all you need to know is&nbsp;
that it’s a dangerous religious cult that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:15.060 --> 01:42:21.480
worships flesh and disease and has close ties&nbsp;
to similar, dangerous anomalies like SCP - 610,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:21.480 --> 01:42:26.160
also known as the Flesh That Hates.&nbsp;
People familiar with that SCP will&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:26.160 --> 01:42:31.260
note eerily strange similarities to some of the&nbsp;
things the Mole Rats were about to encounter.

01:42:31.260 --> 01:42:38.880
As Charlie Team explored, they saw a huge number&nbsp;
of 3989-2As observing them with eyeless faces from&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:38.880 --> 01:42:45.120
between the ossified trees. They pressed on, until&nbsp;
they discovered what seemed to be an entirely new&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:45.120 --> 01:42:52.440
kind of tree within the Bone Orchard. SCP-3989-2&nbsp;
were huge trees made out of what appears to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:52.440 --> 01:42:58.440
enlarged human spines in place of a trunk. The&nbsp;
smaller twigs on the tree were made from heart&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:42:58.440 --> 01:43:04.020
and lung tissue, and the whole thing was covered&nbsp;
in what appeared to be human amniotic sacs.

01:43:04.020 --> 01:43:09.000
Charlie Team attempted to use their ultrasound&nbsp;
scanners to discover the contents of these sacs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:09.000 --> 01:43:13.320
but one of them exploded in the&nbsp;
process, releasing an entirely&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:13.320 --> 01:43:20.220
new variety of monster. From the sacs&nbsp;
emerged the larval stage of SCP-3989-2B,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:20.220 --> 01:43:27.660
smaller humanoid monsters with no faces, no&nbsp;
sensory organs, two pelvises., four legs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:27.660 --> 01:43:33.540
and an exposed spine. Suddenly, Charlie Team could&nbsp;
feel a horrifying Sarkic presence around them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:33.540 --> 01:43:37.500
which one member of the team described as&nbsp;
being like someone grabbing her liver and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:37.500 --> 01:43:42.720
giggling in her face. As the various monsters of&nbsp;
the Bone Orchard began to converge on the team,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:42.720 --> 01:43:48.480
the voice of the Sarkic prophet of war and&nbsp;
the hunt, Orok, began sounding in their ears.

01:43:48.480 --> 01:43:51.420
He was beckoning them to join him.

01:43:51.420 --> 01:43:53.940
While Charlie Team fled from the active zone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:53.940 --> 01:43:58.920
Dr. Ghazalie felt increasingly drawn&nbsp;
into it. He heard the voice of Orok,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:43:58.920 --> 01:44:05.280
and he liked what he heard. Little by little,&nbsp;
the workers of Area 126 were losing their minds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:05.280 --> 01:44:10.980
manipulated by the Sarkic power of the Bone&nbsp;
Orchard right next to them, day after day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:10.980 --> 01:44:17.100
They were no longer loyal to the Foundation,&nbsp;
they wanted to serve their new dark masters.

01:44:17.100 --> 01:44:22.860
The fourth and final expedition was led by&nbsp;
Dr. Ghazalie himself. He took a band of loyal&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:22.860 --> 01:44:28.800
followers, and one non-believer, on a quest into&nbsp;
the active zone to find an Orokian temple they&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:28.800 --> 01:44:34.380
believed was hidden in the very heart of the Bone&nbsp;
Orchard. Once they were inside, Ghazalie and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:34.380 --> 01:44:40.320
loyalists murdered the non-believer as a sacrifice&nbsp;
to their new master. They carried on until they&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:40.320 --> 01:44:46.500
eventually found what they were looking for: A&nbsp;
giant, stone temple resembling an Aztec ziggurat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:46.500 --> 01:44:55.680
dubbed SCP-3989-4. There, they also encountered&nbsp;
a new kind of monster, dubbed SCP-3989-3.

01:44:56.220 --> 01:45:01.560
These beasts were larger than the others,&nbsp;
and resembled ancient warriors. They had&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:01.560 --> 01:45:06.540
insect-like exoskeletal armor, horned&nbsp;
heads, additional hind and forelimbs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:06.540 --> 01:45:11.940
and integrated bladed weapons. What Dr. Ghazalie&nbsp;
and his companions thought would be paradise&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:11.940 --> 01:45:17.400
turned out to be a kind of Hell as they were&nbsp;
led into the temple, where temporal and spatial&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:17.400 --> 01:45:25.476
distortions broke their mind, and the multiple,&nbsp;
highly aggressive instances of SCP-3989- 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:25.476 --> 01:45:32.160
-2A, and -2B broke their bodies. The&nbsp;
whole thing had been a horrifying trap.

01:45:32.160 --> 01:45:39.060
In that moment, back at Area 126, another fleshy,&nbsp;
horrifying tree sprouted out of the ground in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:39.060 --> 01:45:44.820
middle of the complex. Monsters that had once&nbsp;
been Dr. Ghazalie and his followers emerged&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:44.820 --> 01:45:50.340
from its amniotic sacs, and all hell broke&nbsp;
loose throughout the complex. Soon enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:50.340 --> 01:45:55.260
the base was crawling with monsters from the&nbsp;
Bone Orchard and staff who’d become brainwashed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:55.260 --> 01:45:59.160
Sarkic cultists working in service of Orok. Humans&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:59.160 --> 01:46:03.240
were gathered up to be sacrificed to the&nbsp;
ever-growing number of anomalous trees.

01:46:03.240 --> 01:46:08.580
Things came to a head when the anomaly and&nbsp;
Area 126 was visited by an outside agent&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:08.580 --> 01:46:12.480
from the Foundation working on behalf&nbsp;
of the Hazardous Materials Containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:12.480 --> 01:46:17.700
Liaison. Biological Containment Specialist&nbsp;
Dr. Marshall Grant and his team arrived at&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:17.700 --> 01:46:22.380
the site and were horrified to see the&nbsp;
Sarkic nightmare that had unfolded. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:22.380 --> 01:46:26.460
quickly engaged in a firefight with the&nbsp;
anomalous creatures and Sarkic Devotees&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:26.460 --> 01:46:32.220
who’d gained control over Area 126. A number&nbsp;
of Dr. Grant’s team were lost in the process,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:32.220 --> 01:46:37.620
but thankfully, they were able to eventually&nbsp;
regain control of the base and the anomalous area.

01:46:37.620 --> 01:46:44.460
After this incident, SCP-3989 was upgraded to&nbsp;
Keter Class and given a huge upgrade in security,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:44.460 --> 01:46:49.500
including four meter high concrete&nbsp;
walls and a platoon sized regiment&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:49.500 --> 01:46:52.740
of Mobile Task Force members&nbsp;
with heavy weaponry. The force&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:46:52.740 --> 01:46:57.300
that took over the minds of those&nbsp;
exposed was designated SCP-3989-V

01:46:57.300 --> 01:47:04.320
, a force so powerful that those infected&nbsp;
are given the choice to self-terminate… or be&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:04.320 --> 01:47:11.340
contained forever. This may seem like a somewhat&nbsp;
happy ending to a grim tale, but one detail keeps&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:11.340 --> 01:47:17.040
Dr. Grant, and everyone at the Foundation who&nbsp;
is forced to deal with 3989 awake at night.

01:47:17.040 --> 01:47:20.280
According to all recent&nbsp;
studies into the Bone Orchard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:20.280 --> 01:47:26.520
it isn’t contained at all. In fact,&nbsp;
the active zone… is getting bigger...

01:47:26.520 --> 01:47:29.700
Disturbing things had been&nbsp;
happening on the fifth floor&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:29.700 --> 01:47:33.060
of the Rose Heights apartment&nbsp;
building in Albany, New York.

01:47:33.060 --> 01:47:38.940
Residents had reported strange noises over&nbsp;
the last few days. Screaming in the night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:38.940 --> 01:47:45.780
pained muttering, soft weeping. Scratching&nbsp;
and scuttling in the walls. And worst of all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:45.780 --> 01:47:50.700
what seemed like an infestation of&nbsp;
bugs unlike anything the unfortunate&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:50.700 --> 01:47:53.760
occupants of Rose Heights had ever seen before.

01:47:53.760 --> 01:47:59.760
They weren’t abnormal in size or shape - they&nbsp;
looked an awful lot like the common earwig,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:47:59.760 --> 01:48:02.520
around two and a half centimeters long with large,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:02.520 --> 01:48:08.520
curved pincers on the back. But the color&nbsp;
wasn’t right - unlike the usual dark brown,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:08.520 --> 01:48:15.240
these earwigs were a silvery, almost translucent&nbsp;
gray. When people spotted them crawling across&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:15.240 --> 01:48:19.140
their walls or hiding in the carpet,&nbsp;
they seemed to shimmer in the light.

01:48:19.140 --> 01:48:23.280
Eventually the building’s landlady,&nbsp;
Donna Tompkins, was called in to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:23.280 --> 01:48:26.940
something about the infestation. She&nbsp;
spoke to each of the residents about&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:26.940 --> 01:48:31.860
their experience - they reported the&nbsp;
strange noises, the mysterious bugs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:31.860 --> 01:48:37.560
and even a funny smell they’d sometimes catch&nbsp;
in the hall. A smell like someone had thrown up.

01:48:37.560 --> 01:48:42.120
And every single person that Donna&nbsp;
spoke to couldn’t help but remark that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:42.120 --> 01:48:48.000
the smell was particularly strong outside the&nbsp;
apartment of a certain resident, Bill Parham.

01:48:48.000 --> 01:48:52.800
Stranger still was the fact that&nbsp;
Bill hadn’t been seen in days.

01:48:52.800 --> 01:48:57.360
Donna knocked on his door, but&nbsp;
received no answer. She called&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:48:57.360 --> 01:49:01.320
him on his cell phone and could hear&nbsp;
the phone ringing inside the apartment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:01.320 --> 01:49:06.300
but it just went to voicemail. When she&nbsp;
checked the security footage of the lobby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:06.300 --> 01:49:10.200
she saw that Bill hadn’t left the&nbsp;
building in the last few days either.

01:49:10.200 --> 01:49:15.120
Donna called the police, worried that&nbsp;
Bill might be sick or even dead inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:15.120 --> 01:49:20.040
his apartment. It was strange, given that&nbsp;
he was only in his thirties and didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:20.040 --> 01:49:24.120
seem to have any health conditions,&nbsp;
but stranger things had happened.

01:49:24.120 --> 01:49:27.540
Much stranger things were about to happen, too.

01:49:27.540 --> 01:49:32.640
Two police officers arrived not long after.&nbsp;
They called through the door one more time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:32.640 --> 01:49:36.780
and when they got no response, Donna&nbsp;
gave them the key to head inside.

01:49:36.780 --> 01:49:42.960
The apartment was a wreck. All the furniture&nbsp;
was covered in dust. Filthy dishes were piled&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:42.960 --> 01:49:48.180
high in the sink and on the draining board. The&nbsp;
smell of rot was thick in the air. There were&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:49:48.180 --> 01:49:53.820
empty boxes of painkillers, all the pills popped&nbsp;
from their silvery foil, laying on the ground.

01:49:53.820 --> 01:50:00.360
But worst of all were the bugs. The apartment&nbsp;
was crawling with them, and they were on every&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:00.360 --> 01:50:06.660
surface. Those silvery gray earwigs. Neither&nbsp;
of the officers liked bugs, and it seemed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:06.660 --> 01:50:12.540
the deeper they got into the apartment, the more&nbsp;
bugs there were. Some even seemed to be crawling&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:12.540 --> 01:50:17.460
towards them - pointing their pincers at them&nbsp;
as though they were defending their territory.

01:50:17.460 --> 01:50:23.340
This looked to be a textbook case of what happens&nbsp;
when a resident keels over and dies, but there was&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:23.340 --> 01:50:29.940
just one problem. Where was the body? Bill Parham&nbsp;
had seemingly dropped off the face of the earth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:29.940 --> 01:50:35.520
and now, a colony of mysterious bugs had started&nbsp;
squatting in his apartment in his absence.

01:50:35.520 --> 01:50:42.900
Then came that smell again. That truly&nbsp;
awful smell, like bile and blood. It was&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:42.900 --> 01:50:47.760
even stronger now and it seemed like&nbsp;
it was coming from a nearby closet.

01:50:47.760 --> 01:50:51.420
The two officers, acting on pure&nbsp;
instinct, drew their weapons and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:51.420 --> 01:50:55.320
approached the closet with caution. Even&nbsp;
if they weren’t consciously aware of it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:50:55.320 --> 01:51:02.760
they knew they were going to find something awful&nbsp;
inside. Something evil. Something dangerous.

01:51:02.760 --> 01:51:07.560
When they threw open the closet door,&nbsp;
they couldn’t help but scream. They’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:07.560 --> 01:51:13.380
found the nest. It was a huge, round hive,&nbsp;
like the biggest beehive you’ve ever seen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:13.380 --> 01:51:18.900
melded to the lower corner of the closet.&nbsp;
The unnatural earwigs were crawling into,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:18.900 --> 01:51:24.240
out of, and around it. Thousands&nbsp;
of them. Tens of thousands of them.

01:51:24.240 --> 01:51:27.540
And the second they registered&nbsp;
the presence of the two officers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:27.540 --> 01:51:31.800
intruders into their nest, they began to swarm.

01:51:31.800 --> 01:51:35.760
In sheer panic, both raised their&nbsp;
guns and opened fire into the closet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:35.760 --> 01:51:40.320
but it didn’t do them any good. Their&nbsp;
bullets just pierced and splintered the hive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:40.320 --> 01:51:45.540
causing even more enraged insects to spill&nbsp;
out and begin crawling over the two cops.

01:51:45.540 --> 01:51:49.860
They fled from the apartment, screaming&nbsp;
in pain from the gnashing pincers of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:51:49.860 --> 01:51:54.840
insects crawling all over their skin. They&nbsp;
never did find the corpse of Bill Parham.

01:51:54.840 --> 01:52:00.180
But that’s because Bill Parham wasn’t&nbsp;
dead. At least, not until mere moments ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:00.180 --> 01:52:04.680
when the bullets from the cops’ guns had torn&nbsp;
through his bones and perforated his organs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:04.680 --> 01:52:10.140
He died not long after, and if he could still&nbsp;
speak close to the end, he would have thanked&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:10.140 --> 01:52:15.180
them both for the mercy. Because the monstrosity&nbsp;
that they’d just encountered in the closet wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:15.180 --> 01:52:20.760
just a nest of mysterious insects in Bill&nbsp;
Parham’s apartment. It was Bill himself.

01:52:20.760 --> 01:52:26.580
This is the fate worse than death in store&nbsp;
for anyone supremely unlucky enough to fall&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:26.580 --> 01:52:32.160
victim to SCP-439, better known by&nbsp;
the nickname for their unique nests,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:32.160 --> 01:52:37.800
The Bone Hive. And while these nasty little&nbsp;
critters may be small, they’re filled with enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:37.800 --> 01:52:43.020
pure nightmare fuel to send you running into&nbsp;
682’s containment chamber for a little comfort.

01:52:43.020 --> 01:52:45.660
Let’s go through the whole nightmarish process,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:45.660 --> 01:52:49.500
and tell you exactly what&nbsp;
happened to poor Bill Parham.

01:52:49.500 --> 01:52:55.320
First discovered by the SCP Foundation in&nbsp;
mainland China, SCP-439 specimens largely&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:52:55.320 --> 01:53:00.780
get by on the fact they’re not much to look at.&nbsp;
Unless you’re an entomologist, when you see a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:00.780 --> 01:53:05.040
strange insect, you probably just accept the&nbsp;
fact it’s a perfectly normal breed you’ve just&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:05.040 --> 01:53:09.780
never encountered before. Nobody is hammering&nbsp;
down the doors of their local news station to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:09.780 --> 01:53:14.520
alert the press about the gray earwig they saw&nbsp;
crawling out of a crack in their bathroom wall.

01:53:14.520 --> 01:53:20.160
But if Bill Parham had done just that, it&nbsp;
would have saved his life. The Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:20.160 --> 01:53:25.680
would have immediately flagged the incident&nbsp;
as an SCP-439 infestation, and dispatched a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:25.680 --> 01:53:30.240
mobile task force to deal with it. Instead,&nbsp;
when Bill saw the earwig for the first time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:30.240 --> 01:53:34.380
he was getting ready for work and didn’t&nbsp;
have the time to stop and deal with it.

01:53:34.380 --> 01:53:37.500
He made a mental note to buy&nbsp;
some bug killer on the way home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:37.500 --> 01:53:40.740
but quickly forgot. The insect didn’t forget him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:40.740 --> 01:53:46.260
though. In fact, it thought he would be a&nbsp;
perfect candidate for the SCP-439 process.

01:53:46.260 --> 01:53:51.900
The Foundation has tested extensively with&nbsp;
the one SCP-439 sample they’ve been able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:51.900 --> 01:53:57.660
successfully catch and contain. In all these&nbsp;
tests, they found that 439 specimens rejected&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:53:57.660 --> 01:54:04.200
hosts from any species other than humans. They’re&nbsp;
an extraordinarily specific parasite. It’s also&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:04.200 --> 01:54:10.860
only one particular type of SCP-439 specimen that&nbsp;
you actually need to worry about: The Queens.

01:54:10.860 --> 01:54:18.240
Despite their superficial similarities, SCP-439&nbsp;
behave nothing like non-anomalous earwigs. Normal&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:18.240 --> 01:54:24.480
earwigs are not social creatures, they’re solitary&nbsp;
scavengers and they don’t keep nests as permanent&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:24.480 --> 01:54:31.500
habitats. The same can definitely not be said&nbsp;
for SCP-439. They have complex social structures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:31.500 --> 01:54:38.160
much like that of bees, ants, and termites,&nbsp;
with queens, scouts, workers, and warriors.

01:54:38.160 --> 01:54:43.560
If you happen to encounter a worker or warrior,&nbsp;
you may get a painful pinch from their pincers&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:43.560 --> 01:54:48.060
if you get too close. But if you end up&nbsp;
on the wrong side of one of the queens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:48.060 --> 01:54:51.900
then you have a much, much&nbsp;
worse fate in store for you.

01:54:51.900 --> 01:54:57.300
And it just so happened that the SCP-439&nbsp;
specimen that appeared in Bill Parham’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:54:57.300 --> 01:55:02.880
bathroom that morning was visiting royalty.&nbsp;
This 439 queen had selected her target,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:02.880 --> 01:55:09.480
and now, it was time to move to the next&nbsp;
part of the process: Initial infiltration.

01:55:09.480 --> 01:55:14.400
When Bill returned home from work, he was&nbsp;
delighted to find that the gray earwig was&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:14.400 --> 01:55:19.860
nowhere to be seen - but that didn’t mean&nbsp;
it was gone. It was still there, lurking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:19.860 --> 01:55:26.400
it just didn’t want to be seen. After all, the&nbsp;
real fun would happen after Bill went to bed.

01:55:26.400 --> 01:55:32.700
Once SCP-439 detects that its potential host&nbsp;
has fallen into a deep sleep, it will crawl onto&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:32.700 --> 01:55:38.280
the person’s body, and into their mouth, which&nbsp;
is exactly what it did to Bill. It feels like&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:38.280 --> 01:55:43.080
little more than a tickle in your throat, and you&nbsp;
will have no idea that the tiny creature crawling&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:43.080 --> 01:55:48.960
down your windpipe and into the soft, warm tissue&nbsp;
of your lungs spells your doom. Very few people&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:48.960 --> 01:55:54.660
wake up during this process. But even if they&nbsp;
did, there’s virtually nothing they could do.

01:55:54.660 --> 01:55:59.460
When Bill woke up, he was suffering from&nbsp;
mild chest pains and shortness of breath,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:55:59.460 --> 01:56:04.440
a symptom not uncommon in a number of&nbsp;
respiratory ailments. He had no idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:04.440 --> 01:56:08.160
that the SCP-439 Queen was already inside him.

01:56:08.160 --> 01:56:13.500
He got up and went about his day, trying to ignore&nbsp;
the pain as it gradually grew worse and worse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:13.500 --> 01:56:18.900
feeling almost like something was moving&nbsp;
inside his chest. He spent the whole day&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:18.900 --> 01:56:23.940
having to stop to let out a deep, hacking&nbsp;
cough, but coughing didn’t expel or change&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:23.940 --> 01:56:28.500
anything. He looked and felt so terrible&nbsp;
that his boss let him go home early,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:28.500 --> 01:56:32.940
hoping that Bill would be able to sleep off&nbsp;
whatever illness he thought he had picked up.

01:56:32.940 --> 01:56:38.400
But over the next couple days, his&nbsp;
condition only worsened. The pain grew&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:38.400 --> 01:56:43.380
so excruciating he could barely move, and&nbsp;
he was popping painkillers like tic tacs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:43.380 --> 01:56:49.080
to no effect. He started running a dangerously&nbsp;
high fever, his body trying in vain to fight&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:49.080 --> 01:56:54.000
back against its lethal intruder. He&nbsp;
felt worse than he ever had in his life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:56:54.000 --> 01:56:59.640
but little did poor Bill know, the most&nbsp;
terrible parts of the process were yet to come.

01:56:59.640 --> 01:57:06.480
Through anomalous means, an SCP-439 infection&nbsp;
is able to induce Fibrodysplasia ossificans&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:06.480 --> 01:57:12.000
progressiva, or FOP, in its victims, which&nbsp;
is typically a genetic disease that presents&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:12.000 --> 01:57:17.520
itself before the victim turns ten years old. The&nbsp;
condition is infamous for its primary symptom:&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:17.520 --> 01:57:22.980
Turning muscle and other soft tissue&nbsp;
into bone, slowly but surely paralyzing&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:22.980 --> 01:57:27.960
the victim and putting them in a state of&nbsp;
unspeakable pain. This bone transformation&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:27.960 --> 01:57:33.900
process is known as “Ossification”, and&nbsp;
Bill was about to experience it first hand.

01:57:33.900 --> 01:57:39.600
His pain increased as his mobility decreased,&nbsp;
with more of his flesh becoming solid lumps of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:39.600 --> 01:57:46.500
bone underneath the skin. Soon enough, all&nbsp;
he knew was pain. It’d become so agonizing&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:46.500 --> 01:57:52.140
that he was delirious with it, he was drunk&nbsp;
on pain. Even perceiving sunlight felt like&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:52.140 --> 01:57:57.180
being stabbed in the eyes. That’s why,&nbsp;
like all the other victims of SCP-439,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:57:57.180 --> 01:58:02.160
he decided to conceal himself in a warm,&nbsp;
dark place where no light could get to him.

01:58:02.160 --> 01:58:06.000
In Bill’s case, of course,&nbsp;
that place was his closet.

01:58:06.000 --> 01:58:10.920
He was hurting so bad that all he could do was&nbsp;
curl up into the fetal position and weep as his&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:10.920 --> 01:58:16.560
muscles turned to bone and his body began to&nbsp;
compact and shrink. He didn’t even look like a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:16.560 --> 01:58:22.980
human anymore - he was more like a ball, covered&nbsp;
in a bone shell and filled with warm organs.

01:58:22.980 --> 01:58:27.420
That’s when the queen started&nbsp;
laying eggs among his organs.

01:58:27.420 --> 01:58:30.360
It wasn’t long before there&nbsp;
was a new brood of around&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:31.200 --> 01:58:37.260
30,000 specimens living inside Bill’s body.&nbsp;
He was still very much alive, but there wasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:37.260 --> 01:58:42.600
anything he could do about his situation.&nbsp;
His muscles had long since turned to bone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:42.600 --> 01:58:47.160
and they had eaten large portions of his&nbsp;
brain, leaving mainly the parts needed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:47.160 --> 01:58:53.160
keep his organs just barely functioning. After&nbsp;
all, the colony still needs central heating.

01:58:53.160 --> 01:58:58.560
SCP-439 colonies have developed a perfect&nbsp;
parasitic relationship with the human body.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:58:58.560 --> 01:59:03.900
They even use the stomach inside the hive to&nbsp;
predigest food into a liquid slurry that’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:03.900 --> 01:59:08.820
easier for them to consume. The only loser&nbsp;
in this situation is someone like Bill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:08.820 --> 01:59:13.740
who is forced to become the new home for&nbsp;
the world’s most nightmarish freeloaders.

01:59:13.740 --> 01:59:18.180
Eventually, when the colony becomes too&nbsp;
big, a queen departs to start a new one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:18.180 --> 01:59:22.380
and the process repeats itself&nbsp;
once more. It’s enough to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:22.380 --> 01:59:25.860
you want to sleep with your mouth&nbsp;
closed for the rest of your life.

01:59:25.860 --> 01:59:29.460
Oh, and we haven’t even&nbsp;
told you the worst part yet.

01:59:29.460 --> 01:59:34.140
Foundation scientists have conducted&nbsp;
tests on some victims of SCP-439,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:34.140 --> 01:59:37.620
and found that while the creatures&nbsp;
do consume large parts of the brain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:37.620 --> 01:59:44.040
the parts they leave are capable of consciousness.&nbsp;
That’s right, their victims remain aware of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:44.040 --> 01:59:49.740
what’s happening to them the whole time, even&nbsp;
when they hardly seem human at all anymore.

01:59:49.740 --> 01:59:55.260
What actually finally kills the victims&nbsp;
of SCP-439 isn’t the bodily trauma.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:59:55.260 --> 02:00:00.060
It’s the starvation that sets in when&nbsp;
the colony inevitably moves on. Did&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:00.060 --> 02:00:03.360
we just hear you cough? You might&nbsp;
want to go get that checked out…

02:00:03.360 --> 02:00:09.180
A woman wanders through the lonely hills in&nbsp;
the dead of night. Her purple sari is torn&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:09.180 --> 02:00:14.580
and filthy from days of exposure to the elements;&nbsp;
her bare feet have been cut up and bruised by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:14.580 --> 02:00:20.100
rough terrain she walks. But her clothes and her&nbsp;
feet are not the most noticeable thing about her:&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:20.100 --> 02:00:25.560
This woman is pregnant, her belly swollen to&nbsp;
freakish proportions. It’s frankly a miracle&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:25.560 --> 02:00:30.300
that she’s even able to walk in this state. She&nbsp;
stumbles and sways under the weight of the thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:30.300 --> 02:00:32.640
growing inside her.
Whatever it is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:32.640 --> 02:00:39.060
it’s too large to be any kind of ordinary baby.
But she keeps moving, muttering to herself in&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:39.060 --> 02:00:45.360
a language that no human ear has heard in years.&nbsp;
Her eyes are glazed over, almost hypnotized. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:45.360 --> 02:00:50.220
moves with great purpose, but her vacant facial&nbsp;
expression makes it appear as though she doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:50.220 --> 02:00:56.520
know exactly what that purpose is. She just needs&nbsp;
to keep moving further into the wilderness until&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:00:56.520 --> 02:01:03.540
“It” happens, whatever “It” is. The one thing&nbsp;
that’s certain is that It isn’t anything good.&nbsp;

02:01:03.540 --> 02:01:09.480
A car rumbles down a nearby dirt road. It’s&nbsp;
being driven by Dr. Vinay Ramachandran, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:09.480 --> 02:01:14.820
medical practitioner from the nearby city of Surat&nbsp;
who occasionally drives out to more rural areas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:14.820 --> 02:01:20.520
where the locals might not have easy access to&nbsp;
medical help. He spots the staggering woman and&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:20.520 --> 02:01:25.260
immediately pumps the breaks of his car. She’s&nbsp;
clearly in need of medical attention, thank&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:25.260 --> 02:01:30.540
goodness he happened to be driving by at the time!
Dr. Ramachandran grabs his medical bag from&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:30.540 --> 02:01:36.060
the back seat and rushes towards the woman, who&nbsp;
collapses in a heap before he reaches her. That’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:36.060 --> 02:01:40.800
when, to his utter horror, Dr. Ramachandran&nbsp;
notices that the woman’s belly is continuing&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:40.800 --> 02:01:45.840
to swell at an unnatural rate. Even for a&nbsp;
woman who was heavily pregnant with triplets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:45.840 --> 02:01:50.100
this would still be far too large.&nbsp;
And the rate at which she’s swelling&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:50.100 --> 02:01:54.900
is akin to someone blowing up a balloon.
By the time Dr. Ramachandran reaches her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:54.900 --> 02:01:59.820
the worst has already happened. The woman’s&nbsp;
belly has burst open, and crouching on her&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:01:59.820 --> 02:02:06.060
corpse is the thing that was growing inside&nbsp;
her: An adult man, nude and covered in blood.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:06.060 --> 02:02:11.460
Dr. Ramachandran’s terror only increases&nbsp;
when he notices that the man is eating her.&nbsp;

02:02:11.460 --> 02:02:16.920
Elsewhere, a riot is unfolding in the streets.&nbsp;
A megaphone-wielding instigator barks orders&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:16.920 --> 02:02:22.080
for violence and chaos as the rioters&nbsp;
spread, setting fires, smashing windows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:22.080 --> 02:02:27.420
and attacking any unfortunate civilians caught&nbsp;
in their way. It’s one of the worst riots that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:27.420 --> 02:02:32.460
the area has ever seen. Even the veteran riot&nbsp;
cops are frightened by the ferocity of it.&nbsp;

02:02:32.460 --> 02:02:37.260
The cops descend and clash with the crowd of&nbsp;
ever-advancing rioters. They’re beaten back&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:37.260 --> 02:02:41.880
with crowbars, baseball bats, knives,&nbsp;
and metal pipes. And behind them all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:41.880 --> 02:02:47.460
the instigator continues spitting his venomous&nbsp;
words, working the crowd into an unmatchable&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:47.460 --> 02:02:51.540
frenzy. They’ll need heavy reinforcements&nbsp;
if they want to get this riot under control.&nbsp;

02:02:51.540 --> 02:02:57.240
That’s when one of the riot cops on the front&nbsp;
line, Sergeant Abhishek, notices something&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:02:57.240 --> 02:03:03.780
strange: So many of the rioters seem to have&nbsp;
the exact same face. The face of the instigator.&nbsp;

02:03:03.780 --> 02:03:08.580
Another place, another time, four men&nbsp;
are digging up a grave in a desolate&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:08.580 --> 02:03:13.560
old graveyard. They work tirelessly, all&nbsp;
moving in perfect synchronicity. They’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:13.560 --> 02:03:18.240
only interrupted when a group of heavily-armed&nbsp;
men crash the party and start firing on them.&nbsp;

02:03:18.240 --> 02:03:23.220
But these graverobbers are prepared. All of&nbsp;
them draw revolvers like a gang in an old&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:23.220 --> 02:03:28.320
Western and begin returning fire, causing the&nbsp;
men in tactical gear to seek cover behind the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:28.320 --> 02:03:33.660
nearby tombstones. While one of the graverobbers&nbsp;
continues to fire, the other three scatter during&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:33.660 --> 02:03:38.640
the confusion. When his gun runs dry with&nbsp;
that telltale click, the men in tactical&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:38.640 --> 02:03:44.160
gear immediately rise up and pincushion him&nbsp;
with shot after shot of their assault rifles.&nbsp;

02:03:44.160 --> 02:03:48.960
He does the bullet dance like Tony Montana&nbsp;
and collapses to the ground. But when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:48.960 --> 02:03:54.780
gunmen approach to confirm the kill, there’s a&nbsp;
horrifying twist of fate: Swarms of horrible red&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:03:54.780 --> 02:04:00.540
flies start pouring out of every bullet wound,&nbsp;
swarming the attackers, who retreat, swatting&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:00.540 --> 02:04:05.580
away these horrible little insects. But there’s so&nbsp;
many of them. There’s no way to stop at least some&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:05.580 --> 02:04:10.260
of them from crawling into their mouths.
Here’s an interesting fact: All of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:10.260 --> 02:04:15.900
nightmarish incidences are connected.
In the year 1969, a mysterious man was&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:15.900 --> 02:04:21.660
arrested in Himatnagar, an area in the Indian&nbsp;
state of Gujarat. This man had been accused&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:21.660 --> 02:04:26.580
of inciting civil unrest, terrorizing and&nbsp;
distressing the local people. He was later&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:26.580 --> 02:04:31.920
extradited to an unknown location after the Indian&nbsp;
authorities received a request from a mysterious&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:31.920 --> 02:04:38.160
organization known as - yep, you guessed it&nbsp;
- the SCP Foundation. Who could this man have&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:38.160 --> 02:04:42.360
possibly been to attract such attention? The&nbsp;
authorities thought it best not to question it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:42.360 --> 02:04:45.720
they were probably just glad to be rid&nbsp;
of the troublemaker once and for all.&nbsp;

02:04:45.720 --> 02:04:51.960
Except they weren’t - Not by a long shot.
A few years later, in 1975, a group of four&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:51.960 --> 02:04:58.140
men were discovered in a cemetery, this time in&nbsp;
Ahmedabad, another location in Gujarat, India, for&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:04:58.140 --> 02:05:03.600
desecrating graves. This would be strange and&nbsp;
upsetting enough, but what really sent things to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:03.600 --> 02:05:10.140
the next level of weirdness was the discovery that&nbsp;
these four men were all the same man. each one was&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:10.140 --> 02:05:16.980
not only genetically identical to one another, but&nbsp;
also to the man that had been extradited in 1969.&nbsp;

02:05:16.980 --> 02:05:21.000
You’d be more than justified in asking,&nbsp;
“What the hell is going on here?&nbsp;

02:05:21.000 --> 02:05:26.220
Maybe they were a group of highly rare&nbsp;
quintuplets, five children all born from the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:26.220 --> 02:05:32.100
mother, who just happened to have a predilection&nbsp;
towards crime and antisocial behavior. Or perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:32.100 --> 02:05:36.900
something stranger was afoot: The four who&nbsp;
appeared in the cemetery might have been clones&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:36.900 --> 02:05:41.820
of the original troublemaker in Himatnagar. As&nbsp;
relatively simple as those explanations would be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:41.820 --> 02:05:48.000
the truth was in fact far, far weirder than mad&nbsp;
science or coincidentally criminal quintuplets.&nbsp;

02:05:48.000 --> 02:05:52.260
The four from the cemetery had been ambushed&nbsp;
by operatives of the Global Occult Coalition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:52.260 --> 02:05:57.720
another shadowy organization fans of this&nbsp;
channel are likely to recognize. The Coalition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:05:57.720 --> 02:06:03.720
or “GOC”, is a group that views itself as the&nbsp;
police of the paranormal world, using extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:03.720 --> 02:06:08.580
advanced technology to destroy supernatural&nbsp;
entities and artifacts rather than contain&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:08.580 --> 02:06:13.920
them. They’ve been known to work both alongside&nbsp;
and against the SCP Foundation; both groups’&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:13.920 --> 02:06:18.780
combined interest in four genetically identical&nbsp;
men in an Indian graveyard seems to suggest there&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:18.780 --> 02:06:24.180
was something supernatural about their origin.
One of the men had been killed by the GOC, while&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:24.180 --> 02:06:29.460
the remaining three were taken into custody by the&nbsp;
SCP Foundation. Gotta love the power of teamwork.&nbsp;

02:06:29.460 --> 02:06:34.380
But who were these men? Where had they&nbsp;
come from and why did they share identical&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:34.380 --> 02:06:39.420
genes to the first man from six years earlier?&nbsp;
Could there have been even more of them? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:39.420 --> 02:06:42.840
in the years following, the Foundation&nbsp;
has been able to determine that, yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:42.840 --> 02:06:47.520
there are more of these genetically identical&nbsp;
individuals out there. Across the more rural&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:47.520 --> 02:06:54.780
states of India, like Gujarat, Rajasthan, Himachal&nbsp;
Pradesh, Haryana, Punjab, Jammu, and Kashmir,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:06:54.780 --> 02:07:02.460
there may be over a thousand instances of the same&nbsp;
person. Collectively, they are known as SCP-2833.&nbsp;

02:07:02.460 --> 02:07:08.760
While their outward appearances can vary somewhat,&nbsp;
instances of SCP-2833 all share the exact same&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:08.760 --> 02:07:13.860
genetic traits as each other. Depending on the&nbsp;
area they are located in, these anomalous people&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:13.860 --> 02:07:18.000
can speak various languages and regional dialects&nbsp;
including Hindi, English, Gujarati, Dogri,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:18.000 --> 02:07:25.980
Kashmiri, Punjabi, Urdu, and even an outdated,&nbsp;
unknown language that doesn’t correspond with&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:25.980 --> 02:07:32.640
any known modern dialect or language family. Each&nbsp;
SCP-2833 also possesses the ability to manipulate&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:32.640 --> 02:07:37.020
the organic matter of their own body. Now, we&nbsp;
don’t mean that these men will stretch themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:37.020 --> 02:07:42.180
like Mr. Fantastic, or turn into something out&nbsp;
of John Carpenter’s The Thing, but they are able&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:42.180 --> 02:07:51.180
to use their bodies to create… well, something.
SCP-2833 instances can produce a small anomalous&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:51.180 --> 02:07:57.300
parasite, known as SCP-2833-A. These are&nbsp;
often released through any bodily orifice&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:07:57.300 --> 02:08:03.060
like the mouth, nose, or ears, or through any&nbsp;
cuts or open wounds suffered by an SCP-2833.&nbsp;

02:08:03.060 --> 02:08:09.060
In other words, if you shot and killed an&nbsp;
SCP-2388, perhaps in a cemetery under the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:09.060 --> 02:08:13.200
orders of the Global Occult Coalition,&nbsp;
then these parasites would still be able&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:13.200 --> 02:08:17.700
to escape through the victim’s bullet wounds.&nbsp;
The only way to stop this from happening is to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:17.700 --> 02:08:23.460
incinerate the body of a deceased SCP-2833,&nbsp;
burning them until there is nothing left.&nbsp;

02:08:23.460 --> 02:08:27.600
So, what exactly are these parasites?
Well, they’re tiny invertebrates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:27.600 --> 02:08:33.060
meaning they’re a small, cold-blooded organism&nbsp;
with no spine that can live on land or in water.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:33.060 --> 02:08:38.940
They closely resemble Dipterans, which are any&nbsp;
order of insects that contain what we know as&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:38.940 --> 02:08:45.480
flies. Red in color and twenty millimeters in&nbsp;
length, SCP-2833-As are composed of a combination&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:45.480 --> 02:08:49.620
of muscle tissue, keratin - the protein that&nbsp;
your hair, skin, and fingernails are made&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:49.620 --> 02:08:54.420
from - and traces of ash, strangely enough.
They are also capable of flying with their&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:54.420 --> 02:08:59.160
two wings and will use these to attempt to&nbsp;
enter the body of a suitable host. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:08:59.160 --> 02:09:03.780
this can be any vertebrate creature, it&nbsp;
seems they have a preference for humans.&nbsp;

02:09:03.780 --> 02:09:09.960
Once inside the host’s body, an SCP-2833-A&nbsp;
parasite will attach itself to their nervous&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:09.960 --> 02:09:15.900
system. This then allows the SCP-2833 instance&nbsp;
that the parasite originated from to control&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:15.900 --> 02:09:20.460
the body of the host, taking over their&nbsp;
bodily and motor functions, nervous system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:20.460 --> 02:09:26.820
and all of their sensory organs. From here, an&nbsp;
SCP-2833 will then either subject the target&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:26.820 --> 02:09:31.620
to vivid, inescapable hallucinations, or&nbsp;
manipulate the functions of their body.&nbsp;

02:09:31.620 --> 02:09:38.580
The parasites also contain a miniature instance of&nbsp;
another SCP-2833, only about two millimeters long.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:38.580 --> 02:09:45.720
While these mini SCP-2833s are usually chemically&nbsp;
inactive, lying dormant and unable to move, this&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:45.720 --> 02:09:53.340
changes if the parasite’s host is a human female.&nbsp;
In these cases, the SCP-2833-A creature will&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:09:53.340 --> 02:10:00.840
implant the miniature SCP-2833 within the uterus&nbsp;
of their female host. After this, the new SCP-2833&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:00.840 --> 02:10:06.780
will begin to rapidly grow, consuming any and&nbsp;
all organic matter that surrounds it. Once again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:06.780 --> 02:10:13.020
the SCP-2833 that the parasite originated from is&nbsp;
still able to manipulate the female host’s body&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:13.020 --> 02:10:18.660
and will use this control to make her leave her&nbsp;
home and travel away from any urban environment.&nbsp;

02:10:18.660 --> 02:10:25.440
After a year, the new instance of SCP-2833&nbsp;
will be born in a truly horrific fashion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:25.440 --> 02:10:30.000
Every time this happens, the female&nbsp;
host is unable to survive the process,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:30.000 --> 02:10:36.540
dying as a result of being used as an incubator&nbsp;
for the parasites. The newly formed SCP-2833&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:36.540 --> 02:10:41.520
will retain all the memories of the previous&nbsp;
instance that released the parasite. They are&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:41.520 --> 02:10:47.100
even able to speak fluently from the moment they&nbsp;
are born. But that isn’t the most horrific part.&nbsp;

02:10:47.100 --> 02:10:53.220
What happens next is that the newborn SCP-2833&nbsp;
will then devour the body of the female host&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:53.220 --> 02:10:59.340
that carried it. Sometimes, the host can die&nbsp;
before an SCP-2833 is born, with the parasite&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:10:59.340 --> 02:11:04.440
keeping their body embalmed until the new&nbsp;
instance emerges. But regardless, the “mother”&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:04.440 --> 02:11:10.560
of an SCP-2833 will always die during birth.
The SCP Foundation has conducted a number of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:10.560 --> 02:11:16.260
interviews with the instances of SCP-2833 that&nbsp;
they have captured and detained. The first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:16.260 --> 02:11:24.420
SCP-2833-1, the man causing civil unrest in&nbsp;
Himatnagar, 1969, referred to himself as ‘we’,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:24.420 --> 02:11:29.520
implying that all of the SCP-2833&nbsp;
instances share the same consciousness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:29.520 --> 02:11:36.720
acting as a hive mind of sorts. One of the&nbsp;
men from the cemetery, SCP-2833-4, elaborated&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:36.720 --> 02:11:41.400
further on the nature of these anomalous beings&nbsp;
when asked how many other instances existed:

02:11:41.400 --> 02:11:49.080
“We are in your cages. We are distant from the&nbsp;
hordes of the ignorant. We are grown like crops&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:49.080 --> 02:11:54.720
and livestock. We are growing in numbers and&nbsp;
faith, and we will grow until the ascension of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:11:54.720 --> 02:12:01.860
Samādhi… Samādhi is beyond sight… the buried&nbsp;
will rise. To be consumed is the doorway to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:01.860 --> 02:12:09.420
rebirth. This is our cycle, waiting for Samādhi&nbsp;
with patience. We shall dance the Tandava and&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:09.420 --> 02:12:14.400
consume the world for its rebirth.”
“Samādhi” is a word meaning a crypt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:14.400 --> 02:12:19.800
usually the final resting place of a saint or&nbsp;
someone of religious significance. Additionally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:19.800 --> 02:12:26.040
the “Tandava” is an ancient dance, that according&nbsp;
to legends, was performed by the Hindu god Shiva,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:26.040 --> 02:12:30.780
who was believed to be the source of all&nbsp;
things, the cycle of creation, preservation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:30.780 --> 02:12:36.180
and destruction. So, these anomalous beings&nbsp;
and their parasites appeared to be awaiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:36.180 --> 02:12:42.660
the discovery of an ancient burial site, where&nbsp;
someone or something was prophesied to rise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:42.660 --> 02:12:48.720
consume the world, and then recreate it.
Thinking this Samādhi might pose a threat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:12:48.720 --> 02:12:54.420
the Foundation probed a later instance of SCP-2833&nbsp;
for further information on its significance.&nbsp;

02:12:54.420 --> 02:13:00.000
“If you intend to seek Samādhi,&nbsp;
your quest is in vain. For we are&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:00.000 --> 02:13:07.080
the inheritor to Samādhi. Only we!”
SCP-2833-42 protested when asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:07.080 --> 02:13:11.280
about the Samādhi by a Foundation&nbsp;
researcher, one Doctor Sanjay Sheel.&nbsp;

02:13:11.280 --> 02:13:15.540
“Samādhi does not threaten.&nbsp;
It is we who were threatened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:15.540 --> 02:13:21.540
exiled when the Colossi overran Samādhi. We&nbsp;
are the remnants, but we are never defeated.”&nbsp;

02:13:21.540 --> 02:13:27.360
The instance went on. “We are of glorious&nbsp;
lineage, the chosen stock of Karcist Vaski.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:27.360 --> 02:13:32.880
Only the strongest and most zealous may serve&nbsp;
his purpose. To that end, we cut and consume&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:32.880 --> 02:13:38.760
ourselves to persist and await for Samādhi.”
When asked who exactly Karcist Vaski was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:38.760 --> 02:13:45.660
SCP-2833-42 answered “We&nbsp;
are. We are Karcist Vaski.”&nbsp;

02:13:45.660 --> 02:13:52.020
That word, “Karcist”, has long been associated&nbsp;
with the religious cult of Sarkicism, another&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:52.020 --> 02:13:56.640
group of interest you’re likely to be familiar&nbsp;
with if you’re a fan of what we do here. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:13:56.640 --> 02:14:02.220
group worships flesh and disease and is seen as&nbsp;
an apocalyptic threat by the SCP Foundation. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:02.220 --> 02:14:06.600
Sarkicist religion was founded thousands of&nbsp;
years ago by an ancient elder being known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:06.600 --> 02:14:13.860
the Sorcerer-King of Adytum, also called Grand&nbsp;
Karcist Ion. The goal of Sarkicism is to bring&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:13.860 --> 02:14:20.100
about a new age of flesh, elevating humanity to&nbsp;
the form of gods and potentially terraforming the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:20.100 --> 02:14:28.200
entire Earth using SCP-610, The Flesh that Hates.
So, who or what was Karcist Vaski? What role did&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:28.200 --> 02:14:32.940
it have in the religion of Sarkicism&nbsp;
and how does it link to SCP-2833?&nbsp;

02:14:32.940 --> 02:14:38.340
The Foundation has collected a number of documents&nbsp;
once belonging to a man named Sir William Henry&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:38.340 --> 02:14:43.980
Sleeman. Sleeman was an administrator who worked&nbsp;
in India on behalf of the British East India&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:43.980 --> 02:14:50.040
Company before his death in 1856. And it is in&nbsp;
his documents that some of the answers can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:50.040 --> 02:14:55.380
found. According to Sir William, the poor of India&nbsp;
told him about a group of mystics, who were both&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:14:55.380 --> 02:15:00.240
revered and feared among the country’s peasantry.&nbsp;
This group called themselves the Vātula,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:00.240 --> 02:15:05.640
and seemed to hold what Sleeman described as&nbsp;
“an unusual fetish towards death and decay”.&nbsp;

02:15:05.640 --> 02:15:08.340
Sounds an awful lot like&nbsp;
the Sarkicists, doesn’t it?&nbsp;

02:15:08.340 --> 02:15:13.860
Sir William heard rumors that these Vātula&nbsp;
worshiped Shiva, but were never seen at temples,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:13.860 --> 02:15:18.060
choosing instead to worship the Hindu&nbsp;
god in seclusion. Additionally, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:18.060 --> 02:15:24.600
each member of the Vātula, when asked, identified&nbsp;
themselves by the title of “Karcist Vaski.” Not&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:24.600 --> 02:15:29.940
everyone feared them, however, as a group of men&nbsp;
would often attack them. These men were Thuggee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:29.940 --> 02:15:34.500
organized gangs of professional robbers and&nbsp;
murderers that traveled India, strangling&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:34.500 --> 02:15:39.540
their victims to death and robbing them blind.
Perhaps because of this, the Vātula seemed wary&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:39.540 --> 02:15:45.000
to interact with any other worshippers of Shiva,&nbsp;
often dismissing them as pretenders to the faith.&nbsp;

02:15:45.000 --> 02:15:49.920
Hoping to appease and gain an audience with&nbsp;
the Vātula, Sir William’s allies unleashed what&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:49.920 --> 02:15:55.860
they called the Daughter of Shadows, better&nbsp;
known as SCP-029. This divided the Thuggee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:15:55.860 --> 02:16:00.120
in the hopes that the Vātula would then&nbsp;
accept Sleeman as an ally. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:00.120 --> 02:16:04.500
he achieved an audience with them and was&nbsp;
unable to determine whether this group was&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:04.500 --> 02:16:08.640
genuinely devoted to their religious&nbsp;
beliefs or was just a group of madmen.&nbsp;

02:16:08.640 --> 02:16:13.320
What Sir William didn’t realize, was that&nbsp;
under the vestige of “Karcist Vaski”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:13.320 --> 02:16:17.880
this group was subtly spreading the&nbsp;
influence of Sarkicism over India.&nbsp;

02:16:17.880 --> 02:16:22.980
As for SCP-2833, perhaps they are&nbsp;
the descendants of the Vātula group,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:22.980 --> 02:16:28.260
their lineage continuing through the passing of&nbsp;
those little parasites. It’s highly likely that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:28.260 --> 02:16:35.821
these Vātula were all early instances of SCP-2833,&nbsp;
which would explain why those captured by the SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:35.820 --> 02:16:42.479
Foundation claim that they are all Karcist Vaski.
A few years back in 2014, one of the Foundation’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:42.479 --> 02:16:47.160
Mobile Task Forces uncovered a body that was&nbsp;
a genetic match to the other instances of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:47.160 --> 02:16:54.359
SCP-2833. However, this one wasn’t found in&nbsp;
India, but in Krasnoyarsk Krai, Russia. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:16:54.359 --> 02:17:00.540
had strange growths on its muscle tissue and&nbsp;
bones, carrying multiple SCP-2833-A parasites&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:00.540 --> 02:17:06.180
inside its internal organs. The body had even&nbsp;
been modified to contain an artificial uterus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:06.180 --> 02:17:14.580
which carried an infant SCP-2833 instance.
It seems that not only have SCP-2833 found a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:14.580 --> 02:17:20.040
way to evolve, carrying themselves in a modified&nbsp;
body, but they’re also beginning to spread further&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:20.040 --> 02:17:25.260
than ever before. You’ve gotta hand it to&nbsp;
the Sarkicists - They’re certainly adaptable.

02:17:25.260 --> 02:17:31.020
Grigori Gusakov and Anatoly Korneev,&nbsp;
both aged ten, tiptoed through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:31.020 --> 02:17:36.781
deep, dark woods bordering their quaint Russian&nbsp;
village of Obrechennyy. The year was 1990,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:36.780 --> 02:17:41.759
a turbulent time for the people of Russia, seeing&nbsp;
as the Soviet Union was on the precipice of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:41.760 --> 02:17:48.600
collapse. But for these two young boys, global&nbsp;
geopolitics was the last thing on their minds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:17:48.600 --> 02:17:55.920
They were too busy hunting for the legendary,&nbsp;
monstrous witch known only as Baba Yaga.

02:17:55.920 --> 02:18:01.080
For those in our audience who grew up in Eastern&nbsp;
Europe, or those at least decently familiar with&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:01.080 --> 02:18:06.840
Slavic Folklore and/or the John Wick film&nbsp;
series, mention of the name Baba Yaga likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:06.840 --> 02:18:12.660
sends a slight chill down your spine. And if it&nbsp;
doesn’t, just wait. By the end of this video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:12.660 --> 02:18:17.700
you’ll be afraid to go into the woods alone.&nbsp;
Not that going with others would save you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:17.700 --> 02:18:22.380
as poor little Grigori and Anatoly&nbsp;
were about to find out the hard way…

02:18:22.380 --> 02:18:26.940
They forged on through those witchy&nbsp;
woods. By our standards, the boys were&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:26.939 --> 02:18:31.620
tough and headstrong. After all, the Russian&nbsp;
wilderness could be a brutal place to grow up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:31.620 --> 02:18:36.240
and in a town like Obrechennyy, the old&nbsp;
ways of stoicism and perseverance were&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:36.240 --> 02:18:42.540
prized over fear and caution. All except&nbsp;
for one particular area: The Supernatural.

02:18:42.540 --> 02:18:47.100
Like many small villages all over the world&nbsp;
at every point in history, Obrechennyy&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:47.100 --> 02:18:52.201
had its fair share of local superstitions.&nbsp;
Chief among them was the belief that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:52.200 --> 02:18:57.840
local forest was enchanted, and that when people&nbsp;
wandered in among the trees, many of them would&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:18:57.840 --> 02:19:03.300
never return. They’d fall into the gnarled&nbsp;
clutches of the carnivorous witch Baba Yaga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:03.300 --> 02:19:08.904
and their bones would lay among the roots and&nbsp;
dead leaves until they someday crumbled into dust.

02:19:08.904 --> 02:19:09.600
The spindly branches of the fall trees looked like&nbsp;
long, thin fingers crisscrossing above them. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:09.600 --> 02:19:13.140
was starting to get dark out. The air was cold&nbsp;
and thick. When the two boys had first set off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:13.140 --> 02:19:18.300
it’d been with the intention of proving their&nbsp;
mettle among the other local children. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:18.300 --> 02:19:22.440
didn’t fear Baba Yaga; the old witch&nbsp;
in the woods was just another fairy&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:22.439 --> 02:19:25.979
story meant to frighten children,&nbsp;
and they weren’t children anymore.

02:19:25.979 --> 02:19:29.519
Though they would never live to be men.

02:19:29.520 --> 02:19:34.560
It wasn’t long before they were beyond&nbsp;
the point of no return. Which way was out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:34.560 --> 02:19:39.180
and which way was further in? It hardly&nbsp;
mattered anymore, as carrion birds cawed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:39.180 --> 02:19:43.800
far above. The bravado that put them here&nbsp;
was starting to falter now, but neither&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:43.800 --> 02:19:48.420
dared show it. They’d rather be put in mortal&nbsp;
peril than show fear in front of one another.

02:19:48.420 --> 02:19:53.399
Was something moving in the distant&nbsp;
shadows? A thin, twisted, human figure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:53.399 --> 02:19:58.500
impossible to make out save for the faint&nbsp;
glow of its eyes in the gathering dark? They&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:19:58.500 --> 02:20:03.300
couldn’t tell what was real and what was&nbsp;
their mind playing cruel tricks on them.

02:20:03.300 --> 02:20:08.580
A hoarse whisper issued through the brittle&nbsp;
trees in the moments that followed. It was&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:08.580 --> 02:20:16.559
an ancient voice, a voice that had echoed in the&nbsp;
nightmares of generations, a voice that had seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:16.560 --> 02:20:22.020
centuries. It spoke in an older Russian dialect&nbsp;
than either of the young boys could understand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:22.020 --> 02:20:29.220
but somehow, the essence of its message&nbsp;
still rung clear in their hearts and minds.

02:20:29.220 --> 02:20:40.620
“Welcome, little children, to my forest.&nbsp;
Here, your lives are forfeit. You are&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:40.620 --> 02:20:48.720
my property. I look forward to chewing&nbsp;
the tender meat off your young bones.”

02:20:50.520 --> 02:20:56.100
That was all they needed to hear to start&nbsp;
running. Gregori and Anatoly turned and fled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:20:56.100 --> 02:21:00.781
screaming for help, into the darkness&nbsp;
of the forest. Both gasped as they&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:00.780 --> 02:21:05.280
ran through what seemed to be a giant&nbsp;
spider web. They spat and spluttered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:05.280 --> 02:21:08.880
trying to swat away the silky&nbsp;
strands as they ran from the voice.

02:21:08.880 --> 02:21:14.160
Little did they know, what they’d&nbsp;
just run through was no spider web.

02:21:14.160 --> 02:21:20.340
They tried to press on, but their footsteps&nbsp;
slowed. The forest was changing around them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:20.340 --> 02:21:29.220
Twisting, shifting, sparkling. What had seemed&nbsp;
terrifying before was suddenly oddly...beautiful.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:29.220 --> 02:21:35.100
The two boys just stood and watched as the forest&nbsp;
turned into a gorgeous Technicolor light show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:35.100 --> 02:21:41.520
unlike anything they’d ever seen before. Strange&nbsp;
figures hopped and danced through the foliage.

02:21:41.520 --> 02:21:48.241
One tall figure approached them out of the trees.&nbsp;
A beautiful, fair-haired maiden. The two boys&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:48.240 --> 02:21:53.819
were entranced by her. Their hearts were filled&nbsp;
with pure golden light. Why were they running&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:21:53.819 --> 02:22:00.000
before? They couldn’t even remember. They just&nbsp;
smiled as the woman approached them in her long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:00.000 --> 02:22:04.859
flowing dress, smiling back. She was&nbsp;
like something out of a fairy tale.

02:22:04.859 --> 02:22:09.179
They didn’t react. They didn’t&nbsp;
even realize what was happening,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:09.180 --> 02:22:15.600
as the jaws of the horrible, ancient old crone&nbsp;
closed around their skulls for the last time.

02:22:15.600 --> 02:22:21.960
Grigori and Anatoly were never seen again. Just&nbsp;
another two children gone missing in the woods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:21.960 --> 02:22:25.980
the latest entries on a long list&nbsp;
of tragedies to hit the village of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:25.979 --> 02:22:30.000
Obrechennyy. But they were also the&nbsp;
straws that broke the camel’s back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:30.000 --> 02:22:36.120
The villagers were sick of living in fear under&nbsp;
the fabled witch. They would have their revenge.

02:22:36.120 --> 02:22:40.800
The men of the village gathered up their&nbsp;
weapons and formed a hunting party. Guns,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:40.800 --> 02:22:46.560
torches, knives, axes, and fury. They&nbsp;
would slay the beast that had taken so&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:46.560 --> 02:22:51.540
many of their friends and their children in the&nbsp;
woods. As soon as their forces were assembled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:22:51.540 --> 02:22:54.660
they charged into the forest, looking for blood.

02:22:54.660 --> 02:23:00.059
With their numerical advantage and single-minded&nbsp;
determination, it didn’t take them long to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:00.060 --> 02:23:05.520
the monster in the woods. She was every bit as&nbsp;
hideous and nightmarish as they’d anticipated:&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:05.520 --> 02:23:12.060
A gnarled, snarling crone, with long, clawed&nbsp;
fingers and dirty fangs. They got her in their&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:12.060 --> 02:23:18.300
sights and prepared to open fire, but none of&nbsp;
them were ready for Baba Yaga’s counteroffensive.

02:23:18.300 --> 02:23:24.240
She moved like a leaf in a strong wind,&nbsp;
swift and effortless. The men who’d made&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:24.240 --> 02:23:28.859
the mistake of getting too close to her with&nbsp;
knives and axes tasted her terrible wrath.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:28.859 --> 02:23:35.099
She tore through them with claws like iron.&nbsp;
Sank her fangs into their flesh. Lifted and&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:35.100 --> 02:23:40.380
tossed them like rag dolls. How could&nbsp;
she be so fast and so strong? The men&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:40.380 --> 02:23:48.359
were terrified. This was no mere woman. It was a&nbsp;
true monster, squeezed into a barely human form.

02:23:48.359 --> 02:23:52.319
By the time the creature was finally&nbsp;
incapacitated, it’d taken countless&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:52.319 --> 02:23:57.240
bullets and strikes. How any creature could&nbsp;
survive such an assault was unimaginable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:23:57.240 --> 02:24:02.340
Several members of the hunting party were dead&nbsp;
by this point. Others had been overtaken by a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:02.340 --> 02:24:07.680
strange form of madness. A couple of them had&nbsp;
been given to constant giggling fits or were&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:07.680 --> 02:24:14.281
speaking long strings of nonsense. Others had been&nbsp;
rendered entirely catatonic by the experience.

02:24:14.280 --> 02:24:18.120
It was clear that the witch had&nbsp;
powers beyond their understanding.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:18.120 --> 02:24:22.979
They needed to return it to the village&nbsp;
and destroy it as quickly as possible.

02:24:22.979 --> 02:24:27.000
The monster was bound and dragged&nbsp;
back to Obrechennyy. After seeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:27.000 --> 02:24:30.359
how it bewitched some of the men,&nbsp;
they avoided direct contact whenever&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:30.359 --> 02:24:35.280
possible. They would do everything&nbsp;
they could to see justice done.

02:24:35.280 --> 02:24:40.620
Of course, there would be no due process for&nbsp;
Baba Yaga. The violence that had erupted in&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:40.620 --> 02:24:44.160
the forest was more than enough proof&nbsp;
to justify the beast’s immediate death&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:44.160 --> 02:24:48.540
sentence. The local priest gave a prayer&nbsp;
- though he remarked that he was sure this&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:48.540 --> 02:24:53.280
monster was the creation and servant of&nbsp;
the devil - and the execution commenced.

02:24:53.280 --> 02:24:57.899
A local used a blessed sword, anointed&nbsp;
with holy water, to hack off the Baba&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:24:57.899 --> 02:25:03.059
Yaga’s head. Its body was shot several times&nbsp;
for good measure, and it was finally doused in&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:03.060 --> 02:25:07.980
gasoline and set on fire. The remains were&nbsp;
buried just outside the village limits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:07.979 --> 02:25:13.620
hoping that the Baba Yaga’s evil wouldn’t&nbsp;
continue to haunt their town, even in death.

02:25:13.620 --> 02:25:18.479
Isolated villages in the Russian steppe aren’t&nbsp;
famous for their communication with outsiders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:18.479 --> 02:25:23.759
especially back in 1990, when the Soviet&nbsp;
Union was still clinging on to control and&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:23.760 --> 02:25:28.140
the internet was still in its infancy. It&nbsp;
took a few weeks for the news of a village&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:28.140 --> 02:25:33.120
capturing its so-called local witch to&nbsp;
reach the SCP Foundation. After closely&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:33.120 --> 02:25:37.319
studying the peculiar disappearance records&nbsp;
in the area, they sent over a detachment of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:37.319 --> 02:25:41.759
field agents to investigate, and perhaps&nbsp;
conduct a few interviews with the locals.

02:25:41.760 --> 02:25:46.800
They had no way of knowing there wouldn’t&nbsp;
be any left by the time they arrived.

02:25:46.800 --> 02:25:52.140
When the field agents reached Obrechennyy,&nbsp;
it was already a ghost town. Not a single&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:52.140 --> 02:25:58.080
survivor was found, only the evidence of fresh&nbsp;
carnage. Desiccated bodies were found in some&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:25:58.080 --> 02:26:03.840
of the village’s houses. In others, only body&nbsp;
parts. A hole in the ground next to the village&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:03.840 --> 02:26:09.060
seemed to show evidence of some subterranean&nbsp;
creature clawing its way back up to the top.

02:26:09.060 --> 02:26:14.640
Whatever this creature was, it’d clearly crawled&nbsp;
back up from the earth and exacted bloody revenge&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:14.640 --> 02:26:19.500
against those who had buried it. Blood trails&nbsp;
from some of the bodies leading back into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:19.500 --> 02:26:24.960
woods made it clear where the creature had fled&nbsp;
to after massacring the entire village. Given&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:24.960 --> 02:26:29.340
the sudden increase in the situation’s&nbsp;
severity, Mobile Task Force Epsilon-6,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:29.340 --> 02:26:33.960
aka The Village Idiots, were brought&nbsp;
in to apprehend the fugitive witch.

02:26:33.960 --> 02:26:37.680
But much like the literal village&nbsp;
idiots that’d come before them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:37.680 --> 02:26:40.920
this MTF had no idea what they were up against.

02:26:40.920 --> 02:26:45.960
They entered the forest outside Obrechennyy with&nbsp;
superior tactics and weaponry to the villagers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:45.960 --> 02:26:50.160
with orders to contain the creature&nbsp;
at all costs. They didn’t exactly know&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:50.160 --> 02:26:54.120
what they were searching for in the&nbsp;
dark amongst the trees, but when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:54.120 --> 02:26:58.559
first operatives laid eyes on the twisted&nbsp;
old crone, they almost reflexively relaxed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:26:58.560 --> 02:27:04.020
their guard. For some of the Village Idiots,&nbsp;
this would be the last mistake they ever made.

02:27:04.020 --> 02:27:08.460
Some of the operatives began to feel&nbsp;
funny. Much like Grigori, Anatoly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:08.460 --> 02:27:12.180
and some members of the hunting party,&nbsp;
they began to see the forest warping&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:12.180 --> 02:27:16.620
and shifting around them. They giggled&nbsp;
at all the funny colors, and sighed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:16.620 --> 02:27:22.319
feeling an overwhelming sense of calmness and&nbsp;
euphoria. It was honestly the best they’d felt&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:22.319 --> 02:27:27.000
in years. Perhaps they were wrong about&nbsp;
hunting the witch in here. Maybe the real&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:27.000 --> 02:27:31.260
anomaly here was a Russian forest that made&nbsp;
you feel awesome when you stepped inside.

02:27:31.260 --> 02:27:35.340
While the affected agents were giggling&nbsp;
away in their own little la la land,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:35.340 --> 02:27:41.580
Baba Yaga was bringing the pain. With the same&nbsp;
freakish speed, strength, and ferocity that had&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:41.580 --> 02:27:46.620
surprised the hunting party weeks earlier,&nbsp;
the witch was tearing through MTF Epsilon-6,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:46.620 --> 02:27:52.800
ripping through hardened tactical armor with her&nbsp;
long claws and teeth. She took shot after shot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:27:52.800 --> 02:27:57.420
enough tranquilizer to put down an&nbsp;
elephant, but she kept fighting.

02:27:57.420 --> 02:28:01.440
In the end, the training and numerical&nbsp;
superiority of the task force won out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:01.439 --> 02:28:07.259
They were able to secure and contain the&nbsp;
Baba Yaga, soon redesignated SCP-352,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:07.260 --> 02:28:12.420
and take it to a nearby Foundation containment&nbsp;
site for further studies. There they officially&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:12.420 --> 02:28:17.220
recorded all the details: From the creature’s&nbsp;
incredible speed and strength to its regenerative&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:17.220 --> 02:28:22.200
ability so extensive that it could even&nbsp;
survive being decapitated and burned.

02:28:22.200 --> 02:28:24.660
But what about the hallucinogenic effects?

02:28:24.660 --> 02:28:30.479
Like a hungry spider, the Baba Yaga’s true&nbsp;
power comes in her ability to spin a deadly&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:30.479 --> 02:28:36.359
web. Her body is able to produce long, thin,&nbsp;
hair-like fibers, each one coated in powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:36.359 --> 02:28:41.580
hallucinogenic enzymes that induce a sense&nbsp;
of placid, euphoric stillness in its victims.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:41.580 --> 02:28:46.380
When it isn’t engaging multiple targets, the&nbsp;
creature can sometimes take multiple days to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:46.380 --> 02:28:51.900
consume a single, still-living victim, taking&nbsp;
them apart and eating them piece by piece.

02:28:51.899 --> 02:28:58.439
Speaking of eating: As you can probably imagine,&nbsp;
in order to keep SCP-352 uneventfully contained,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:28:58.439 --> 02:29:04.019
it’s ideal to make sure it isn’t hangry.&nbsp;
In order to keep 352 well-fed, they need to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:04.020 --> 02:29:11.460
stock up on its favorite food, human flesh. Though&nbsp;
specifically, 352 has a real hankering for babies.

02:29:11.460 --> 02:29:16.319
While the Foundation are currently exploring&nbsp;
anomalous means of keeping the Baba Yaga fed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:16.319 --> 02:29:20.880
until those means are fully ironed out,&nbsp;
they need to keep this monster fed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:20.880 --> 02:29:26.520
old-fashioned way - only ever withdrawing food as&nbsp;
punishment if it attempts to breach containment.

02:29:26.520 --> 02:29:32.220
After all, there’s a very good reason why&nbsp;
parents and children across the Slavic world&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:32.220 --> 02:29:40.741
fear Baba Yaga. She’s always hungry, and in&nbsp;
the end, she always gets what she wants...

02:29:40.740 --> 02:29:47.340
Who doesn’t love their pets, right? Whether&nbsp;
it’s a dog, a cat, a goldfish, or a hamster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:47.340 --> 02:29:52.560
any pet owner will tell you that their furry&nbsp;
friend is so much more than just an animal&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:52.560 --> 02:29:58.260
that they adopted. To many, pets become permanent&nbsp;
additions to the family; while they might not look&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:29:58.260 --> 02:30:03.660
like a human being, or even have the ability&nbsp;
to speak the way we do, a lot of owners view&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:03.660 --> 02:30:09.420
their pets as people in their own right. Of&nbsp;
course, a person can’t be a pet, at least a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:09.420 --> 02:30:16.980
human person can’t, right? Well, not unless&nbsp;
you happen to be part of SCP-1897, otherwise&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:16.979 --> 02:30:22.259
known as the Human Domestication Society.
If you’ve ever been brave enough to travel&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:22.260 --> 02:30:28.740
alone to the rural parts of southwestern states&nbsp;
like Arizona, New Mexico, Texas, Oklahoma, Utah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:28.740 --> 02:30:36.059
or Nevada, then it’s likely you would’ve been&nbsp;
an ideal victim for SCP-1897. This designation&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:36.060 --> 02:30:42.420
doesn’t refer to one single creature or entity,&nbsp;
but rather a group of similar beings. Witness&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:42.420 --> 02:30:49.380
testimonies and photographs of SCP-1897 depict&nbsp;
them as humanoid creatures, standing approximately&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:49.380 --> 02:30:55.440
five meters in height. These beings have displayed&nbsp;
speed and strength far beyond that of any human,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:55.439 --> 02:30:59.879
they are capable of traveling roughly&nbsp;
two hundred meters in only nine seconds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:30:59.880 --> 02:31:04.319
and lifting weights of up to five&nbsp;
hundred kilos with a single hand.&nbsp;

02:31:04.319 --> 02:31:11.219
These entities are not immortal and can be harmed&nbsp;
by conventional means, but that doesn’t mean it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:11.220 --> 02:31:19.440
an easy task. Any SCP-1897 instance that is killed&nbsp;
or incapacitated immediately vanishes, resulting&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:19.439 --> 02:31:25.080
in them dropping anything that they may have been&nbsp;
carrying at the time. And surprisingly, these are&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:25.080 --> 02:31:30.960
not mindless monsters, and actually appear to be&nbsp;
capable of communication. Furthermore, they do not&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:30.960 --> 02:31:37.080
seem to speak a unique or distinct language but&nbsp;
instead communicate in standard American English,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:37.080 --> 02:31:42.059
with accents and vernacular appropriate&nbsp;
to the regions they appear in. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:42.060 --> 02:31:47.220
they will actively refuse to reply to any human&nbsp;
that attempts to engage them in conversation.&nbsp;

02:31:47.220 --> 02:31:52.500
Now, these creatures don’t spend every waking hour&nbsp;
of the day roaming around the states of Texas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:52.500 --> 02:31:57.780
Oklahoma, and all the others we listed. If they&nbsp;
did, it’s likely a lot more civilians would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:31:57.780 --> 02:32:03.599
spotted them by now, and would probably live their&nbsp;
lives in fear of these gigantic five-meter-tall&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:03.600 --> 02:32:11.100
humanoids. But instances of SCP-1897 will only&nbsp;
manifest if certain specific criteria are met,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:11.100 --> 02:32:19.201
and these are as follows. To encounter SCP-1897,&nbsp;
a person must be alone, or part of a group of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:19.200 --> 02:32:24.720
no more than two. If more than one other person&nbsp;
is with them, then no manifestation will occur.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:24.720 --> 02:32:29.820
There is one exception to the rule: If a&nbsp;
child under the age of twelve is present.&nbsp;

02:32:29.819 --> 02:32:35.880
Secondly, neither the person nor anyone with them&nbsp;
can be carrying any kind of weapon - that means&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:35.880 --> 02:32:42.240
no knives, no guns, not even pepper spray.&nbsp;
Third and finally, they must be at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:42.240 --> 02:32:47.880
twenty-five meters from a major population center.
And what happens when all of these conditions are&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:47.880 --> 02:32:53.280
met and one of these creatures appears? Anyone&nbsp;
witnessing their arrival will notice the creatures&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:53.280 --> 02:32:58.979
materializing, appearing to emerge from some&nbsp;
form of unseen vehicle. When they manifest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:32:58.979 --> 02:33:04.919
the SCP-1897 entities are almost always&nbsp;
carrying long poles with large nets at the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:04.920 --> 02:33:11.280
as well as steel cages, and are often seen&nbsp;
wearing dark green uniforms. In most cases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:11.280 --> 02:33:16.679
they will attempt to capture any nearby person,&nbsp;
in a way that causes them the least possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:16.680 --> 02:33:23.220
harm. Should an SCP-1897 creature successfully&nbsp;
apprehend a person and place them in a cage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:23.220 --> 02:33:28.440
both them and their captive will vanish in a&nbsp;
similar manner to the way the creature appeared.&nbsp;

02:33:28.439 --> 02:33:34.259
All attempts to track SCP-1897 or one&nbsp;
of its abducted victims have failed;&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:34.260 --> 02:33:39.660
there is no way to know where they are taken.&nbsp;
But as far as what happens to them? That,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:39.660 --> 02:33:45.059
we do have a little more insight into.
Sometimes, although it is a highly rare&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:45.060 --> 02:33:49.980
occurrence, the captured human victims may&nbsp;
reappear around a month after their capture.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:49.979 --> 02:33:54.719
While never in the same location as where they&nbsp;
disappeared from, they will always be accompanied&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:33:54.720 --> 02:34:01.440
by an SCP-1987 instance and will stay close by&nbsp;
the creature’s side. At this point, the abductee&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:01.439 --> 02:34:09.179
is barely human anymore. They are considered an&nbsp;
instance of what is known as SCP-1897-1. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:09.180 --> 02:34:14.400
signifies this sudden and drastic transformation?&nbsp;
For one, these victims are always found to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:14.399 --> 02:34:19.620
been forcibly castrated or sterilized,&nbsp;
essentially no longer able to reproduce&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:19.620 --> 02:34:27.120
the way humans naturally do. For another, these&nbsp;
instances of SCP-1897-1 universally display a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:27.120 --> 02:34:32.640
decreased level of cognitive and mental function.
What we mean by that is their brains do not&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:32.640 --> 02:34:37.080
function the way they should anymore.&nbsp;
Instead, these abductees exhibit the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:37.080 --> 02:34:41.880
same level of intelligence and capability&nbsp;
as the average Canis lupus familiaris,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:41.880 --> 02:34:47.340
otherwise known as the common domestic dog.
Should someone attempt to rescue a person&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:47.340 --> 02:34:55.260
that has become an instance of SCP-1897-1, or&nbsp;
display hostility towards the SCP-1897 creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:34:55.260 --> 02:35:00.300
that accompanies them, they will be met with&nbsp;
outward, animalistic aggression from the victim.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:00.300 --> 02:35:05.580
It has been discovered by the SCP Foundation that&nbsp;
these behaviors can be treated with amnestics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:05.580 --> 02:35:13.319
Unfortunately, though, the process of an abducted&nbsp;
person becoming an SCP-1897-1 instance seems to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:13.319 --> 02:35:18.840
be the result of an invasive medical procedure&nbsp;
known as a lobotomy. This typically involves&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:18.840 --> 02:35:24.180
removing or disabling certain parts of the human&nbsp;
brain, meaning that what has been done to these&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:24.180 --> 02:35:30.480
victims is permanent, and cannot be reversed.
So, who is doing all this? Why are these&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:30.479 --> 02:35:35.759
creatures collecting innocent human beings only&nbsp;
to reduce them to little more than animals? The&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:35.760 --> 02:35:42.781
answers lie in something currently referred to&nbsp;
as SCP-1897-2; not another creature or entity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:42.780 --> 02:35:48.059
not an anomalous artifact or location&nbsp;
with strange properties, but a website&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:48.060 --> 02:35:55.201
found at the address ‘www.hdsociety.gov’.&nbsp;
According to the information on this site,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:35:55.200 --> 02:36:01.019
it belongs to a group calling themselves&nbsp;
the Human Domestication Society. The website&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:01.020 --> 02:36:07.440
features pages such as ‘Adoption’, ‘Training’,&nbsp;
‘Breeding Programs’, ‘Volunteering’ and more.&nbsp;

02:36:07.439 --> 02:36:11.939
The fact that this is the kind of website&nbsp;
you might expect to be about dogs or cats&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:11.939 --> 02:36:17.099
but instead focuses on the domestication of&nbsp;
humans is certainly enough to turn the stomach.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:17.100 --> 02:36:23.100
As we said at the start of the video, surely&nbsp;
a human being can’t be somebody’s pet, right?&nbsp;

02:36:23.100 --> 02:36:29.701
Wrong, at least as far as the Human Domestication&nbsp;
Society goes. Their website contains everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:29.700 --> 02:36:35.519
and anything one of these SCP-1897 creatures&nbsp;
could ever hope to learn about owning a human&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:35.520 --> 02:36:41.400
as a pet. “Has your human been misbehaving? Need&nbsp;
to train them to use the toilet? These pages have&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:41.399 --> 02:36:45.899
all the information you need to help your human&nbsp;
become the most well-trained human on your block!”&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:45.899 --> 02:36:53.939
boasts the Training page of www.hdsociety.gov. The&nbsp;
remainder of the page contains links to various&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:53.939 --> 02:36:59.399
articles such as ‘Obedience Training’, which&nbsp;
claims an owner of a human can “show them who’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:36:59.399 --> 02:37:04.379
boss without the need for physical violence”.
Also featured are mentions of how to toilet train&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:04.380 --> 02:37:09.540
or play fetch with a human, how to introduce a&nbsp;
human to others due to them naturally not getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:09.540 --> 02:37:16.620
along. Perhaps most chilling of all is one article&nbsp;
titled ‘Understanding What Your Human Wants’ that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:16.620 --> 02:37:22.439
warns human beings shouldn’t talk. And another,&nbsp;
‘Dealing with Strays’ offers tips for anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:22.439 --> 02:37:28.080
wanting to capture their own pets themselves.&nbsp;
It doesn’t seem like too much of a leap to think&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:28.080 --> 02:37:33.960
that the SCP-1897 creatures have followed a&nbsp;
lot of advice from this particular article.&nbsp;

02:37:33.960 --> 02:37:41.160
Arguably worst of all is an image featured&nbsp;
on the website, of a tall, menacing SCP-1897&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:41.160 --> 02:37:47.340
entity, brandishing a picana electrica.
This device, for any unfamiliar with that term,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:47.340 --> 02:37:53.040
is a form of high voltage electrical cattle&nbsp;
prod, normally used for purposes of torture.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:53.040 --> 02:37:57.840
In the photograph in question, the creature is&nbsp;
wielding one of these while standing sternly&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:37:57.840 --> 02:38:04.860
over a helpless captive human male, now an&nbsp;
instance of SCP-1897-1 with tears in his eyes.&nbsp;

02:38:04.859 --> 02:38:13.620
Further pages found on www.hdsociety.gov recommend&nbsp;
solutions to certain human behaviors. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:13.620 --> 02:38:18.180
like one might expect to find on other&nbsp;
pet care websites, some of the Human&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:18.180 --> 02:38:22.680
Domestication Society’s articles pertain&nbsp;
to dealing with aggression, grooming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:22.680 --> 02:38:28.320
house training, and even toilet training.
Then there’s the Adoption page, which states&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:28.319 --> 02:38:33.719
“We offer a large variety of humans for&nbsp;
adoption every single day. While we cannot&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:33.720 --> 02:38:37.980
guarantee a human you see listed on our website&nbsp;
will be available when you reach the shelter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:37.979 --> 02:38:43.500
our inventory is updated every half-hour. We&nbsp;
cannot answer any questions about specific&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:43.500 --> 02:38:49.080
humans pictured on our website over the phone or&nbsp;
email.” It is still unclear whether or not the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:49.080 --> 02:38:55.140
SCP-1897 creatures that have been known to appear&nbsp;
in the southwestern United States are sent out to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:55.140 --> 02:38:59.760
gather humans en masse to offer for adoption,&nbsp;
or whether these creatures are individuals&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:38:59.760 --> 02:39:05.760
trying to obtain human pets on their own.
Of course, the worst conceivable answer is both.&nbsp;

02:39:05.760 --> 02:39:12.300
The site is horrifyingly comprehensive, with links&nbsp;
to an annual human ownership convention - with&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:12.300 --> 02:39:16.800
panels on breeding and preventing illegal&nbsp;
human poaching and skinning. It’s safe to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:16.800 --> 02:39:21.840
say that if ever you were unlucky enough to&nbsp;
read this website, it’d haunt you for life.&nbsp;

02:39:21.840 --> 02:39:26.940
Naturally, the SCP Foundation has made several&nbsp;
attempts to contact the owners of this website.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:26.939 --> 02:39:33.000
They tried in vain to communicate through the&nbsp;
official channels about SCP-1897-1 adoption&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:33.000 --> 02:39:39.000
as a way of peacefully negotiating that the Human&nbsp;
Domestication Society website be shut down as well&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:39.000 --> 02:39:44.160
as its practices of capturing, lobotomizing,&nbsp;
breeding, and adopting humans. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:44.160 --> 02:39:49.200
these communication attempts were met with&nbsp;
silence. That is until a message was received&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:49.200 --> 02:39:55.859
by The Foundation at Site 06, addressed to a&nbsp;
member of personnel that does not exist. No&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:55.859 --> 02:39:59.639
data pertaining to the physical location of&nbsp;
the sender could be derived from the email,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:39:59.640 --> 02:40:05.100
but it was traced to the same IP address as&nbsp;
the Human Domestication Society’s website.&nbsp;

02:40:05.100 --> 02:40:12.241
The email read as follows: “We will not listen&nbsp;
to your lies any longer. It was you who came&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:12.240 --> 02:40:17.280
after us first. You who tore holes in&nbsp;
our world and tried to annihilate us.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:17.280 --> 02:40:22.859
You who took our olive branch of peace and&nbsp;
fashioned it into a spear. You who nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:22.859 --> 02:40:28.979
drove us to extinction. And now that we have the&nbsp;
advantage, you attempt to patronize us with your&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:28.979 --> 02:40:36.359
crocodile tears. We will not be deceived again.
“But unlike you, we are not monsters. We have&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:36.359 --> 02:40:41.759
much anger towards your kind, but we are willing&nbsp;
to forgive. But first, you must be willing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:41.760 --> 02:40:48.360
change. Slavery and genocide are immoral, and not&nbsp;
even you deserve such a fate. It is our belief,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:48.359 --> 02:40:53.819
then, that this alternative is a fair compromise&nbsp;
between guaranteeing our safety and allowing your&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:53.819 --> 02:40:59.519
kind to live. This is our mercy to you.
“Look at the humans who have gone through&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:40:59.520 --> 02:41:04.081
our program. See how much happier they&nbsp;
are? Your correspondence tells us that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:04.080 --> 02:41:09.059
you have seen them. Seen how much they&nbsp;
love us. Why, then, do you continue to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:09.060 --> 02:41:15.420
defiant? Someday you will thank us. Please try&nbsp;
to understand that this is for your own good.”&nbsp;

02:41:15.420 --> 02:41:21.960
For now, there is little that the SCP Foundation&nbsp;
can do to prevent the Human Domestication Society&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:21.960 --> 02:41:28.859
from abducting human beings to sell as pets&nbsp;
to other SCP-1897 creatures. Civilian access&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:28.859 --> 02:41:35.040
to the hdsociety.gov website has been restricted,&nbsp;
so we recommend you stop typing into the search&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:35.040 --> 02:41:40.859
bar of your browser to go take a peek.&nbsp;
Yes, we mean you! Seriously, stop that!&nbsp;

02:41:40.859 --> 02:41:46.139
As for the entities that have appeared in the&nbsp;
rural areas of the southwestern states? All the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:46.140 --> 02:41:51.600
Foundation can do is position its agents nearby,&nbsp;
in the hopes that they can detain and neutralize&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:51.600 --> 02:41:59.100
the SCP-1897s as they appear, with lethal force if&nbsp;
necessary. At present, the only procedure for any&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:41:59.100 --> 02:42:03.960
human pets that are successfully recaptured&nbsp;
is to have them moved safely to containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:03.960 --> 02:42:10.800
until a way of rehabilitating them is found. So&nbsp;
far, there hasn’t been any luck on that front.

02:42:10.800 --> 02:42:17.520
“Help me! Would somebody please&nbsp;
help me? I’m lost and I can’t see!”

02:42:17.520 --> 02:42:22.140
It echoed through the alley in a thin,&nbsp;
reedy voice that suggested brittleness&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:22.140 --> 02:42:27.000
of body and spirit. Who wouldn’t hear&nbsp;
that cry and feel a pang of sympathy?&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:27.000 --> 02:42:31.620
Are you so heartless that you’d ignore the&nbsp;
desperate pleas for help of a blind man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:31.620 --> 02:42:36.840
clearly in distress? For all you know, he&nbsp;
might even be in danger. What if he walks&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:36.840 --> 02:42:41.280
into a road and gets hit by a car? Would&nbsp;
you really want that on your conscience?

02:42:41.280 --> 02:42:45.719
Questions like these were flying through&nbsp;
the head of the Good Samaritan when he&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:45.720 --> 02:42:49.440
decided to go and investigate, when&nbsp;
it seemed like everyone else was just&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:49.439 --> 02:42:54.299
content to pretend they didn’t hear it and&nbsp;
carry on with their day as normal. The Good&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:54.300 --> 02:42:59.700
Samaritan was a person not unlike yourself. They&nbsp;
were also the kind of person we all hoped and&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:59.700 --> 02:43:06.179
wished we would be in a situation such as this.&nbsp;
Kindness and generosity is a virtue, after all.

02:43:06.180 --> 02:43:10.860
The problem is, there are people out there who&nbsp;
know this, and are willing to take advantage&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:10.859 --> 02:43:16.500
of that kindness and generosity. But even&nbsp;
worse is the fact that there are things that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:16.500 --> 02:43:21.479
are definitely not people out there willing&nbsp;
to take advantage of human compassion, too.

02:43:21.479 --> 02:43:26.939
But back to the Good Samaritan. He approached&nbsp;
the sound of the distressed man in the alley: He&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:26.939 --> 02:43:33.179
looked old and frail, hunched over with the weight&nbsp;
of his years. He wore thick, dark glasses, and his&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:33.180 --> 02:43:39.241
white cane was laying on the road a few feet away&nbsp;
from him. It was a tragic scene, but thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:39.240 --> 02:43:44.819
the Good Samaritan was here to help. He approached&nbsp;
the old man, calmly telling him that it was okay.

02:43:44.819 --> 02:43:48.059
The Good Samaritan picked up&nbsp;
the walking cane and passed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:48.060 --> 02:43:52.860
it over to the blind old man. His face&nbsp;
spread into a warm smile, and he said.

02:43:52.859 --> 02:43:56.399
“Thank you, thank you, thank you, young man.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:57.120 --> 02:44:01.680
It warms my heart to know there are still&nbsp;
good people like you on this earth.”

02:44:01.680 --> 02:44:06.960
The old man told the Good Samaritan that he’d&nbsp;
come into town to get some fresh air and a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:06.960 --> 02:44:12.359
exercise, at which point he’d gotten lost. When&nbsp;
the Good Samaritan asked whether it was safe for&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:12.359 --> 02:44:16.740
him to come alone, the old man told him that&nbsp;
he always used to go on walks with his wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:16.740 --> 02:44:21.420
but ever since the accident, she didn’t&nbsp;
seem to want to be seen in public.

02:44:21.420 --> 02:44:25.859
The Good Samaritan naturally felt for&nbsp;
the old man, who seemed as sweet as he&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:25.859 --> 02:44:29.759
was feeble. He offered to escort the&nbsp;
old man back to his house personally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:29.760 --> 02:44:35.640
wanting to make sure that he returned home safely.&nbsp;
The old man smiled and graciously accepted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:35.640 --> 02:44:40.620
saying that his wife would probably want to thank&nbsp;
the kind young man for helping him in person.

02:44:40.620 --> 02:44:46.080
Of course, the Good Samaritan was so wrapped up&nbsp;
in the warm glow of doing a good deed that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:46.080 --> 02:44:51.300
never once stopped to question the strangeness&nbsp;
of this whole situation. He just walked along&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:51.300 --> 02:44:57.060
with the old man, listening to him tell his&nbsp;
fanciful stories, as they left the city center&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:44:57.060 --> 02:45:02.340
and crept further into the sleepy outskirts&nbsp;
of their small Kentucky town. He was just&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:02.340 --> 02:45:07.920
rambling on, as old men tend to. He told the Good&nbsp;
Samaritan a little more about his beloved wife:&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:07.920 --> 02:45:13.319
She was a kind woman whom he’d known for as&nbsp;
long as he could remember. His elementary school&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:13.319 --> 02:45:18.660
sweetheart, then his high school girlfriend, and&nbsp;
not long after they graduated, his beautiful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:18.660 --> 02:45:24.359
blushing bride. Oh yes, she’d always been&nbsp;
the prettiest lady, until the accident.

02:45:24.359 --> 02:45:30.299
Curiosity was getting the better of him: The Good&nbsp;
Samaritan couldn’t help but ask what exactly the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:30.300 --> 02:45:36.120
“accident” he kept alluding to was, and the old&nbsp;
man was all too happy to give him an answer. Not&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:36.120 --> 02:45:41.519
that this answer was, in any way, pleasant.&nbsp;
His wife had been trapped in a terrible fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:41.520 --> 02:45:47.820
in town that gave her severe burns all over her&nbsp;
body. She was lucky to be alive, but the flames&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:47.819 --> 02:45:52.799
took her beauty and her confidence away from&nbsp;
her. Since then, she’d become a real homebody,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:45:52.800 --> 02:45:57.000
often refusing to leave the house, and&nbsp;
rarely ever letting strangers see her.

02:45:57.000 --> 02:46:02.040
The Good Samaritan’s heart ached for this&nbsp;
poor old couple. Why were such nice people&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:02.040 --> 02:46:07.080
often forced to endure so much suffering? Did&nbsp;
this old man even have anyone else to talk to?

02:46:07.080 --> 02:46:11.519
They reached his house soon enough, it was&nbsp;
the furthest one on the end of the street,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:11.520 --> 02:46:17.340
right next to the darkness of the woods. It looked&nbsp;
old and dilapidated, but it wasn’t like the old&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:17.340 --> 02:46:21.900
blind man could even know that. As they were&nbsp;
walking up the small set of stairs to the porch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:21.899 --> 02:46:26.519
the old man stumbled slightly, causing his&nbsp;
thick, dark glasses to fall to the floor.

02:46:26.520 --> 02:46:31.680
The Good Samaritan reflexively leaned over to pick&nbsp;
up the glasses for the old man, and as he passed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:31.680 --> 02:46:37.920
them back, he noticed something strange. The old&nbsp;
man wasn’t just blind, he literally didn’t have&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:37.920 --> 02:46:44.520
any eyes. Just two black, empty sockets where&nbsp;
his eyes should be. The Good Samaritan was just&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:44.520 --> 02:46:48.541
thankful that the old man wasn’t able to see&nbsp;
him staring as he put the glasses back on.

02:46:48.540 --> 02:46:52.800
The two of them entered the house. The Good&nbsp;
Samaritan was too busy thinking about the old&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:52.800 --> 02:46:57.420
man’s empty eye sockets to even notice him&nbsp;
locking the door behind them, and by then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:46:57.420 --> 02:47:03.240
it was already too late for him. The old man&nbsp;
called out into the dark expanse of the house.

02:47:03.240 --> 02:47:07.800
“Sweetheart, I’ve got you a live one!”

02:47:07.800 --> 02:47:12.360
Before the Good Samaritan could ask what he&nbsp;
actually meant by that, the old man shuffled off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:12.359 --> 02:47:14.939
deftly navigating the halls through memory alone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:14.939 --> 02:47:21.240
and took one of the two seats at the dining&nbsp;
table. He just sat there, smiling. Waiting.

02:47:21.240 --> 02:47:26.399
That’s when the Good Samaritan heard a creaking&nbsp;
sound coming from above. Something moving,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:26.399 --> 02:47:31.559
up in the darkness of the second floor,&nbsp;
and then descending the stairs with heavy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:31.560 --> 02:47:36.420
clomping footsteps. When his eyes came&nbsp;
into focus in the dark, he saw it there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:36.420 --> 02:47:41.760
the most terrifying thing he’d ever&nbsp;
witnessed, coming down the stairs towards him.

02:47:41.760 --> 02:47:47.760
It was vaguely human in its shape alone, but in&nbsp;
all other respects, it was a monster through and&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:47.760 --> 02:47:53.400
through. This gnarled, twisted creature with&nbsp;
bulging eyes, dead flesh, and filthy exposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:53.399 --> 02:47:58.259
fangs. Like it’d stepped straight out of&nbsp;
a nightmare and into the physical world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:47:58.260 --> 02:48:04.500
where it did not belong. There looked to be a huge&nbsp;
hole in its lower torso, too, with no blood or&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:04.500 --> 02:48:11.520
organs inside. Just an infinite blackness. The&nbsp;
creature’s lipless mouth twisted into a smile.

02:48:11.520 --> 02:48:16.260
The creature said something in a voice that&nbsp;
the Good Samaritan couldn’t understand. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:16.260 --> 02:48:22.140
was the Black Tongue, something ancient,&nbsp;
terrifying, and unknown. As the creature got&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:22.140 --> 02:48:26.040
closer and closer, the Good Samaritan&nbsp;
turned and made a run for the door.

02:48:26.040 --> 02:48:31.080
He tried to figure out the lock, his hands&nbsp;
fumbling and uncoordinated by fear. He could&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:31.080 --> 02:48:35.280
hear the footsteps and the heavy breathing&nbsp;
of that thing getting closer behind him.

02:48:35.280 --> 02:48:38.099
He was so close...Almost there...

02:48:38.100 --> 02:48:43.621
That’s when a strange, black substance seemed&nbsp;
to encase the world around him. It separated&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:43.620 --> 02:48:49.080
him from the door he was so nearly able to&nbsp;
breach, locking him in. He was trapped inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:49.080 --> 02:48:53.760
what looked like a giant, black sphere&nbsp;
made of some unknown material or energy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:53.760 --> 02:48:59.100
He turned to see that monster standing right&nbsp;
behind him, just grinning and waiting for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:48:59.100 --> 02:49:05.220
inevitability of the situation to sink in. The&nbsp;
Good Samaritan had never been more terrified.

02:49:05.220 --> 02:49:10.620
Something else began to shift inside the sphere.&nbsp;
A structure was growing out of the ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:10.620 --> 02:49:17.580
up and around him, like a cage within a cage. He&nbsp;
was trapped and huddled inside a strange conical&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:17.580 --> 02:49:22.740
structure, as more figures entered the sphere&nbsp;
around him. They were just like the first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:22.740 --> 02:49:29.219
this horrible horde of desiccated not-people.&nbsp;
All with grinning, lipless mouths. When they&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:29.220 --> 02:49:34.020
closed in on him, the Good Samaritan had the&nbsp;
one consolation that at least it was over.

02:49:34.020 --> 02:49:36.480
But it wasn’t. Not yet.

02:49:36.479 --> 02:49:41.459
The blind old man waited in the kitchen&nbsp;
for five hours as unmentionable horrors&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:41.460 --> 02:49:46.080
unfolded inside the black sphere. The Good&nbsp;
Samaritan was actually lucky, all in all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:46.080 --> 02:49:52.319
because some sessions for victims inside the&nbsp;
sphere had lasted as long as 27 hours. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:52.319 --> 02:49:56.819
screamed the entire time, with the sphere&nbsp;
finally de-manifesting just moments after&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:49:56.819 --> 02:50:02.939
the screaming stopped. Remaining, was only&nbsp;
one of the creatures, but no Good Samaritan.

02:50:02.939 --> 02:50:07.919
Just several neat piles of human&nbsp;
organs, arranged by organ type.

02:50:07.920 --> 02:50:13.800
“Are you done in there, honey?” the blind old&nbsp;
man asked. “I’ve been getting awfully hungry.”

02:50:13.800 --> 02:50:16.440
The creature replied, in perfect English.

02:50:16.439 --> 02:50:20.040
“Yes, dear. I’ll fix you up some&nbsp;
supper before you go to bed.”

02:50:20.040 --> 02:50:28.859
The creature picked up some of the discarded&nbsp;
organs and took them into the kitchen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:28.859 --> 02:50:34.139
where it began cooking them into a stew for&nbsp;
the old man. He ate the stew not long after,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:34.140 --> 02:50:40.020
blissfully ignorant to its contents, and went to&nbsp;
sleep. Whatever organs from the Good Samaritan&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:40.020 --> 02:50:45.121
weren’t used in the stew were simply thrown&nbsp;
into the fireplace to burn away into ashes.

02:50:45.120 --> 02:50:49.800
Later that night, the old man would&nbsp;
die peacefully of a heart attack in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:49.800 --> 02:50:54.780
sleep at age 81. He spent the latter&nbsp;
ten years of his life in service of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:50:54.780 --> 02:51:00.599
SCP-957. He’d never even had a wife, and&nbsp;
when the monster first invaded his home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:00.600 --> 02:51:06.960
he wasn’t even blind. He’d simply come home&nbsp;
one day to find SCP-957 lurking in his home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:06.960 --> 02:51:13.620
waiting for him. As far as the SCP Foundation is&nbsp;
aware, it always targets people who live alone.

02:51:13.620 --> 02:51:19.680
The man had tried to resist, but the creature was&nbsp;
freakishly strong in spite of its wiry frame. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:19.680 --> 02:51:25.320
grabbed him and forced his body into the dark,&nbsp;
gaping chasm of its chest. He was swallowed up&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:25.319 --> 02:51:29.700
into another world on the other side of&nbsp;
the void, and returned four hours later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:29.700 --> 02:51:37.139
a changed man. His eyes were gone, and he now&nbsp;
firmly believed that SCP-957 was his beloved,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:37.140 --> 02:51:43.440
if burn-scarred, wife of many years. He’d&nbsp;
do anything for her: Even heading out into&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:51:43.439 --> 02:51:48.359
the world and feigning distress, to lure&nbsp;
people back into her terrible clutches.

02:51:48.359 --> 02:51:55.920
That’s how the old man became SCP-957-1. He&nbsp;
wasn’t the first, and wouldn’t be the last.

02:51:55.920 --> 02:52:01.859
With the old man now dead, SCP-957 would&nbsp;
de-manifest and head off in search of a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:01.859 --> 02:52:06.899
victim, invading their home and repeating&nbsp;
the cycle once more somewhere else. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:06.899 --> 02:52:12.779
somewhat happy ending is that in one of these&nbsp;
cases, the SCP Foundation somehow got wise to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:12.779 --> 02:52:18.000
the baiting activities of SCP-957, and&nbsp;
they were able to contain the creature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:18.000 --> 02:52:23.279
giving it the Keter object class for its frequent&nbsp;
attempts to either get out or lure in new victims.

02:52:23.279 --> 02:52:27.300
It’s never been actively hostile to&nbsp;
Foundation researchers and guards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:27.300 --> 02:52:32.700
just a little obtuse. Despite the fact that it’s&nbsp;
perfectly capable of speaking fluent English,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:32.700 --> 02:52:38.639
it prefers to speak in an unknown, dead language&nbsp;
for somewhat mysterious reasons. Very little is&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:38.640 --> 02:52:44.280
known about the origins or true nature of&nbsp;
SCP-957, but our one brief glimpse into its&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:44.279 --> 02:52:49.800
interior life does little to comfort us. In&nbsp;
2008, the Foundation recorded 957 having a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:49.800 --> 02:52:54.660
conversation with an unseen individual in&nbsp;
its native tongue. Foundation linguistic&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:52:54.660 --> 02:52:58.800
experts have been able to partially crack&nbsp;
the code on what was being said that day.

02:52:58.800 --> 02:53:04.260
957 asked the unseen figure how much longer&nbsp;
it would have to stay here. The figure told&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:04.260 --> 02:53:08.580
it that it would need to wait there for a&nbsp;
while and that its disguise was extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:08.580 --> 02:53:15.120
convincing. 957 complained that being “here”&nbsp;
was boring and tiresome, but the unseen figure&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:15.120 --> 02:53:20.640
urged 957 to remain patient. It said “We have&nbsp;
to let them watch the few so that the many can&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:20.640 --> 02:53:27.180
move freely. We will be done&nbsp;
with our research soon enough…”

02:53:27.180 --> 02:53:33.060
Before we start today’s video, we need to ask you&nbsp;
a question: Are you alone in the room? Seriously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:33.060 --> 02:53:39.540
are you alone? You may think that the room around&nbsp;
you is empty, but how can you really know that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:39.540 --> 02:53:45.600
right? Think of the technology out there being&nbsp;
developed by groups like DARPA, the CIA, or even&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:45.600 --> 02:53:51.060
the SCP Foundation - Secret agents in cloaking&nbsp;
suits could be standing around you right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:51.060 --> 02:53:55.800
watching your every move, without you even&nbsp;
knowing. You could tell someone about this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:53:55.800 --> 02:54:01.140
but if you did, they’d think you’re crazy,&nbsp;
and nobody believes crazy people, do they?

02:54:01.140 --> 02:54:06.960
Sometimes people’s whole worlds just collapse.&nbsp;
One day they’re living happy, successful lives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:06.960 --> 02:54:12.000
with families and friends who love and care&nbsp;
about them. Then the next day, they’re truly&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:12.000 --> 02:54:16.380
convinced that the US government is tapping&nbsp;
not only their phone calls and their emails,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:16.380 --> 02:54:22.740
but their thoughts. Perhaps even putting dangerous&nbsp;
brainwaves directly into their mind. Or they start&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:22.740 --> 02:54:27.719
to believe that those loving family members&nbsp;
and friends seek to do them harm. Maybe they&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:27.720 --> 02:54:32.700
start to believe their food is poisoned, and&nbsp;
stop eating, causing them to waste away from&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:32.700 --> 02:54:37.800
malnutrition. Most terrifying of all, maybe&nbsp;
they start to see things that nobody else&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:37.800 --> 02:54:45.779
could see. Monsters that defy rationality and&nbsp;
shake the very soul. Terrible, terrible things…

02:54:45.779 --> 02:54:51.059
These are all, sadly, relatively common symptoms&nbsp;
of someone suffering from a severe case of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:51.060 --> 02:54:56.760
Schizophrenia - A mental illness with a wide range&nbsp;
of detrimental effects to sufferers, first and&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:54:56.760 --> 02:55:02.040
foremost giving them an incredibly complicated&nbsp;
relationship with reality. There’s sadly a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:02.040 --> 02:55:06.359
of misconceptions in the media about people&nbsp;
who suffer from illnesses like Schizophrenia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:06.359 --> 02:55:12.120
painting them as unstable individuals who present&nbsp;
a danger to the people around them. In reality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:12.120 --> 02:55:16.500
people with a condition like this are three&nbsp;
times more likely to be the victim of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:16.500 --> 02:55:21.300
violent crime. And they’re also more likely&nbsp;
to be the victim of something else, too...

02:55:21.300 --> 02:55:27.480
Like we said earlier, sometimes people’s&nbsp;
worlds just collapse, and in severe cases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:27.479 --> 02:55:31.620
they might simply drop off the&nbsp;
map. And nine times out of ten,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:31.620 --> 02:55:37.380
the reason for that is SCP-870:&nbsp;
The Maybe There Monsters.

02:55:37.380 --> 02:55:42.060
Take the experience of Katrina Wayne.&nbsp;
She was an office temp in Tallahassee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:42.060 --> 02:55:46.260
Florida, with an undiagnosed case of&nbsp;
mild schizophrenia. For the most part,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:46.260 --> 02:55:51.180
she was able to operate just fine at her job,&nbsp;
getting her work done at a satisfactory level&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:51.180 --> 02:55:56.520
while also maintaining a decent social life after&nbsp;
hours. It came as a shock to everyone when she&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:55:56.520 --> 02:56:01.440
began screeching horrifically in the middle of the&nbsp;
office. She backed herself up against the wall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:01.439 --> 02:56:06.299
picking up nearby objects and throwing&nbsp;
them into the aisles at some invisible foe.

02:56:06.300 --> 02:56:11.400
And this isn’t a metaphor: There really&nbsp;
was an invisible foe moving towards her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:11.399 --> 02:56:16.859
and only she could truly see it. Seeing the&nbsp;
huge, scaly body of a mature alligator from&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:16.859 --> 02:56:21.599
the Florida Everglades moving towards you would&nbsp;
be scary enough on its own, but this wasn’t any&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:21.600 --> 02:56:27.420
ordinary alligator. Its long, reptilian head had&nbsp;
three eyes instead of two, and it moved towards&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:27.420 --> 02:56:33.840
her on eight huge, articulated spider legs. It&nbsp;
was like something straight out of a nightmare.

02:56:33.840 --> 02:56:37.500
Katrina was put on leave due to a&nbsp;
stress-induced mental breakdown and&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:37.500 --> 02:56:41.399
prescribed a course of antipsychotic&nbsp;
medication by a psychiatrist. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:41.399 --> 02:56:44.819
disappeared from her home without&nbsp;
a trace a mere two weeks later.

02:56:44.819 --> 02:56:49.500
Or take the story of Daryl Simon. He was a&nbsp;
mechanic working in Michigan with a family&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:49.500 --> 02:56:54.300
history of schizophrenia, though he’d never&nbsp;
been officially diagnosed himself. He was&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:54.300 --> 02:56:59.880
working on the engine of a vintage corvette when&nbsp;
something strange happened: His garage began to&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:56:59.880 --> 02:57:04.680
fill up with smoke. He considered at first that&nbsp;
perhaps it was some kind of engine malfunction&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:04.680 --> 02:57:09.720
causing smoke to belch out of the old corvette’s&nbsp;
tailpipe, but then he saw something standing in&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:09.720 --> 02:57:15.480
the smoke - A human figure. Daryl suddenly felt&nbsp;
a profound sense of dread seeping into his mind.

02:57:15.479 --> 02:57:19.379
He grabbed a monkey wrench and began to&nbsp;
slowly approach the intruder standing in&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:19.380 --> 02:57:22.859
the smoke. It was only when he was already&nbsp;
too close that he realized that the figure&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:22.859 --> 02:57:28.200
wasn’t just standing in the smoke. It was&nbsp;
made of smoke. The second he noticed this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:28.200 --> 02:57:34.260
the figure’s eyes opened, glowing red. Its smoky&nbsp;
face opened into a wide, toothy mouth and let out&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:34.260 --> 02:57:39.540
an ear splitting shriek. Daryl suddenly found&nbsp;
himself running as the creature gave chase. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:39.540 --> 02:57:43.920
threw his wrench at it as he ran; it breezed&nbsp;
through the creature’s semi-intangible form.

02:57:43.920 --> 02:57:49.260
Daryl was found later that day, huddled in the&nbsp;
corner of his garage, muttering incoherently.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:49.260 --> 02:57:53.820
After seeing a mental health professional and&nbsp;
sharing his story, he was given a schizophrenia&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:53.819 --> 02:57:59.460
diagnosis. He was given a mix of talk therapy and&nbsp;
medication, and seemed to be improving over time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:57:59.460 --> 02:58:03.779
He would occasionally report hallucinations&nbsp;
of the man made of smoke, watching from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:03.779 --> 02:58:08.040
corner of his eye, but it was dismissed as&nbsp;
nothing more than that: A hallucination.

02:58:08.040 --> 02:58:12.840
A month later, he was gone.&nbsp;
Never to be seen again. But he&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:12.840 --> 02:58:15.660
wasn’t the only one to fall victim to the anomaly.

02:58:15.660 --> 02:58:20.880
Shirley Nicholson, a retiree whose schizophrenic&nbsp;
symptoms developed later in life, was having a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:20.880 --> 02:58:25.920
quiet evening in her home when she first&nbsp;
encountered an instance of SCP-870. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:25.920 --> 02:58:29.700
was watching a game show on television when&nbsp;
she heard a strange noise coming from her&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:29.700 --> 02:58:34.500
kitchen. A rustling, like someone was messing&nbsp;
with the food inside her fridge. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:34.500 --> 02:58:38.399
she’d always had a tendency to hear things,&nbsp;
which was why she wasn’t that nervous when&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:38.399 --> 02:58:42.719
she got up and walked into the kitchen.&nbsp;
That sense of confidence didn’t last long.

02:58:42.720 --> 02:58:46.980
When she entered her kitchen, she saw the&nbsp;
fridge door open, with the back half of what&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:46.979 --> 02:58:52.200
looked like a giant ant emerging from it. Her&nbsp;
breath caught in her throat. That giant ant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:52.200 --> 02:58:57.840
which seemed to be eating the food inside her&nbsp;
fridge, suddenly froze, seeming to realize that&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:58:57.840 --> 02:59:01.920
Shirley had entered the room. When it backed&nbsp;
out of the fridge, Shirley couldn’t help but&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:01.920 --> 02:59:07.800
scream. Instead of antennas and mandibles,&nbsp;
the giant ant had a grinning, human face.

02:59:07.800 --> 02:59:13.740
As Shirley screamed, the giant ant’s human face&nbsp;
began to cackle with sadistic glee. Its jaw began&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:13.740 --> 02:59:19.920
to stretch open, impossibly wide, exposing the&nbsp;
never-ending darkness within. Shirley turned&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:19.920 --> 02:59:24.480
and ran as the creature skittered towards her&nbsp;
at a frightening speed. Adrenaline kicked in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:24.479 --> 02:59:29.099
and Shirley ran for her life as the monster&nbsp;
pursued her through the house. It was only&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:29.100 --> 02:59:33.000
when she ran out into the street, and was&nbsp;
seen by others in this bizarre outburst,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:33.000 --> 02:59:36.000
that the horrifying ant&nbsp;
monster seemed to disappear.

02:59:36.000 --> 02:59:39.180
And several weeks after her&nbsp;
schizophrenia diagnosis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:39.180 --> 02:59:44.820
Shirley Nicholson sadly disappeared too. Before&nbsp;
she vanished, she made a panicked 911 call,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:44.819 --> 02:59:48.840
where she screamed down the line&nbsp;
that the monster had come back. No&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:48.840 --> 02:59:53.580
explanation has yet to be found, but there&nbsp;
are more cases to be investigated still.

02:59:53.580 --> 02:59:59.819
Don Jones, who had a documented history with&nbsp;
schizophrenia, had his SCP-870 experience while&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:59:59.819 --> 03:00:04.139
waiting for the bus out of town late one&nbsp;
October evening. He was checking his phone&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:04.140 --> 03:00:09.000
at the bus stop when he saw a figure shuffling&nbsp;
towards him in the distance. He tried to ignore&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:09.000 --> 03:00:13.319
it at first - Years of therapy had taught&nbsp;
him to try his best to ignore these strange&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:13.319 --> 03:00:18.240
little anomalies. He’d been medicated for years,&nbsp;
and while occasionally he had minor episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:18.240 --> 03:00:22.319
he’d lived with the condition for long&nbsp;
enough now that he’d learned how to cope.

03:00:22.319 --> 03:00:25.200
That’s when the strange,&nbsp;
shuffling figure got closer.

03:00:25.200 --> 03:00:30.599
Don looked up, just for a moment, to see the&nbsp;
thing coming towards him out of the dark. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:30.600 --> 03:00:34.680
was about the size of a child, though a little&nbsp;
shorter because of how far the creature was&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:34.680 --> 03:00:39.960
hunched over. Literally, hunched, the entity&nbsp;
had a rather prominent hunchback. But that&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:39.960 --> 03:00:44.220
wasn’t nearly as notable as the thing’s&nbsp;
face: It had the head of a particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:44.220 --> 03:00:49.140
mangy-looking parrot, its curved beak&nbsp;
caked in what looked like old blood.

03:00:49.140 --> 03:00:52.860
This was stranger than some of the&nbsp;
hallucinations he’d suffered in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:52.859 --> 03:00:57.479
past. It looked more tangible, more&nbsp;
real, even after years of medication&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:00:57.479 --> 03:01:02.099
and therapy. He felt nervous as the thing&nbsp;
approached him. On some subconscious level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:02.100 --> 03:01:05.701
he knew the thing intended to&nbsp;
harm him in one way or another.

03:01:05.700 --> 03:01:10.019
When it opened its mouth, and sunk the&nbsp;
bladed tip of its beak into Don’s hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:10.020 --> 03:01:14.760
he knew that he wasn’t dealing with any&nbsp;
mundane fantasy here. He screamed and ran&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:14.760 --> 03:01:19.320
off into the night, the monster giving chase.&nbsp;
He later reported the incident to the police,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:19.319 --> 03:01:22.920
but his fears were written off when&nbsp;
his medical history came to light.

03:01:22.920 --> 03:01:28.020
Everyone just assumed the man was experiencing&nbsp;
another episode, and that the wound in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:28.020 --> 03:01:31.680
hand was self-inflicted. Of course, as&nbsp;
you’ve probably gathered by this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:31.680 --> 03:01:35.100
poor Don Jones would disappear&nbsp;
without a trace not long after.

03:01:35.100 --> 03:01:38.040
Still, the testimonies get freakier...

03:01:38.040 --> 03:01:42.660
A warehouse security guard, Alex Landry,&nbsp;
had his terrifying encounter while on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:42.660 --> 03:01:46.859
job. He was on his nightly patrol when he&nbsp;
heard a strangely soft skittering noise&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:46.859 --> 03:01:51.899
coming from inside the warehouse. He deployed&nbsp;
his flashlight and ran inside after radioing&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:51.899 --> 03:01:56.460
for assistance. He was expecting maybe an&nbsp;
escaped animal or a young hoodlum messing&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:01:56.460 --> 03:02:01.319
around inside. What he didn’t expect was&nbsp;
a face-to-face encounter with pure terror.

03:02:01.319 --> 03:02:04.979
As his flashlight’s beam traced its&nbsp;
way up to the top of the warehouse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:04.979 --> 03:02:10.799
he saw a monster crawling across the ceiling.&nbsp;
It was a giant, fifteen-foot-long centipede,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:10.800 --> 03:02:14.880
but instead of having normal centipede&nbsp;
legs, it had scores of twitching,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:14.880 --> 03:02:20.460
grasping human arms. He was found in a comatose&nbsp;
state by his partner, and spent the brief rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:20.460 --> 03:02:25.920
of his life in a psychiatric facility before -&nbsp;
you guessed it - disappearing without a trace.

03:02:25.920 --> 03:02:31.500
And most exhilaratingly, we come to the&nbsp;
tale of Mr. Holgate, which both ends a&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:31.500 --> 03:02:36.840
little more hopeful for him, but paints a grim&nbsp;
picture of what happened to everyone else. Mr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:36.840 --> 03:02:41.400
Holgate had encountered a spider-like&nbsp;
creature with a freakish number of legs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:41.399 --> 03:02:46.080
which he soon realized only he could&nbsp;
see. During his periods of observation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:46.080 --> 03:02:50.160
he’d seen the creature both devour a&nbsp;
ruler - as in, the measurement device,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:50.160 --> 03:02:55.859
not a king - as well as swallow a human whole&nbsp;
after an extended period of stalking the victim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:02:55.859 --> 03:03:03.059
leaving nothing behind. Just like the SCP-870&nbsp;
instances had done to all their other victims.

03:03:03.060 --> 03:03:07.140
When the monster eventually came&nbsp;
for Holgate, he was ready. It ran&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:07.140 --> 03:03:11.880
screeching towards him on its too many legs,&nbsp;
and Holgate whipped out a gun and shot it.

03:03:11.880 --> 03:03:16.260
The Foundation has prioritized the&nbsp;
capture or destruction of SCP-870.&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:16.260 --> 03:03:21.840
It’s believed to be not a single instance,&nbsp;
but an entire species, living out there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:21.840 --> 03:03:27.180
preying on humans and hiding in the space between&nbsp;
our perceptions. Even two schizophrenic people&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:27.180 --> 03:03:31.260
looking at the same instance will report&nbsp;
seeing completely different entities.

03:03:31.260 --> 03:03:35.760
The monsters are all the more dangerous&nbsp;
due to the fact that sufferers of severe&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:35.760 --> 03:03:40.560
schizophrenia often report hallucinations&nbsp;
of strange monsters or entities, so their&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:40.560 --> 03:03:46.201
pleas for help are often ignored by neurotypical&nbsp;
authorities. Neurotypical meaning those who don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:46.200 --> 03:03:51.599
experience any form of mental illness, personality&nbsp;
disorder, or developmental condition - People&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:03:51.600 --> 03:03:56.640
who could never see SCP-870 coming until&nbsp;
they’re already being swallowed whole.

03:03:56.640 --> 03:04:02.701
The lead researcher on the SCP-870 case follows up&nbsp;
the file on the monsters with an ominous note that&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:02.700 --> 03:04:07.380
leaves little comfort for even those of us who&nbsp;
don’t suffer from schizophrenia. The note reads:

03:04:07.380 --> 03:04:13.500
“I, personally, don't believe that the&nbsp;
schizophrenics are really seeing SCP-870 fully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:13.500 --> 03:04:18.600
they can just see it more than us. We don't&nbsp;
see it because our brains aren't made to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:18.600 --> 03:04:23.520
it. The schizophrenics, their brains are&nbsp;
wired up just that tiny bit differently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:23.520 --> 03:04:29.581
and they can see it just a tiny bit more.&nbsp;
These things have the perfect camouflage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:29.580 --> 03:04:32.220
and we simply are unable to see through it.”

03:04:32.220 --> 03:04:35.820
To return to what we said at the&nbsp;
very beginning of this video. Look&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:35.819 --> 03:04:41.219
around the room and answer our&nbsp;
question: Are you alone? Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:04:41.220 --> 03:04:46.560
at least you know the answer to that&nbsp;
question may not be as simple as it seems...

